window.GEM_DATA = {"galleries":[{"key":"obelisk","cn":"悬空方尖碑","en":"Hanging Obelisk","count":1,"order":0},{"key":"hall","cn":"中央大厅","en":"Grand Hall","count":5,"order":1},{"key":"stairs","cn":"大阶梯","en":"Grand Stairs","count":14,"order":2},{"key":"main","cn":"主展厅","en":"Main Galleries","count":128,"order":3},{"key":"tut","cn":"图坦卡蒙展厅","en":"Tutankhamun Galleries","count":25,"order":4}],"items":[{"id":"obelisk-of-king-ramesses-ii","no":"21331","en":"Obelisk of King Ramesses II","cn":"拉美西斯二世方尖碑","g":"obelisk","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 19 王朝","m":"花岗岩","dim":"高 1550 cm · 宽 174 cm · 长 184 cm","prov":"下埃及 · 东部省","star":true,"n":1,"body":"这座方尖碑最特别的地方，在它的底部。博物馆用四根巨柱支撑起展示平台，让原本紧贴基座的碑底露出来。站在下方，便能看到刻有拉美西斯二世名字的王名圈。\n拉美西斯二世曾在尼罗河三角洲东部的塔尼斯竖立十余座方尖碑，这座是其中最高的一座。它由花岗岩制成，重约87吨，总高约16米，四面铭文记载了国王的荷鲁斯名、登基名和本名。\n如今，它矗立在博物馆入口广场上。这样的展示方式既保留了方尖碑的宏伟气势，也让过去难以看见的铭文成为参观的起点。","src":"Ramesses II raised over ten obelisks at Tanis (San el-Hagar) in the Eastern Delta. With a total height of 16 meters, this granite obelisk is the highest that ever stood at Tanis. On the four sides of the obelisk are inscriptions giving the Horus name, throne name and the birth name of the king. The 87-ton obelisk is now lifted on a platform supported by four massive pillars on a huge concrete base to allow visitors of the Grand Egyptian Museum to view the cartouches of Ramesses II carved on its bottom. Placed in a square of 30,000 m2, the Hanging Obelisk is the first artefact welcoming visitors at the Grand Egyptian Museum.","i":0},{"id":"colossal-statue-of-ramesses-ii","no":"1","en":"Colossal Statue of Ramesses II","cn":"拉美西斯二世巨像","g":"hall","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 19 王朝","m":"花岗岩","dim":"高 1135 cm · 宽 180 cm","prov":"孟菲斯 · 米特拉希纳","star":true,"n":1,"body":"走进中央大厅，拉美西斯二世的巨像便映入眼帘。它原本立在孟菲斯普塔神庙的外侧，以国王的形象守护神庙的神圣空间，也展示王室的力量与财富。\n普塔是工匠之神，孟菲斯则是他的重要崇拜中心。长期以来，人们还把这尊王像视为能够倾听祈祷的神圣形象，向它献上供品。\n不妨再留意国王双腿后方：那里刻着王子卡埃姆瓦塞特和公主宾塔娜特。两位王室子女的形象，让这座巨像除了宣示王权，也留下了王室家族的印记。","src":"Then as now, this giant statue reflects the power and richness of King Ramesses II. It originally stood outside the main temple of god Ptah at Memphis, guarding its sacred inner space. For many years, the statue was thought of as a god listening to the prayers of the devout and receiving their offerings. Two royal children, Prince Khaemwaset and Princess Bintanath are carved behind the king’s legs.","i":1},{"id":"colossus-of-a-ptolemaic-queen","no":"48137","en":"Colossus of a Ptolemaic Queen","cn":"托勒密王后巨像","g":"hall","p":"托勒密时期","d":null,"m":"花岗岩","dim":"高 425 cm · 宽 141 cm · 长 168 cm","prov":"亚历山大","star":true,"n":1,"body":"这尊王后巨像来自一座沉入海底的古城——托尼斯—赫拉克利翁。古城位于今天的阿布基尔湾，曾是埃及的重要贸易港口，后来因地震与海潮等灾害逐渐沉没。水下考古让这尊花岗岩雕像重新回到了人们面前。\n王后戴着三分式假发，身穿细褶长裙，披巾两端在腰间打结。她头上的牛角、日轮与双羽冠表明，雕像将她塑造成了伊西斯女神的形象。\n它原本与一尊托勒密国王巨像一同立在当地的阿蒙—格列布神庙外。王室形象与女神装束结合，是理解这件作品的关键。","src":"This granite colossus was recovered through underwater excavations at the sunken city of Thonis-Heracleion (Abuqir Bay) that gradually disappeared under the waters of the Mediterranean due to a series of earthquakes and tidal waves. The colossus shows a Ptolemaic queen wearing a tripartite hair wig, a finely pleated dress and a shawl whose ends are knotted around her waist. A sun disk between two horns and a two-feathered crown above her head presents her as the goddess Isis. Together with another colossus representing a Ptolemaic king, the two statues originally stood outside a temple dedicated to god Amun-Gereb at Thonis-Heracleion. The archaeological material excavated from Thonis-Heracleion clearly reflects the importance of the now sunken city whose harbours once controlled all trade into Egypt.","i":2},{"id":"seated-statue-of-senwosert-i","no":"1689","en":"Seated Statue of Senwosert I","cn":"塞努塞尔特一世坐像","g":"hall","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"石灰岩","dim":"高 194 cm · 宽 58 cm · 长 123 cm","prov":"孟菲斯 · 利什特","star":false,"n":1,"body":"塞努塞尔特一世端坐在王座上，头戴涅墨斯头巾，身着王室短裙。这尊坐像属于1894年在利什特国王祭庙内发现的一组雕像，同组共有十尊，国王的姿态基本相同。\n它们的区别藏在王座侧面。这里刻着象征上下埃及统一的“塞玛塔维”图案：两地的代表植物被系在同一个象形符号上，表达国家合一的观念。\n十尊雕像中，五尊由两位尼罗河神哈皮完成这个动作，另外五尊则由荷鲁斯和塞特完成。本件属于后者。观看时，可以把注意力从国王正面移到王座两侧，寻找这组讲述统一的浮雕。","src":"A cache of ten seated statues of King Senwosret I was discovered in 1894 during excavations made at his funerary temple at El-Lisht. All ten statues show the king seated on the throne, wearing the nemes head cloth and the royal kilt. The sides of the throne are decorated with the sema­tawy sign symbolising the unification of Upper and Lower Egypt. Five of the thrones were decorated with the unification performed by two representations of god Hapi, while the remaining five, including this statue, were decorated with the action of unification performed by Horus and Seth.","i":3},{"id":"column-of-king-merenptah","no":"22711","en":"Column of King Merenptah","cn":"梅伦普塔石柱","g":"hall","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 19 王朝","m":"花岗岩","dim":"高 600 cm · 直径 105 cm","prov":"下埃及 · 泰勒希森","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这根石柱把一场战争的胜利写进了神庙建筑。柱上铭文记载，梅伦普塔在即位第五年击败了侵入埃及边境的敌人；浮雕则把胜利描绘为诸神赐予国王的力量。\n画面中，女神阿纳特向国王授予权标，阿蒙、拉—霍拉赫提、塞特、蒙图和塞赫麦特等神祇授予他胜利之剑。靠近柱基的位置，还刻有被绳索捆绑的俘虏，以及战果和战利品的简短记录。\n石柱由石灰岩高座、砂岩基座和红色花岗岩柱身、柱顶板组成。它的残件出土于赫利奥波利斯，为梅伦普塔曾在当地兴建神庙提供了线索。","src":"Parts of this column were found during excavations at Heliopolis (Tell Hisn). It is formed of a high limestone stand, a sandstone base and a red granite shaft and abacus. Inscriptions on the column commemorate King Merenptah’s victory in a war he waged in his fifth regnal year against transgressors on Egyptian borders. Scenes on the column show the king receiving a mace from goddess Anath and the sword of victory from the deities Amun, Re-Horakhty, Seth, Montu and Sekhmet. Slightly above the column base are bearded captives bound with ropes accompanied by a concise record of the battle and the received spoils of war. The discovery of this column points to the presence of a temple dedicated by Merenptah to the principal deities of Heliopolis.","i":4},{"id":"colossus-of-a-ptolemaic-king-1","no":"48136","en":"Colossus of a Ptolemaic King","cn":"托勒密国王巨像","g":"hall","p":"托勒密时期","d":null,"m":"花岗岩","dim":"高 500 cm · 宽 75 cm · 长 150 cm","prov":"亚历山大","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这位高约五米的国王左脚前迈，双臂贴近身体，头戴象征上下埃及的双冠，腰间围着王室短裙。虽然属于托勒密时期，雕像采用的却是传统埃及王像的装束与姿态。\n留意他的右手：握紧的拳中有一个小圆柱。这一细节与紧贴身体的双臂、前伸的左腿一起，构成了这尊立像的鲜明特征。\n巨像出土于阿布基尔湾的水下遗址托尼斯—赫拉克利翁，原本立在阿蒙—格列布神庙外。当地发现的雕像、建筑构件、首饰和仪式用品，共同呈现了这座古代港口城市的繁盛面貌。","src":"Underwater excavations at the site of Thonis-Heracleion (Abuqir Bay), northeast of Alexandria, led to the discovery of colossal statues, architectural elements, jewellery, coins, ritual objects, as well as ceramics, all of which speak of the glory of that city and the magnificence of its temples. Among the recovered objects was this granite colossal statue of a Ptolemaic king in Egyptian style, wearing a double crown and a royal shendyt kilt. The king stands with the left leg advanced, his arms held close to his sides and his right fist holds a small cylinder. The five-metre-tall colossus that originally stood outside a temple dedicated to Amun-Gereb at Thonis-Heracleion visited Europe and the United States as part of the ‘Sunken Cities’ temporary exhibition and is now permanently on display at the Grand Egyptian Museum.","i":5},{"id":"colossal-osiride-statue-of-king-senwosret-i","no":"1327","en":"Colossal Osiride Statue of King Senwosret I","cn":"塞努塞尔特一世奥西里斯式巨像","g":"stairs","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"红色花岗岩","dim":"高 387.0 cm · 宽 100 cm · 长 110 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 索哈杰","star":true,"n":1,"body":"塞努塞尔特一世在这里以奥西里斯的形态出现。奥西里斯与死亡和复生有关，国王借用这一神圣形象，表达对死后延续生命的期望。雕像头戴上埃及白冠，年轻的面容带着微笑，规整的眉形格外醒目。\n脚下的“九张弓”也是重要细节。它们象征古埃及传统观念中的敌人，被置于国王脚下，用来宣示王权对敌对力量的压制。\n这尊红色花岗岩巨像于1859年发现于阿拜多斯奥西里斯—肯提阿门提乌神庙的柱廊庭院。观看时，不妨把温和的面容与脚下的征服象征放在一起理解：它同时传达了神圣身份与王者力量。","src":"Discovered in 1859, in the porticoed courtyard of the Temple of Osiris-Khentiimentiu at Abydos, this red granite colossal was shaped to reflect an interesting vigour. Here, King Senwosret I of Dynasty 12 is represented in an Osiride form wearing the white crown of Upper Egypt. His face looks young with a smiling expression and stylized eyebrows that dominate his eyes. Under the king's feet are the nine bows, symbols of the traditional enemies of ancient Egypt.","i":6},{"id":"statue-of-queen-hatshepsut","no":"2205","en":"Statue of Queen Hatshepsut","cn":"哈特谢普苏特女王雕像","g":"stairs","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"红色花岗岩","dim":"高 270 cm · 宽 84 cm · 长 112 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":true,"n":1,"body":"这尊雕像保留了哈特谢普苏特的女性面部特征，同时又配上假胡须、涅墨斯头巾和王室短裙。几种元素的并置，反映了她以女性身份担任法老时的形象选择。\n哈特谢普苏特是图特摩斯一世的女儿、图特摩斯二世的王后。丈夫去世后，她先为年幼的图特摩斯三世摄政，随后凭借自己的王室血统取得王位。她的雕像也逐渐从女性形象转向更具男性国王特征的表现方式。\n本件于1928年发现于卢克索西岸代尔巴哈里的女王祭庙。她双臂向下伸展，双手置于短裙前，采用了一种在中王国雕像中已经出现的虔敬姿态。","src":"Queen Hatshepsut was a daughter of King Thutmose I and chief royal wife of King Thutmose II. Following her husband’s death, she first acted as regent to his son Thutmose III. Then, she assumed the position of a king by asserting her direct royal lineage to her father King Thutmose I and her mother Queen Ahmose. Hatshepsut’s statuary first reflected feminine features, but these were later replaced by increasingly masculinized features. This statue reflects a unique combination of feminine traits with masculine royal symbols, like the false beard, the nemes headcloth and the kilt. It was discovered in 1928 at her mortuary temple at Deir-el-Bahri in West Thebes (Luxor). The queen stands with her arms extended on her kilt in a devotional pose already seen in Middle Kingdom statuary.","i":7},{"id":"sphinx-of-kings-ramesses-ii-and-merenptah","no":"6760","en":"Sphinx of Kings Ramesses II and Merenptah","cn":"拉美西斯二世与梅伦普塔双王狮身人面像","g":"stairs","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"花岗岩","dim":"高 170 cm · 宽 98 cm","prov":"下埃及 · 东部省","star":true,"n":1,"body":"雕像上虽然刻着拉美西斯二世和梅伦普塔的名字，它的制作年代却比两位国王早得多。小巧的嘴、杏仁形双眼、厚眼睑、突出的耳朵，以及头巾条纹的处理，都指向第十二王朝末至第十三王朝初的风格。\n到了第十九王朝，拉美西斯二世与梅伦普塔先后在这尊红色花岗岩狮身人面像上留下王名，将旧雕像重新用于自己的王权表达。\n此后，第三中间期的统治者又把它迁往塔尼斯。它最终在当地阿蒙大神庙遗址中被发现。一件雕像上的不同年代痕迹，记录了它被反复使用和迁移的经历。","src":"This red granite sphinx was discovered among the ruins of the Great Temple of Amun at Tanis (San el-Hagar) in the Eastern Delta. Stylistic details indicate that it was originally a Middle Kingdom monument. The small mouth, almond-shaped eyes, thick eyelids, prominent ears, strong arches of the eyebrows, round cheeks and the treatment of the stripes of the nemes headcloth are all features specific to royal statuary from the end of Dynasty 12 to the beginning of Dynasty 13. The royal names of Ramesses II and Merenptah on the statue are marks of later reuse of the monument in Dynasty 19. Rulers of the Third Intermediate Period had the statue moved to Tanis (San el-Hagar), which became the seat of power during Dynasties 21 and 22.","i":8},{"id":"statue-of-god-ptah-king-ramesses-ii-and-sekhmet","no":"45815","en":"Statue of God Ptah, King Ramesses II & Goddess Sekhmet","cn":"普塔神、拉美西斯二世与塞赫麦特女神像","g":"stairs","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 19 王朝","m":"花岗岩","dim":"高 350 cm · 宽 265 cm · 长 275 cm","prov":"上埃及","star":true,"n":1,"body":"拉美西斯二世站在两位神祇之间：一侧是工匠之神普塔，另一侧是狮首女神塞赫麦特。三者并列，突出国王与神的密切关系。\n普塔呈木乃伊形态，戴贴头小帽，手持神杖。塞赫麦特头顶日轮与圣蛇。居中的国王戴蓝冠、穿褶纹短裙，右肩处持着象征王权的弯钩杖，左手与女神的手相接。宽阔的肩膀和细致的腿部刻画，使他的形象格外有力量。\n这组红色花岗岩雕像于1904年发现于赫拉克利奥波利斯的赫里舍夫神庙附近。基座与背柱上的铭文提示，今天的塞赫麦特形象替代了更早的赫里舍夫神像，说明这件作品曾经被改刻。","src":"Discovered in 1904 near the courtyard of the Temple of Heryshef at Herakleopolis Magna (Ihnasya el-Medina), this red granite colossal represents King Ramesses II standing between god Ptah and goddess Sekhmet. Ptah, a god of craftsmen, whose cult was centred at Memphis, is shown mummy-shaped wearing a skull cap, a royal beard and holding a staff. His consort, the warrior goddess Sekhmet, is depicted with a lioness head topped with a sun disk and a protective uraeus snake. The central figure of King Ramesses II is muscular with broad shoulders and powerful upper arms. With its carefully modelled anatomical details, such as the protruding collarbones, rounded pectoral muscles, the remarkable kneecaps and the salient tibia bone, the King’s figure can hardly skip the attention of the viewer. Ramesses II wears a blue crown, also known as the khepresh crown, a pleated royal kilt (shendyt) ornamented with a leopard pendant and seven cobras, each crowned with a sun disk. On his right shoulder, he holds a crook, symbol of his kingship. His left arm extends along his body, touching the right hand of the goddess. It appears from the inscriptions carved on the statue base and the back pillar that the figure of goddess Sekhmet replaced an earlier figure of god Harsaphes. Nine vertical columns of text, incised on the back pillar, name King Ramesses II as the ‘beloved of’ the deities: Ptah, Horus, Heryshef, Bastet, Atum and Amun-Re.","i":9},{"id":"sarcophagus-of-nitocris","no":"2381","en":"Sarcophagus of Nitocris","cn":"尼托克丽丝石棺","g":"stairs","p":"后期埃及","d":"第 26 王朝","m":"花岗岩","dim":"高 80 cm · 宽 110 cm · 长 270 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":true,"n":1,"body":"这具大型花岗岩石棺属于第二十六王朝国王普萨美提克一世的女儿尼托克丽丝。她被授予“阿蒙—拉的神圣崇拜者”称号，是一位拥有重要宗教身份的王室女性。\n棺盖将她表现为双臂交叉的木乃伊形象，手持弯钩与连枷。石棺整体借鉴了新王国王室石棺的形式，面部造型则带有她所处的赛伊斯时代的风格。\n尼托克丽丝曾在麦迪奈特哈布为自己修建祭祀礼拜堂，石棺却于1885年出土于代尔麦地那的一处岩凿竖穴。这两个地点也为研究她的葬仪安排留下了线索。","src":"This massive granite sarcophagus was made for Nitocris, the daughter of King Psamtik I of Dynasty 26. Under her father’s reign, Nitocris was installed as a ‘Divine Adoratrice of Amun Re’. Like earlier priestesses who held the same title, she had a funerary chapel built for her at Medinet Habu. Her sarcophagus was, however, discovered in 1885 in a rock cut pit at Deir el-Medina. She is represented as a mummy lying with arms crossed on her chest, holding the crook and flail. The shape of the sarcophagus recalls New Kingdom royal sarcophagi although the facial features of the princess clearly reflect a Saite style.","i":10},{"id":"sphinx-of-king-amenemhat-iii","no":"1381","en":"Sphinx of King Amenemhat III","cn":"阿蒙涅姆赫特三世狮身人面像","g":"stairs","p":"中王国时期","d":null,"m":"花岗岩","dim":"高 144 cm · 宽 72 cm · 长 248.5 cm","prov":"下埃及 · 东部省","star":false,"n":1,"body":"与常见的“人头狮身”不同，这尊狮身人面像保留了更完整的狮子头部与身体，只有面部采用人的形象。这是中王国部分王室狮身人面像的典型特点。此类造型也与太阳神拉的崇拜有关。\n雕像以深色花岗岩制成，属于阿蒙涅姆赫特三世。它后来经历多次改刻：先被一位喜克索斯统治者占用，第十九王朝的拉美西斯二世和梅伦普塔又先后留下自己的印记。\n第二十一王朝普苏森尼斯一世在位时，雕像被运往塔尼斯，并于1861年在那里出土。它的漫长经历说明，王室雕像的历史往往远不止最初制作的那一刻。","src":"Statues of sphinxes are first attested in Egypt in Dynasty 4, the most famous example being the Great Sphinx at Giza. In ancient Egypt, this type of statuary was associated with the sun god Re. It usually represented a king with a human head and a lion’s body. Sphinxes of Middle Kingdom kings have a recognizable style showing a complete lion’s body and only a human face as in this dark granite sphinx. Discovered in 1861 at Tanis (San al–Hagar) in the Eastern Delta, it was first usurped by a Hyksos ruler in Dynasty 15 or 16, then by Ramesses II and Merenptah in Dynasty 19. Under King Psusennes I of Dynasty 21, the statue was finally brought to Tanis (San al–Hagar).","i":11},{"id":"doorway-of-king-amenemhat-i","no":"9590","en":"Doorway of King Amenemhat I","cn":"阿蒙涅姆赫特一世门道","g":"stairs","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"花岗岩","dim":"高 415 cm · 宽 75 cm · 长 280 cm","prov":"下埃及 · 东部省","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这组花岗岩构件由一块门楣和两根门柱组成。它们于1883年发现于尼罗河三角洲东部，可能原属于附近一座阿蒙涅姆赫特一世的宫殿。\n门道两面的铭文提供了不同年代的信息。一面记述阿蒙涅姆赫特一世建造这处建筑；另一面则记述近百年后的塞努塞尔特三世对它进行了修复。文字从门楣延伸至两侧门柱，把两位国王的活动留在同一座门道上。\n虽然原建筑的位置与面貌尚不完全清楚，这些构件仍保存了一段清晰的线索：一处王室建筑曾被后来的统治者修缮并继续使用。","src":"The granite blocks forming this doorway were discovered in 1883 at Ezbet Helmi in the Eastern Delta. It consists of a lintel and two jambs. It probably once stood at an unknown palace of Amenemhat I located at the nearby site of Ezbet Rushdi el-Saghira. Both faces of this portal are decorated with a text that starts on the lintel and continues down the jambs. One face bears a text stating that King Amenemhat I had constructed a monument, while the opposite face mentions that King Senwosret III, who ruled almost a hundred years later, renewed this monument.","i":12},{"id":"sarcophagus-of-djehutymose","no":"2192","en":"Sarcophagus of Djehutymose","cn":"杰胡提摩斯石棺","g":"stairs","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 19 王朝","m":"花岗岩","dim":"高 145 cm · 宽 105 cm · 长 225 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 明亚","star":false,"n":1,"body":"杰胡提摩斯的石棺上，几乎每组图像都与保护死者有关。他是第十九王朝的官员，曾管理阿蒙—拉神的牲畜，并负责托特神庙的工程。石棺于1915年出土于图纳盖贝勒。\n棺盖上的他呈木乃伊形态，双手交叉，握着象征生命的“安赫”和象征稳定的“杰德”符号。下方是张开双翼的天空女神努特，周围还有荷鲁斯四子、伊西斯与奈芙蒂斯等守护形象。\n棺身外壁多次出现鹮首的托特神，他托举天空符号，寓意为死者打开天空，使风进入鼻息。铭文除了《亡灵书》，还选用了《金字塔铭文》中的咒文，这在同时期石棺中颇为特别。","src":"This coarse-grained granite sarcophagus of Djehutymose was discovered in 1915 in a burial shaft at Tuna el-Gebel. Djehutymose served as the ‘Great Overseer of Cattle of Amun-Re in Upper and Lower Egypt’ and ‘Overseer of Works in the House of Thoth’ during Dynasty 19. On the lid, Djehutymose is shown in the shape of a mummy wearing a hair wig decorated with three garlands and a bouquet of lotus flowers. A broad collar and a pectoral adorn his chest and his hands are crossed on his chest in the Osiride form, clenching the ankh (life) and djed (stability). Below, the goddess Nut is kneeling with winged arms on the nwb sign (gold). Five transverse bands of text divide the lid into vignettes showing Djehutymose standing and kneeling before the Sons of Horus. At the foot end of the lid are two wedjat eyes and the goddesses Isis and Nephthys kneeling before the shen sign (eternity). Scenes of deities decorate the outer walls of the bottom of the sarcophagus, including the ibis-headed god Thoth who is depicted four times holding a standard with the heaven sign on top. His role is to open the sky to allow the four winds to enter the nose of the deceased. Interestingly, this sarcophagus was inscribed not only with spells from the Book of the Dead but also with excerpts from different spells from the Pyramid Texts not attested on other stone sarcophagi of that time.","i":13},{"id":"seated-statue-of-thutmose-iii","no":"3769","en":"Seated Statue of Thutmose III","cn":"图特摩斯三世坐像","g":"stairs","p":"新王国时期","d":null,"m":"花岗岩","dim":"高 195 cm · 宽 58 cm · 长 118 cm","prov":"上埃及","star":false,"n":1,"body":"图特摩斯三世端坐在王座上，头戴涅墨斯头巾，腰围王室短裙，双手掌心向下放在膝头。这种端正、稳定的姿态，是古埃及王室坐像常见的表现方式。\n这尊花岗岩雕像于1859年发现于卡纳克。王座正面两侧各有一列竖向铭文，记载国王的名字和王室头衔。观看时，可以将这些文字与人物装束一同辨认：它们共同说明了雕像主人的身份。","src":"A seated granite statue of Thutmose III discovered at Karnak in 1859. The statue shows the king seated on the throne, wearing the nemes headcloth and the shendyt royal kilt. His hands are placed, palms down, on his knees. On either jamb of the throne is a vertical line of text indicating his name and royal titles.","i":14},{"id":"standing-statue-of-king-thutmose-iii","no":"3771","en":"Standing Statue of King Thutmose III","cn":"图特摩斯三世立像","g":"stairs","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"花岗岩","dim":"高 180 cm · 宽 52 cm · 长 59 cm","prov":"上埃及","star":false,"n":1,"body":"腰带上的王名圈写着图特摩斯三世的名字，但这尊雕像可能并非最初为他制作。仔细观察王名圈周围略显粗糙的石面，还能辨认出较早名字的残留痕迹。\n据此推测，雕像原本可能属于哈特谢普苏特，后来才被改刻为图特摩斯三世。它于1860年发现于卡纳克阿蒙大神庙，人物头戴涅墨斯头巾、佩假胡须，身穿前襟突出的王室短裙。\n这件作品值得留意的，是新旧铭文之间的关系。外形相近的国王雕像，有时正是通过重刻姓名，被赋予了新的主人。","src":"This standing statue was discovered in 1860 at the Great Temple of Amun at Karnak. It represents a king wearing the traditional nemes headcloth, a false beard and a kilt with a projecting front section. Although the cartouche on the belt gives the name of King Thutmose III, traces of another name are still visible underneath the slightly roughened area around the cartouche. It is, therefore, probable that this statue was first made for Hatshepsut and was later on reinscribed for her stepson Thutmose III.","i":15},{"id":"pyramidion-of-an-obelisk-of-queen-hatshepsut","no":"4701","en":"Pyramidion of an Obelisk of Queen Hatshepsut","cn":"哈特谢普苏特方尖碑顶石","g":"stairs","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"红色花岗岩","dim":"高 340 cm · 宽 178 cm · 长 178 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这块红色花岗岩顶石，原属于哈特谢普苏特在卡纳克阿蒙—拉神庙竖立的一座方尖碑。它于1861年在图特摩斯三世节庆大厅后方被发现，下端还保留着一小段碑身。\n原来的浮雕表现女王跪在阿蒙—拉面前，由神为她头上的王冠赐福。后来，女王的形象被改成两座祭坛，神的手势也被调整，变为手持象征权能的瓦斯杖与象征生命的安赫符号。\n原本写有女王名字的前两列文字也遭到抹除。这些改动可能发生于图特摩斯三世时期。如今，图像与铭文的变化成为辨认这件作品历史的重要依据。","src":"This red granite pyramidion originally belonged to an obelisk erected by Queen Hatshepsut at the Temple of Amun-Re at Karnak. It was discovered in 1861 in the area behind King Thutmose III’s Hall of Festivals. It has been detached below its base and it includes a few centimeters of the shaft of the obelisk. The original representations showed the queen kneeling with her back to Amun-Re who blesses the crown on her head. Later, these were altered, probably by King Thutmose III, who replaced the figure of the queen with two altars and changed the gesture of the god who now holds the was scepter (prosperity) and the ankh sign (life). The first two columns of texts, which contained the queen's name, were also erased.","i":16},{"id":"king-ramesses-ii-and-a-goddess","no":"20084","en":"King Ramesses II and a Goddess","cn":"拉美西斯二世与一位女神","g":"stairs","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 19 王朝","m":"花岗岩","dim":"高 290 cm · 宽 90 cm · 长 160 cm","prov":"下埃及 · 东部省","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这组雕像中，女神一手触碰国王的王冠，另一手搭在他的手臂上，以亲近的动作表现守护关系。女神可能是来自西亚的战神阿纳特，她在埃及也被视为国王的保护者。\n红色花岗岩雕像的残件于1825年发现于塔尼斯阿蒙大神庙。虽然没有铭文直接说明身份，研究者仍依据国王的面部特征，以及当地发现的大量拉美西斯二世雕像，将其中的王者辨认为拉美西斯二世。\n观看时，可以留意两只手的位置。比起单独的王像，这些相互接触的动作，更直接地表达了国王受到神祇庇护的观念。","src":"Fragments of this red granite statue were discovered in 1825 in the Great Temple of Amun located at Tanis (San el-Hagar). The statue shows Ramesses II and a goddess (probably Anath, a foreign goddess of war who played the role of protector of the king). The goddess touches the king's crown with her right hand and rests her left hand on his arm. Though the statue does not have an inscription, it has been positively identified as Ramesses II as it has the facial features of the king and was found at Tanis where many other statues of the king have been uncovered.","i":17},{"id":"seated-statue-of-goddess-sekhmet","no":"45251","en":"Seated Statue of Goddess Sekhmet","cn":"塞赫麦特女神坐像","g":"stairs","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"花岗岩","dim":"高 172 cm · 宽 51 cm · 长 85 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"塞赫麦特是一位兼具破坏力与守护力量的女神，名字意为“强大者”。她与火焰、毁灭有关，同时也承担保护国王的职责。\n阿蒙霍特普三世曾在底比斯西岸的王室祭庙内安置多尊塞赫麦特坐像与立像。约三百年后，其中一部分被运过尼罗河，迁入卡纳克的穆特神庙。\n理解这尊女神像，可以从她的双重身份入手：令人敬畏的力量，也正是人们寻求庇护的力量。雕像的迁移则反映出，神像能够在不同神庙中继续受到供奉。","src":"Sekhmet, whose name means ‘she who is powerful’, was associated with fire and destruction, and also with protection of the king. King Amenhotep III placed sitting and standing statues of the goddess in his mortuary cult temple on the West Bank at Thebes. About 300 years later, some of the statues were transported across the River Nile to a temple of the goddess Mut at Karnak.","i":18},{"id":"hathor-capital","no":"21359","en":"Hathor Capital","cn":"哈托尔柱头","g":"stairs","p":"托勒密时期","d":null,"m":"红色花岗岩","dim":"高 260 cm · 宽 100 cm · 长 90 cm","prov":"下埃及","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这件柱头以哈托尔女神的头像为主体，上方托着一座小神龛，龛内伸出一条头戴日轮的蛇。如果把柱头与原来的柱身连在一起，整根柱子就像一件放大的叉铃。\n叉铃是一种摇奏乐器，也是哈托尔的象征。建筑因此借用了乐器的外形，把女神的标志融入神庙空间。\n柱头由红色花岗岩制成，1892至1893年间出土于尼罗河三角洲东部的门德斯。它可能属于一座柱厅，相关建筑与当地的圣公羊墓地有关。","src":"This red granite capital of a column was discovered in 1892-1893 during excavations at Mendes (Tell el-Ruba) in Eastern Delta. The head of goddess Hathor is topped by a naos (shrine) with a snake crowned with a sun disk projecting from within. The complete form of the column would have represented a gigantic sistrum (rattle), a musical instrument used as an emblem of goddess Hathor. It probably belonged to a hall of columns that formed part of a building connected with the cemetery of sacred rams at Mendes.","i":19},{"id":"falcon-shaped-palette","no":"600","en":"Falcon-Shaped Palette","cn":"隼形调色板","g":"main","p":"前王朝时期","d":"涅伽达文化三期","m":"片岩","dim":"高 13.8 cm · 宽 17.9 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 塔尔汗","star":true,"n":1,"body":"这块石板被雕成一只停栖的隼，出土于开罗以南约50公里的塔尔罕墓地。它属于前王朝时期常见的动物形调色板，用杂砂岩制成。\n这类平板最初用于研磨矿物颜料，供人们化妆使用。随着形制的发展，部分调色板也逐渐具有纪念和仪式用途。\n在约公元前3500至前3300年的涅伽达二期，动物形调色板较为流行。这只隼可能体现了荷鲁斯神的早期形象，而荷鲁斯后来与埃及王权紧密相连。它将日常梳妆用品与早期宗教观念联系在一起。","src":"Flat stone palettes of various shapes were produced in ancient Egypt since the Predynastic Period. They were first used for grinding minerals into pigments for cosmetic use, but their shape and function evolved over time to include a commemorative and ceremonial use as well. Animal-shaped palettes made of greywacke became common during Naqada II (about 3500‒3300 BC). This falcon-shaped palette was found at Tarkhan, an ancient Egyptian necropolis located about 50 km south of Cairo on the west bank of the Nile. The perched falcon possibly represents an early manifestation of god Horus who was closely linked to the ideology of kingship in ancient Egypt.","i":20},{"id":"beaker-with-river-nile-scene","no":"5500","en":"Beaker with River Nile Scene","cn":"尼罗河景纹陶杯","g":"main","p":"前王朝时期","d":null,"m":"陶、颜料","dim":"高 18 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 索哈杰","star":true,"n":1,"body":"陶杯上的鳄鱼、河马、鱼和植物，把前王朝时期的尼罗河环境带到了眼前。几何纹样穿插其间，使河谷中的动物与植物成为器物装饰的一部分。\n这件交叉线纹陶杯出土于纳加代尔。当地墓地延续时间很长，从前王朝早期一直到拜占庭时期，都留下了人类活动的痕迹。\n它所处的涅伽达文化，是埃及进入王朝时代之前的重要阶段。比起记住复杂的分期，更值得观察的是杯面上的选择：当时的人用熟悉的河流生物，装饰自己制作和使用的器物。","src":"The Naqada civilization dates back to prehistoric times in Egypt. It is classified by historians into three historical phases: Naqada I (about 4000–3500 BC), Naqada II (about 3500–3300 BC), and Naqada III (about 3300–3050 BC). Naqada I is generally known for its black-topped painted pottery, while Naqada II is noted for the introduction of marl pottery, usually with ochre-brown paintings on a beige background. This cross-lined ware beaker was discovered at Naga-el-Deir, a site with a number of cemeteries covering a remarkable span of time - from the early Predynastic to the Byzantine Period. The beaker reflects the rich Nile Valley environment in Egypt during Predynastic times. It is decorated with geometric shapes, plants, crocodiles, hippopotami and fish.","i":21},{"id":"stela-of-djer","no":"5429","en":"Stela of Djer","cn":"哲尔石碑","g":"main","p":"早王朝时期","d":"第 1 王朝","m":"石灰岩","dim":"高 80 cm · 宽 20 cm · 长 54.5 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 索哈杰","star":true,"n":1,"body":"石碑上方的隼与下方的宫殿式框格，共同构成了一种早期王名标识。框格称为“塞雷赫”，外形模仿宫殿正面，里面刻着第一王朝国王哲尔的名字；上方的隼则代表荷鲁斯。\n十九世纪末，考古人员在阿拜多斯乌姆卡阿布王室墓地发现了十块大小不一的王室石碑，分属八位早期统治者。它们很可能原本立在墓葬上方，用于标示墓主。\n这块碑顶部圆弧、底部平直。简洁的碑面集中表达了两件事：墓主是谁，以及他与王权之神荷鲁斯的联系。","src":"Excavations made at the end of the nineteenth century in the royal cemetery of Umm el-Qa’ab at Abydos uncovered ten royal tomb stelae (stone markers or monuments) of variable sizes. These stelae belonged to eight Early Dynastic Period rulers and most likely once stood as tomb markers above their tombs at Umm el-Qa’ab. During the reigns of Narmer to Merneith limestone was used for these stelae. From the reign of Den until the end of Dynasty 2 harder stones such as basalt, schist or granite were used. The stelae were usually decorated with the name of the king carved within a serekh (the niched façade of the palace) with the falcon-god Horus above. This stela has a rounded top and a flat base. Inside the serekh is the name of King Djer, who reigned during Dynasty 1.","i":22},{"id":"statue-of-the-royal-scribe-rahotep","no":"1127","en":"Statue of the Royal Scribe Rahotep","cn":"王室书吏拉霍特普像","g":"main","p":"古王国时期","d":"第 5 王朝","m":"雪花石膏（埃及雪花石）、颜料","dim":"高 32.5 cm · 宽 16 cm · 长 24.5 cm","prov":"孟菲斯 · 萨卡拉","star":true,"n":2,"body":"拉霍特普盘腿而坐，双手掌心向下，手指轻轻弯在短裙边缘。他戴着遮住耳朵的短卷发假发，颈部饰有彩绘项圈，基座正面的文字记录了他的姓名与头衔。\n他是第五王朝的一名王室书吏，墓葬于1861年在萨卡拉被发现。在古埃及，书吏承担王室通信、税收记录、宗教文书和法律契约的书写工作，是行政体系中十分重要的一群人。\n这尊雕像以安静的坐姿呈现一位文职人员。理解他的身份后，盘坐的姿态便有了更具体的含义：文字工作也能成为一个人留给后世的主要形象。","src":"This statue shows Rahotep, a royal scribe during Dynasty 5, whose tomb was discovered in 1861 at Saqqara. Scribes were held in great esteem by ancient Egyptian society. They were an essential part of the government as they were employed to write royal correspondence, record taxes, religious texts and all types of legal contracts. In this statue, Rahotep appears seated, legs crossed with his hands resting palms down, fingers gently curving over the hem of his kilt. He wears a short curly hair wig that covers his ears and a painted collar. The text on the front of the statue base lists his titles and name.","i":23},{"id":"canopic-chest-of-queen-hetepheres-i","no":"6363","en":"Canopic Chest of Queen Hetepheres I","cn":"赫特菲雷斯一世王后卡诺匹斯箱","g":"main","p":"古王国时期","d":"第 4 王朝","m":"雪花石膏（埃及雪花石）","dim":"高 34.8 cm · 宽 48.8 cm · 长 54.3 cm","prov":"孟菲斯","star":true,"n":1,"body":"这只石箱是保存死者内脏的卡诺匹斯箱，属于赫特菲雷斯一世王后。她是第四王朝国王斯尼夫鲁的妻子，也是胡夫的母亲。\n1925年，考古人员在吉萨发现王后的墓葬。石箱藏在墓室西壁的一处壁龛内，内部划分为四格。经历数千年后，箱中仍保存着经过处理的内脏残留，可能包括肝、肺、胃和肠。\n这件器物为了解早期王室木乃伊制作提供了实物证据：对身体的保存，并不只涉及遗体本身，也包括被取出后单独安置的器官。","src":"Canopic chests held the embalmed internal organs of the deceased in ancient Egypt. This travertine canopic chest was concealed in a niche cut in the west wall of the burial chamber of Queen Hetepheres I whose tomb was discovered in 1925 on the Giza Plateau. Hetepheres I was wife of King Sneferu and mother of King Khufu of Dynasty 4. Her canopic chest has four compartment that after five thousand years of her burial still contained the remains of her embalmed internal organs, possibly the liver, lungs, stomach and intestines.","i":24},{"id":"sandals-of-mesehti","no":"9200","en":"Sandals of Mesehti","cn":"梅塞赫提的凉鞋","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 11 王朝","m":"木","dim":"高 5.8 cm · 长 26.4 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 阿西尤特","star":true,"n":1,"body":"这双凉鞋的鞋底由木头制成，白色皮革鞋带由靠近后部的两根竖柱支撑。材质和结构都清楚可见，呈现出与现代凉鞋不同的制作方式。\n它出土于艾斯尤特的梅塞赫提墓。梅塞赫提是第十一王朝的地方长官，墓中还发现了其他随葬用品。\n埃及人早在早王朝时期就已制作鞋履，使用的材料包括植物纤维、草、皮革和木材。这双随葬凉鞋也让人看到，墓葬中除了仪式用品，还会保存与日常穿用有关的物件。","src":"The ancient Egyptians had been making footwear since the Early Dynastic Period. They used a variety of materials, such as fibre, straw, leather and wood. This pair of sandals was found among other funerary equipment in the tomb of Mesehti who served as a provincial governor of Asyut in Dynasty 11. They have wooden soles and white leather straps supported by two vertical poles near the back of the sandal.","i":25},{"id":"exterior-coffin-of-mesehti","no":"9293","en":"Exterior Coffin of Mesehti","cn":"梅塞赫提外棺","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 11 王朝","m":"木","dim":"高 107 cm · 宽 94 cm · 长 241 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 阿西尤特","star":true,"n":2,"body":"梅塞赫提的墓中出土了内外两具木棺，这件是外棺。他是艾斯尤特的地方长官，同时负责乌普瓦韦特与阿努比斯的祭司事务。双层棺的配置，反映了他在中王国时期的地位。\n棺上的铭文部分取自《金字塔铭文》，用来为死者祈求保护。两只镶嵌的“乌加特”眼也值得留意：它们可能被认为能让棺内的死者与生者世界保持联系。\n对当时的非王室成员来说，使用双层棺并不寻常。木棺的数量、铭文和装饰，共同说明这是一场为重要官员安排的隆重安葬。","src":"A set of two wooden coffins were found in the tomb of Mesehti in Asyut. Mesehti was a nomarch of Asyut and an overseer of priests of Wepwawet and Anubis. This exterior coffin of Mesehti bears inscriptions that are partly derived from the Pyramid Texts. The two inlaid wedjat eyes possibly allowed him to communicate with the living. For an individual, to rest inside a double coffin was exceptional. Therefore, the presence of this exterior coffin reflects the prestige of Mesehti as an important official in the Middle Kingdom.","i":26},{"id":"silver-lion-treasure-of-tod","no":"65731","en":"Silver Lion (Treasure of Tod)","cn":"托德宝藏·银狮","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"银","dim":"高 2.7 cm · 宽 2.4 cm · 长 5 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":true,"n":2,"body":"这只小银狮侧身卧着，前爪收拢，尾巴向前弯成一圈。微张的嘴像是在打哈欠，也可能是在低声鸣叫，姿态显得轻松而自然。\n它于1936年与其他器物一同出土，属于“托德宝藏”的一部分。研究者推测，这件精巧的小像可能曾被用作称量物品的砝码，但用途尚不能完全确定。\n观看时，可以留意它身体的倾斜和尾巴的弧度。雕刻者通过这些细小变化，让一只体量不大的银狮显出了生动的神态。","src":"This small recumbent silver lion was discovered in 1936 among other artefacts in the Tod Treasure. The front paws of the lion are brought in together, its relaxed body lays partially on its side with its tail curled forward in a loop. Utterly charming, its mouth is slightly opened perhaps in a yawn or vocalization. The exquisite figure may have served as a weight for measuring.","i":27},{"id":"a-cup-treasure-of-tod","no":"65866","en":"A Cup (Treasure of Tod)","cn":"托德宝藏·银杯","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"银","dim":"高 9 cm · 宽 11 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":true,"n":1,"body":"这只银杯出土时曾被折叠、压扁，后来才恢复成今天的形状。杯壁十分纤薄，制作精巧，也因此让人怀疑它是否用于日常饮用。\n银杯属于托德宝藏。研究者提出，这批银器可能最初是外交赠礼，随后由国王献给托德神庙供奉的蒙图神，作为仪式供品保存下来。\n这些解释仍属推测，但它们提示了理解银杯的另一种角度：一件器皿除了实际用途，也可能经历馈赠、收藏和奉献，承载人与人、人与神之间的关系。","src":"A silver cup, originally folded and flattened, now returned to its original shape. This thin-walled vessel is surprisingly delicate and may not have had a practical purpose. It is possible that the silver vessels found in the Tod Treasure were received as diplomatic gifts and were then deposited by the king as part of his ritual offering to god Montu to whom the Temple of Tod was dedicated.","i":28},{"id":"statue-of-horemheb-as-a-standard-bearer","no":"2226","en":"Statue of Horemheb as a Standard-Bearer","cn":"霍伦海布执杖像","g":"main","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"硅化木","dim":"高 59 cm · 宽 16 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":true,"n":2,"body":"国王左脚向前，左臂旁立着一根长杖，姿态端正。这尊雕像以硅化木制成，于1904年出土于卡纳克窖藏。\n背柱上的象形文字写着霍伦海布的名字，但人物服装的样式，却让人联想到阿蒙霍特普四世在位时的流行风格。\n名字与造型提供了两种不同的线索。观看这件作品时，可以同时留意铭文与服饰，而不只凭王名判断它的全部经历。这种细节上的差异，也是研究古埃及雕像的重要依据。","src":"A statue of silicified wood discovered in 1904 in the Karnak Cache (CK 144). It shows a king, left foot forward, holding a long staff against his left arm. The clothing style of the statue recalls a style in vogue under Amenhotep IV, although the hieroglyphic text on the back pillar gives the name of King Horemheb.","i":29},{"id":"group-statue-of-amun-re-king-thutmose-i-and-queen-ahmose","no":"3760","en":"Group Statue of Amun-Re, King Thutmose I and Queen Ahmose","cn":"阿蒙-拉、图特摩斯一世与阿摩斯王后组像","g":"main","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"雪花石膏","dim":"高 68 cm · 宽 20 cm · 长 45 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":true,"n":5,"body":"阿蒙—拉坐在中央，图特摩斯一世与阿摩斯王后分居两侧。国王和王后的手臂从神的身后伸过，阿蒙则把一只手搭在王后肩头。相互连接的动作，强调了王室与神祇的亲近关系。\n这组雕像出土于卡纳克窖藏。铭文写的是第十八王朝早期的国王与王后，人物面部的塑造却带有图坦卡蒙时期常见的风格。\n研究者据此推测，雕像可能在阿肯那顿的宗教改革中受损，随后于图坦卡蒙时期得到修复。今天所见的形象，或许同时保留了最初制作与后来修复的痕迹。","src":"This group statue was found in the Karnak Cache (CK 96). It represents the god Amun-Re enthroned between King Thutmose I and Queen Ahmose, reflecting the close relationship between the divine and royalty. Thutmose I passes his left arm behind Amun and holds a royal handkerchief in his right hand. Amun holds an ankh sign (life) in his right hand and places his other hand on the left shoulder of Queen Ahmose. The queen’s right arm passes behind Amun, while her left hand is extended flat on her thigh. Interestingly, although it is King Thutmose I and Queen Ahmose of early Dynasty 18 who are named in the text, the modelling of the facial features recalls a style common under Tutankhamun. It is, therefore, possible that the group had fallen victim to Akhenaten’s religious revolution and was later restored under Tutankhamun.","i":30},{"id":"statue-of-bakenkhonsu","no":"5998","en":"Statue of Bakenkhonsu","cn":"巴肯孔苏像","g":"main","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 20 王朝","m":"深色花岗岩","dim":"高 105 cm · 宽 26.5 cm · 长 42 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":true,"n":3,"body":"巴肯孔苏双手握着羊首长杖，左腿前迈。他是第二十王朝卡纳克的阿蒙大祭司，羊首正是阿蒙神的象征。杖首的公羊还饰有圣蛇和宽项圈。\n他身穿宽袖长袍与三角形前襟，雕像左侧刻着儿子阿蒙涅姆奥佩特持扇的形象。双肩上的王名圈属于拉美西斯三世，基座则记有巴肯孔苏本人的姓名与头衔。\n这尊像于1904年发现于卡纳克窖藏，出土时头部已与身体分离。长杖和背柱上的祈祷铭文向诸神请求供品，表明这件雕像也承担着为主人祈求福祉的作用。","src":"Bakenkhonsu (III) was a 'First Prophet of Amun at Karnak' in Dynasty 20. His statue was discovered in 1904 in the Karnak Cache (CK 75). Upon its discovery, the head was found separated from the rest of the statue. Bakenkhnosu (III) stands with his left leg forward. He holds a ram-headed staff (symbol of the god Amun) in both hands. On the head of the ram is a uraeus snake, and around its neck is the wesekh collar. He wears a long robe with flared sleeves and a triangular apron. On the left side of the statue, his son Amenemopet is represented holding the khou-fan. On the two shoulders of the statue are the cartouches of King Ramesses III. Bakenkhnosu’s name and titles are written on the pedestal. Two offering prayers, on the ram-headed staff and on the back pillar, invoke the deities to grant him offerings.","i":31},{"id":"block-statue-of-wsirwer","no":"3993","en":"Block Statue of Wsirwer","cn":"乌西尔维尔方块坐像","g":"main","p":"后期埃及","d":"第 30 王朝","m":"黑色花岗岩","dim":"高 34 cm · 宽 13.1 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":true,"n":7,"body":"乌西尔维尔把双腿收在胸前，双臂交叠在膝上，身体包裹在披衣中，整体形成近似方块的轮廓。只有双手以浮雕形式显露在衣外，这是方块坐像很有辨识度的特点。\n披衣正面刻着一尊小型奥西里斯神像，两旁各有一列文字。结合其他铭文可知，乌西尔维尔担任过“神父”、负责神像衣饰的祭司，以及工程监督等职务。\n这件花岗岩雕像于1904年出土于卡纳克窖藏。观看时，可以从整体的方形轮廓，再转向衣面上的小神像与文字，辨认人物身份和宗教诉求。","src":"This granite squatting statue was discovered by G. Legrain in the Karnak Cache (CK 405) in 1904. Its owner Wsirwer wears a shoulder-length hair wig and a false beard. His legs are drawn up before his chest and his arms are crossed over his knees. His body is fully enveloped in a cloak, only the hands are indicated in relief, protruding from the cloak. A small figure of god Osiris, flanked by two vertical columns of text, decorate the front of his cloak. It appears from the texts on the statue that Wsirwer held important priestly titles, such as the ‘god Father’, ‘Stolist’ and ‘Supervisor of Works’","i":32},{"id":"mummified-child-in-gilded-cartonnage","no":"5782","en":"Mummified Child in Gilded Cartonnage","cn":"贴金木乃伊罩中的孩童","g":"main","p":"希腊罗马时期","d":null,"m":"亚麻布胎彩绘、金","dim":"高 33 cm · 宽 42 cm · 长 125 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 贝尼苏韦夫","star":true,"n":2,"body":"木棺内安放着一名小女孩的木乃伊，身体外包覆着贴金的卡通纳吉罩。所谓“卡通纳吉”，是将织物与石膏等材料层层塑形后制成的葬仪用品。\n在罗马时期的埃及，这种材料常用于木乃伊面具和身体上的装饰片。因为女孩身形较小，工匠能够制作覆盖全身的外罩。\n细致的工艺与金饰反映出家庭为安葬她投入了相当的资源。面对这件展品，除了观察材料与装饰，也可以想到它最初的用途：为一个早逝的孩子安排身后的守护。","src":"Mummified child in a gilded cartonnage placed inside a wooden coffin. Cartonnage refers to the moulded layers of plastered fabric used by ancient Egyptians for different funerary purposes. During the Roman Period, it was primarily used for creating masks and decorative pieces placed on the deceased. Here, it was possible to cover the entire body with cartonnage given the small size of this young girl. The beautiful artistry and the amount of gold used speak to the wealth of her family and possibly how much they missed her.","i":33},{"id":"vessel-with-gazelles","no":"5476","en":"Vessel with Gazelles","cn":"彩绘羚羊纹双耳罐","g":"main","p":"前王朝时期","d":"涅伽达文化二期","m":"陶、颜料","dim":"高 9.5 cm · 长 14.5 cm · 直径 14 cm","prov":null,"star":false,"n":1,"body":"这只陶罐的装饰分为上下两层：上方排列着羚羊，下方是一圈三角纹带。两侧把手绘有竖线，并留有可供穿绳的小孔。宽阔的罐底略平，口沿下方则有内收的转折。\n这类容器可以用于日常盛放食物和饮品，也会作为随葬品进入墓中，为死者来世的生活作准备。\n它的看点在于器形与纹饰的配合：穿绳孔、宽底和口沿关系到使用方式，动物与几何纹样则让实用器物兼具装饰性。","src":"This pottery vessel has a slightly flattened broad base, an undercut lip on the rim and two handles with holes for strings. It is painted with two rows of decoration - gazelles above triangle friezes. The handles are decorated with vertical lines. Vessels like this would be used for food and drink in daily life and for the afterlife.","i":34},{"id":"statue-of-duaptah-and-his-father","no":"1076","en":"Statue of Duaptah and his Father","cn":"杜阿普塔与父亲像","g":"main","p":"古王国时期","d":null,"m":"石灰岩、颜料","dim":"高 72 cm · 宽 28 cm · 长 32 cm","prov":"不明","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这组石灰岩雕像表现一位父亲与成年的儿子。父亲体形较大，左腿前迈；儿子双脚并拢，站在一旁。两人都戴短卷发假发，留细小胡须，穿着样式相近的及膝短裙。\n父亲的名字已经无法辨读，较小人物身旁的文字却保存了“他的儿子，书吏杜阿普塔”的身份。两张相似的脸，也加强了父子之间的联系。\n这类形象近似的组像在古王国第五、六王朝短暂流行。有些重复表现同一个人，有些则加入家庭成员。本件将相近的面容与不同的站姿、比例结合，呈现出父子二人的关系。","src":"Pseudo-group statues are a short-lived type of statuary that flourished briefly during Dynasties 5 and 6 of the Old Kingdom. The statues often showed the figure of the deceased repeated twice or more, and in some examples, he is accompanied by a family member. This type is characterized by the almost identical similarity in facial features, costume and sometimes in the attitude of the depicted figures. This limestone statue represents a man and his adult son. The father’s name is no longer legible but the surviving text refers to the smaller figure as ‘his son, the scribe Duaptah’. Both figures are depicted standing on a plinth that protrudes slightly in front of the taller figure. Duaptah stands with his feet together, while his father strides with the left leg forward. The son is markedly smaller, but the similarity in their facial features is unmistakable. Each wears a short curly hair wig and has a small thin moustache. Both figures are in similar clothes, each wears a knee-length kilt with a pleated flap, the tip of which is pulled up through the belt.","i":35},{"id":"seated-statue-of-a-man","no":"1108","en":"Seated Statue of a Man","cn":"无名男子坐像","g":"main","p":"古王国时期","d":null,"m":"花岗岩","dim":"高 68 cm · 宽 21.5 cm · 长 36 cm","prov":"孟菲斯","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这位身份未明的男子端坐在方形座椅上，脚下基座的前缘呈圆弧形。他戴着中分的齐肩假发，露出双耳，身穿及膝短裙。\n两只手采用不同姿势：右手握拳放在大腿上，左手平放。这样细微的变化，使端正的坐姿仍有清楚可辨的层次。\n这尊花岗岩雕像来自萨卡拉。虽然主人的姓名未能确定，发式、衣着、座椅和手势，仍为我们观察古埃及人物雕像提供了具体线索。","src":"A granite statue from Saqqara showing a man seated on a cube seat with a rounded-front plinth. He wears a shoulder-length parted hair wig that leaves his ears exposed and a short kilt reaching to his knees. His right hand is closed in a fist on his thigh, while the left hand rests flat.","i":36},{"id":"seated-male-figure","no":"1112","en":"Seated Male Figure","cn":"男子坐像（方解石）","g":"main","p":"古王国时期","d":"第 5 王朝","m":"方解石","dim":"高 55.7 cm · 宽 20 cm · 长 29.4 cm","prov":"孟菲斯 · 萨卡拉","star":false,"n":1,"body":"男子端坐，戴着有条纹的齐肩假发，耳朵被遮住一半。他颈部佩宽项圈和护身符，身穿及膝短裙，右手握起，左手掌心向下放在膝头。\n这件坐像保留了彩绘。发式、颈饰与手势共同构成人物的形象，说明古埃及雕像的表现并不只依靠石材本身，也会借助色彩。\n观看时，可以先比较左右手的姿势，再留意项圈与护身符的位置。这些细节让一尊姿态简洁的坐像具有了更丰富的内容。","src":"A painted limestone statue showing a seated male figure. He wears a striated shoulder-length hair wig that half covers his ears, a broad collar, an amulet and a short kilt reaching to his knees. His right hand is closed and the left hand is placed, palm down, on his left knee.","i":37},{"id":"statue-of-the-scribe-mitri","no":"1128","en":"Statue of the Scribe Mitri","cn":"书吏米特里像","g":"main","p":"古王国时期","d":"第 5 王朝","m":"木、颜料","dim":"高 81.5 cm · 宽 50 cm · 长 100 cm","prov":"孟菲斯 · 萨卡拉","star":false,"n":2,"body":"米特里盘腿坐着，膝上放着一卷展开了一部分的纸莎草纸，呈现出书吏工作时的典型姿态。这尊彩绘木像以镶嵌石材制作双眼，使沉静的面容显得格外有神。\n他生活在第五王朝，身穿短裙，颈佩宽项圈。基座上的铭文列出了姓名与多项职衔，其中包括地方行政官、玛阿特女神祭司和书吏监督。\n雕像将纸卷放在人物形象的中心。对米特里来说，书写既是一项技能，也与他的行政和宗教职责紧密相关。","src":"This painted wooden statue belongs to Mitri who held many important titles during Dynasty 5. The statue shows him sitting in the traditional pose of an Egyptian scribe with his legs crossed and a roll of papyrus partly unrolled on his lap. He wears a short kilt and a broad collar. His thoughtful face is framed by short hair and he has magnetic eyes made with inlaid stone. Mitri’s name and titles are written on the statue base. Some of his titles include 'Nome Administrator', 'Priest of the goddess Maat' and 'Overseer of Scribes'.","i":38},{"id":"statue-of-rawer","no":"1162","en":"Statue of Rawer","cn":"拉维尔像","g":"main","p":"古王国时期","d":"第 5 王朝","m":"石灰岩","dim":"高 93 cm · 宽 25 cm · 长 45.5 cm","prov":"孟菲斯 · 萨卡拉","star":false,"n":2,"body":"拉维尔左腿前迈，双臂垂在身体两侧，戴短卷发假发，身穿短裙。脚边的基座上刻着他的姓名与头衔，包括荷鲁斯祭司、诵读祭司和宫廷主管。\n这尊第五王朝石灰岩雕像出土于萨卡拉拉维尔墓中的“塞尔达布”。这是墓内专门安置雕像的隐蔽房间。\n明确的姓名、职衔和安放地点，让我们能够把这尊立像与一位具体的官员联系起来。他的形象被留在墓中，成为其身份与宗教活动的见证。","src":"This limestone statue was found in the serdab (hidden room) of the mastaba tomb (D 29) of Rawer at Saqqara. Rawer held important titles that linked him to the priesthood and administration in Dynasty 5. His titles included: priest of Horus, lector priest and director of the palace. He is depicted with his left leg forward, his arms by his sides. He wears a short curly wig and a short kilt. His name and titles are carved on the base next to his feet.","i":39},{"id":"statuette-of-a-servant-roasting-a-goose","no":"1180","en":"Statuette of a Servant Roasting a Goose","cn":"烤禽仆役小像","g":"main","p":"古王国时期","d":"第 6 王朝","m":"木、颜料","dim":"高 24.5 cm · 宽 12 cm · 长 22 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 阿西尤特","star":false,"n":2,"body":"这名仆役蹲在炉前，一手照看串在烤叉上的鸭子，右手持扇拨动热炭。简单的动作组合，清楚呈现了烤制食物的过程。\n彩绘木像出土于梅尔的尼安赫佩皮凯姆墓。墓主生活在第六王朝佩皮一世时期，随葬品包括船模型和十七件仆役小像。\n古王国高官墓中常放置表现日常劳作的仆役像，希望借此保障死者来世的生活。眼前的烤禽场景，正是将“有人准备食物”的愿望做成了可以随葬的模型。","src":"Servant statuettes are among the most significant funerary goods included in the burials of high officials during the Old Kingdom. They typically showed servants performing daily life activities and were placed in burials to ensure the welfare of the deceased in the afterlife. One of the largest groups of this type was discovered in the tomb of Niankhpepikem at the necropolis of Meir. Niankhpepikem served under King Pepy I (Meryre) and his burial goods included model boats and seventeen servant statuettes. This painted wooden statuette is from the tomb of Niankhpepikem and it shows a servant squatting while roasting a spitted duck over a hearth, stoking the hot coals with a fan in his right hand.","i":40},{"id":"statuette-of-two-women-making-beer","no":"1184","en":"Statuette of Two Women Making Beer","cn":"酿酒二女像","g":"main","p":"古王国时期","d":"第 6 王朝","m":"木、颜料","dim":"高 31 cm · 宽 11.1 cm · 长 39.3 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 阿西尤特","star":false,"n":1,"body":"两名女子站在大陶罐前，低头处理酿酒用的混合物。她们都留短发、穿白色短裙，动作集中在罐口，表现的是过滤酒醪的工序。\n这组彩绘木模型出土于梅尔的尼安赫佩皮凯姆墓，年代为第六王朝佩皮一世时期。当时的酿酒方法包括把烤熟的面包掰碎、加水调成糊状，再过滤到容器中发酵；椰枣和蜂蜜等也可用于酿制。\n模型把一项日常生产活动带进墓葬，寄托着让死者在来世继续获得饮品的愿望，也为了解古埃及的食品制作留下了直观材料。","src":"A painted wooden servant statuette found among several other models in the tomb of Niankhpepikem at the necropolis of Meir . The owner of the tomb lived during the reign of King Pepy I (Meryre) in Dynasty 6. This model shows two women with short hair and short white kilts standing in front of two large jars used for brewing beer. They are straining the beer mash into the jars. In the beer brewing process, beer mash was made by mixing pieces of cooked bread loaves into water to create a porridge-like mixture. The mash was then strained into heated jars with yeast, dates and honey to begin the fermentation process to create beer.","i":41},{"id":"statue-of-ishetji","no":"1185","en":"Statue of Ishetji","cn":"伊舍提像","g":"main","p":"古王国时期","d":"第 6 王朝","m":"木、颜料","dim":"高 71 cm · 宽 20.5 cm · 长 39.5 cm","prov":"孟菲斯 · 萨卡拉","star":false,"n":1,"body":"伊舍提左脚前迈，右手持塞赫姆权杖，左手握手杖。短假发、小胡须和带有神采的面容，共同塑造了一位高级官员的形象。\n他在第六王朝佩皮二世时期任职，头衔包括“下埃及国王的掌玺官”和佩皮一世、佩皮二世金字塔庄园的主管。基座铭文还称他为“国王唯一的伴臣”。\n这尊彩绘木像于1950年在萨卡拉阶梯金字塔围墙附近的墓穴中被发现。面部刻画生动，可能保留了墓主本人的相貌特点，但是否属于忠实肖像，仍需谨慎看待。","src":"This beautiful painted wooden statue was discovered in 1950 during work to reconstruct the entrance to the enclosure of the Step Pyramid at Saqqara. A group of late Dynasty 6 burial shafts were discovered about one hundred metres from the northwest corner of the enclosure. One of the shafts belonged to Ishetji who held many important administrative titles under King Pepy II (Neferkare) including 'Sealer of the King of Lower Egypt' and 'Chief of Estates of the Pyramids of Pepy I and Pepy II'. Among the discovered objects in his burial shaft was this statue that shows him standing with his left foot forward, holding the sekhem sceptre in his right hand and a walking stick in the left. Ishetji wears a short wig and has the small beard in fashion with high officials. The vigorous and expressive face of the statue may be a faithful portrait of the man. Inscribed on the statue base are his name and two of his titles, 'Sealer of the King of Lower Egypt' and 'Sole Companion of the King'.","i":42},{"id":"statue-of-ishetji-1","no":"1186","en":"Statue of Ishetji","cn":"伊舍提像（持长杖）","g":"main","p":"古王国时期","d":"第 6 王朝","m":"木、颜料","dim":"高 71 cm · 宽 24.2 cm · 长 34.5 cm","prov":"孟菲斯 · 萨卡拉","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这尊彩绘木像表现伊舍提手持两种杖具的姿态：右手是塞赫姆权杖，左手是一根长杖，左腿向前迈出。木材便于细致雕刻，工匠借此表现出身体的轮廓与行进的动势。\n伊舍提是第六王朝末期的高级官员，担任过“下埃及国王的掌玺官”。1950年，人们在萨卡拉发现他的墓穴，墓中保存了一组大小不一的木雕，本件是其中之一。\n与同一墓主的其他雕像对照，可以观察工匠如何通过比例、持物和姿态的变化，塑造同一个人的不同形象。","src":"A remarkable painted wooden statue of a high official named Ishetji who served as ‘Sealer of the King of Lower Egypt’ towards the end of Dynasty 6. His burial shaft, discovered at Saqqara in 1950, housed a group of wooden statues and statuettes including this one. Ishetji is here shown with his left leg forward, holding a sekhem sceptre in his right hand and a long staff in the left. His body is finely carved using the lightness of wood to emphasize the natural movement of the active Ishetji.","i":43},{"id":"stela-of-neibunesut","no":"2443","en":"Stela of Neibunesut","cn":"涅布内苏特石碑","g":"main","p":"古王国时期","d":null,"m":"砂岩","dim":"高 31 cm · 长 19 cm · 厚 3 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 基纳","star":false,"n":1,"body":"石碑右侧的男子面向左方，头戴齐肩假发，身披豹皮，手持赫雷普权杖与连枷。他就是碑主涅布内苏特。\n这块长方形砂岩碑出土于丹德拉的墓葬。简短的象形文字说明，涅布内苏特曾担任哈托尔的大祭司，而丹德拉自早王朝时期起就是哈托尔的重要崇拜地点。\n碑面没有铺陈复杂场景，而是通过人物服饰、持物和职衔，集中说明他的宗教身份。观看时，可以将豹皮与铭文放在一起理解，认识这位祭司如何希望后人记住自己。","src":"A rectangular sandstone stela from the tomb of Neibunesut at Dendera. The stela owner is depicted standing on the right, facing left, holding the kherep sceptre and a flail. He wears a shoulder length hair wig and a leopard skin. According to the short hieroglyphic text on the stela, Neibunesut served as a ‘High Priest of Hathor’ whose cult was well established at Dendera since early dynastic times.","i":44},{"id":"group-statue-of-shepsi-and-his-family","no":"4569","en":"Group Statue of Shepsi and His Family","cn":"舍普西家族群像","g":"main","p":"古王国时期","d":"第 5 王朝","m":"石灰岩","dim":"高 66 cm · 宽 36 cm · 长 41 cm","prov":"孟菲斯","star":false,"n":3,"body":"舍普西坐在椅上，妻子尼考站在身旁，用右臂环抱着他。儿子则站在椅前，手指放在嘴边——这是古埃及艺术表现儿童时常见的姿态。\n这组石灰岩雕像出土于萨卡拉。舍普西是第五王朝的宫廷官员，尼考则担任哈托尔的女祭司。基座铭文记录了家人的姓名与头衔。\n人物比例体现了当时的表现惯例：妻子的身体明显小于丈夫，但因为丈夫坐着，两人的面部处在相近高度。观看这组像，既能辨认身份等级，也能看到家人之间通过拥抱和相伴表达的联系。","src":"A limestone group statue discovered at Saqqara. It belongs to Shepsi who served as an elder of the court in Dynasty 5. Shepsi is seated on a chair, looking straight ahead, his right hand closed in a fist on his right thigh, while his left hand rests palm down on the left thigh. He wears a short hair wig, a broad collar and a short kilt. His wife Nikau stands next to him. She served as a high priestess of goddess Hathor. Nikau wears a short hair wig and a close fitting dress. She embraces her husband with her right arm, while her left arm hangs down by her side. In conformity with ancient Egyptian art traditions, Nikau is smaller in scale than her husband and although Shepsi is seated, their faces are at the same level. At the front of Shepsi’s chair, his son Shepsipoudjed stands with his finger to his mouth. The hieroglyphic text on the plinth states their names and titles.","i":45},{"id":"group-statue-of-kai-and-family","no":"5332","en":"Group Statue of Kai and Family","cn":"凯伊与家人群像","g":"main","p":"古王国时期","d":"第 4 王朝","m":"石灰岩、颜料","dim":"高 56 cm · 宽 22 cm · 长 36 cm","prov":"孟菲斯 · 吉萨","star":false,"n":3,"body":"凯伊坐在中央，右臂横在胸前，左手平放在大腿上。儿子舍普塞斯卡站在他的右腿旁，女儿奈芙蕾特安赫跪在左侧，双臂抱着父亲的腿。镶嵌的双眼，让凯伊的面容格外醒目。\n这组雕像于1992年出土于吉萨墓地。凯伊大约生活在第四王朝末至第五王朝初，兼具祭司、法官、书吏等多种身份。铭文还说明，他与多位第四王朝国王的祭祀有关。\n孩子们围绕父亲的姿态，是这件作品最容易打动人的部分。王朝与职衔之外，雕像也保存了一个家庭希望长久相伴的形象。","src":"This exceptional group statue was discovered in 1992 at the Giza Necropolis (G1741). It shows the priest Kai with his son and daughter. Kai (also known as Kapunesut Kai) sits looking straight ahead with his right arm crossed against his chest and his left palm resting flat on his thigh. He wears a short hair wig and a knee-length kilt. His eyes are beautifully inlaid. His son Shepseska is shown standing beside his right leg while his daughter Nefretankh is kneeling, embracing her father's left leg. Kai held several important titles, most likely at the end of Dynasty 4 or early in Dynasty 5. Inscriptions on the statue base refer to Kai as ‘Priest of Horus of Behdet, Overseer of Mortuary Priests, Judge, Scribe, Sailor, Priest of Seshat and Steward of the Great Estate’. Inscriptions decorating tomb G1741, which possibly belongs to his daughter Nefretankh, state that Kai also served the cults of the kings Snefru, Khufu, Khafre and Djedefre who ruled Egypt in Dynasty 4.","i":46},{"id":"carrying-chair-of-queen-hetepheres-i","no":"6362","en":"Carrying Chair of Queen Hetepheres I","cn":"赫特菲雷斯一世王后的抬椅","g":"main","p":"古王国时期","d":"第 4 王朝","m":"金、木","dim":"高 56.6 cm · 宽 64 cm · 长 207.5 cm","prov":"孟菲斯","star":false,"n":2,"body":"这把抬椅由随从肩扛，供赫特菲雷斯一世王后出行使用。两根抬杆包覆金箔与银，椅背的镶嵌铭文记录了王后的姓名和头衔。如今所见的木质部分经过修复。\n抬椅出自吉萨大金字塔附近的王后墓。她的随葬品由儿子胡夫重新安置在这处隐蔽的地下墓室内。\n这件家具将王室生活呈现得十分具体：王后的移动方式、侍从的服务，以及器物上的贵金属装饰，都体现了第四王朝宫廷生活的奢华。","src":"The funerary equipment of Queen Hetepheres I was reburied by her son King Khufu in a secret underground tomb (G7000X) next to the Great Pyramid of Giza. Among the discovered objects in her tomb was this carrying chair that would have been lifted on the shoulders of her attendants. It is made of wood (restored) and has two carrying poles covered in gold foil and silver. The inlaid inscription on the back gives the queen’s titles and name. The contents of the queen’s tomb give a startling glimpse of the luxurious life of royalty during Dynasty 4.","i":47},{"id":"headrest-of-queen-hetepheres-i","no":"6425","en":"Headrest of Queen Hetepheres I","cn":"赫特菲雷斯一世王后的头枕","g":"main","p":"古王国时期","d":"第 4 王朝","m":"木、金、银","dim":"高 20.1 cm · 宽 8.9 cm · 长 18.6 cm","prov":"孟菲斯","star":false,"n":1,"body":"古埃及的头枕以弧形托面支撑头部，与今天柔软的枕头很不一样。它既是日常寝具，也被赋予夜间保护与死后复生的含义。\n这件头枕属于赫特菲雷斯一世王后。她是斯尼夫鲁的妻子、胡夫的母亲，墓葬于1925年在吉萨发现。一般认为，她最初可能葬在代赫舒尔，后来随葬品与石棺被迁至胡夫金字塔附近，迁移原因尚不明确。\n在古埃及的葬仪观念中，头枕托起死者的头部，可以比拟太阳每天从东方升起。这也解释了为什么一件寝具会成为重要的随葬用品。","src":"Ancient Egyptian headrests were believed to magically protect the sleeper at night. In the Book of the Dead, the funerary function of headrests is to support the head of the deceased during resurrection, just as the sun rises above the eastern horizon each morning. This headrest was discovered among the collection of Queen Hetepheres I, the wife of King Sneferu and mother of King Khufu, both of whom ruled in Dynasty 4. Her tomb (G7000X) was discovered in 1925 on the Giza Plateau. The queen is believed to have been first buried at Dahshur near her husband's pyramid. For reasons unknown, her funerary equipment including her sarcophagus were reburied at Giza, near her son's pyramid. This headrest, among other objects in her tomb, reflect the luxurious life of a royal person during Dynasty 4.","i":48},{"id":"cartonnage-mummy-mask-of-kheti","no":"1492","en":"Cartonnage Mummy Mask of Kheti","cn":"赫提的贴金木乃伊面具","g":"main","p":"第一中间期","d":null,"m":"亚麻布胎彩绘","dim":"高 48.6 cm · 宽 31.5 cm · 厚 27.7 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 阿西尤特","star":false,"n":1,"body":"面具上是一位戴黑色假发、留蓝色胡须的成年男子，胸前饰有多排彩珠项圈，额前束着彩色头带。它原属于第九至第十王朝时期的贵族赫提。\n然而，1903年考古人员在艾斯尤特发现相关葬具时，石棺内安放的却是一名约四至五岁孩子的骨骸，身体一部分伸入这件成人面具之中。这样的情形说明，葬具后来曾被再次使用。\n这件贴金面具因此保留了两段不同的生命痕迹：最初为赫提制作的成人形象，以及后来使用它的孩子。两者之间的具体关系，目前尚不清楚。","src":"This cartonnage mummy mask was discovered during excavations made in Asyut in Upper Egypt by Ch. Palanque under the direction of E. Chassinat in 1903. It originally belonged to a nobleman named ‘Kheti’ who lived in the Herakleopolitan Period (Dynasties 9–10). His sarcophagus was apparently re-used as it was found to conceal the bones of a child of four to five years of age, whose height may have reached 70–80 cm. The little skeleton had its head turned to the left, without any support. It was discovered in the middle of a pile of textiles, folded or simply rolled into pads, hemmed and fringed on one of the sides. The body was half inserted within this beautiful mask that features a bearded man (the beard is painted blue) wearing a black wig surrounded by a multi-coloured diadem with a central ornament. The chest is covered by a necklace containing several rows of beads of various colours.","i":49},{"id":"model-of-funerary-boat","no":"777","en":"Model of Funerary Boat","cn":"盖贝莱因随葬船模型","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"彩绘木","dim":"高 38.1 cm · 宽 15.6 cm · 长 61 cm · 重 2100 g","prov":"上埃及","star":false,"n":1,"body":"船中央的四柱棚下，一具木乃伊模型躺在狮首低床上。床头的女子作哀悼状，周围还站着其他人物；船首则坐着一位裹白色披衣的男子。整组模型呈现出随葬船上的人物安排。\n这件彩绘木船于1885年发现于盖贝莱因。船上没有桅杆和桨手，船首直立，船尾向内弯曲。两根鹰首舵柱由横梁相连，原有的两支鹰首舵只保存了一支。\n观看时，可以从船的构造转向棚内的葬床，再辨认床边的人物。比起一般的航行模型，它更着重表现送葬场景。","src":"A painted wooden model of a funerary boat discovered in Gebelein in 1885. The model has no mast and no rowers. The bow rises straight up and the stern is recurved. The two hawk-headed rudderposts are joined by a cross piece near the top, only one of the two hawk-headed rudders survived. A canopy supported by four posts shades a mummy figurine lying on a low bed with lion’s heads. At the head of the bed, is a wailing woman wearing a wig and a long skirt. Other small figurines stand around the bed. A man, whose body is wrapped in a white cloak, sits on a low-back chair at the bow of the boat.","i":50},{"id":"model-of-funerary-boat-of-ukhhotep","no":"804","en":"Model of Funerary Boat of Ukhhotep","cn":"乌赫霍特普的随葬船模型","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"彩绘木","dim":"高 40 cm · 宽 18 cm · 长 88 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 阿西尤特","star":false,"n":1,"body":"四柱棚下的石棺模型刻着乌赫霍特普的名字，棚前坐着九名身穿白色长衣的人物，彼此相向。这些细节说明，它表现的是与墓主葬仪有关的船只。\n模型于1885年出土于梅尔。船体由一整块木料制成，人物和棺具用木钉固定，舵柱则插入预留孔中，表面再施石膏和彩绘。\n船身为绿色，甲板以白色配红色横条，首尾末端绘成蓝色，船首两侧各有一只乌加特眼。观看这件展品，既可以了解随葬船的安排，也能辨认模型的拼装和上色方式。","src":"A painted wooden model of a funerary boat discovered in Meir in 1885. The two rudderposts are hawk-headed. A model of a sarcophagus inscribed with the name of Ukhhotep lies under a four-post canopy. Nine figurines, wearing long white garments, sit before the canopy facing each other. The hull is made of one piece. The sarcophagus and all figurines are fastened with pegs, while the rudderposts rest in holes. The whole boat is covered with a layer of plaster and painted. The hull is painted green, the deck is painted white with red bars, while the tips of the bow and stern are in blue. A wedjat eye is painted on each side of the bow.","i":51},{"id":"statuette-of-amenaa","no":"1257","en":"Statuette of Amenaa","cn":"阿梅纳的小雕像","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"滑石","dim":"高 22 cm · 宽 7 cm · 长 8 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 索哈杰","star":false,"n":1,"body":"阿梅纳双臂垂在身旁，戴波纹式假发，穿着从腰部垂至小腿的长裙。裙子正中央刻有一列象形文字，记录了他的姓名和称谓。\n这尊皂石小像出土于阿拜多斯，研究者依据造型风格将其断代为中王国时期。\n人物的姿态十分简洁，长裙上的竖向铭文因此格外醒目。它把雕像与一个具体的名字联系起来，也提醒我们：古埃及人物像上的文字，是理解雕像身份的重要部分。","src":"A steatite statuette of a man named Amenaa. It was discovered in Abydos and is dated on stylistic grounds to the Middle Kingdom. The statuette shows Amenaa standing, both arms hanging straight down by his side. He wears a wavy hair wig and a long kilt closed at the front from the navel to the calves. A single column of hieroglyphs, carved down the centre of his kilt, provides his name and epithet.","i":52},{"id":"model-of-a-woman-grinding-grain","no":"1350","en":"Model of a Woman Grinding Grain","cn":"磨谷女子模型","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"彩绘木","dim":"高 20 cm · 宽 11.5 cm · 长 40 cm","prov":"上埃及","star":false,"n":2,"body":"女子双膝并拢跪在底座上，脚趾抵地，上身前倾，双臂向前伸出。她正在磨谷，原本握持或推动的上层磨石如今已经不存，但身体姿势仍清楚保留了劳动的动作。\n这是一件彩绘木模型。古埃及的富裕墓葬中常放入磨谷、烘焙、酿酒等食品制作模型，希望死者在来世也能得到充足供给。\n观看时，不妨留意她重心前移的姿态。工匠用一具小小的人像，概括了磨谷这项需要反复用力的日常工作。","src":"Models of bakers, brewers and other food production activities in ancient Egypt were deposited in elite burials to cater a comfortable afterlife. This painted wooden model shows a woman grinding grain. She is kneeling on a plinth, knees closed, her toes touch the ground. Her upper body is bent and her arms reach forward to the no longer existing upper millstone.","i":53},{"id":"model-of-a-brewer","no":"1351","en":"Model of a Brewer","cn":"酿酒者模型","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":null,"m":"木、颜料","dim":"高 27.7 cm · 宽 9 cm · 长 17.6 cm","prov":"不明","star":false,"n":1,"body":"酿酒者站在大容器前，身体微微俯下，处理篮中盛放的面团状混合物。旁边还有一只封口的小罐。这件彩绘木模型把酿酒过程中的一个环节保留下来。\n古埃及人会将未完全烤熟的大麦面包掰碎后浸水，有时加入椰枣、蜂蜜或香料。混合物发酵后仍含颗粒，饮用前需要过滤。\n把这样的劳动模型放入墓中，是希望来世的食物与饮品也有人准备。它同时提供了一个直观视角，让我们看到古埃及啤酒制作与面包之间的联系。","src":"In ancient Egypt, beer was made from pieces of partially baked barley bread and was sometimes sweetened with dates, honey or spices. The bread was soaked in large containers filled with water. The mixture eventually turned into a gritty beer that was strained before drinking. This painted wooden model shows a brewer standing on a plinth, slightly bent over a large container with a basket filled with a dough. On the left side of the vessel, is a smaller sealed jar.","i":54},{"id":"statue-of-a-goddess","no":"1388","en":"Statue of a Goddess","cn":"女神像（或为伊西斯）","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":null,"m":"石灰岩","dim":"高 168.5 cm · 宽 38 cm · 长 44 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 索哈杰","star":false,"n":3,"body":"这尊石灰岩残像可能表现伊西斯女神。她戴三分式假发，佩宽项圈，身穿带有两条宽肩带的贴身长裙。\n1902年，雕像与另外三尊像的残件一同发现于阿拜多斯奥西里斯神庙。其中一尊的基座上刻有第三十王朝国王奈克塔内布二世的名字，因此这组像曾被统一归入该时期。\n不过，本件的发式与衣着又显示出更早的风格。它的身份和年代仍需结合不同证据判断，也说明同一地点发现的雕像未必都制作于同一时代。","src":"This fragmentary limestone statue possibly represents goddess Isis. She wears a tri-partite hair wig, a broad necklace and a close-fitting robe with two wide straps. The statue was discovered in 1902 among fragments of three other statues at the Temple of Osiris-Khentyimentiu at Abydos. One of the statues had the royal name of King Nectanebo II carved on its pedestal and accordingly all four figures were dated to Dynasty 30. However, the hair and clothing style of this statue suggests an earlier date.","i":55},{"id":"offering-table-of-king-amenemhat-ii","no":"1442","en":"Offering Table of King Amenemhat II","cn":"阿蒙涅姆赫特二世的供桌","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"花岗岩","dim":"高 33 cm · 宽 60 cm · 长 82.5 cm","prov":"下埃及 · 东部省","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这张花岗岩供桌的中央刻有两种符号：象征上下埃及统一的“塞玛塔维”，以及表示供奉的“赫特普”。两侧各凿出一个长方形凹槽。\n桌边环绕着供奉祷文，请求拉、盖布、奥西里斯和阿努比斯等神祇赐予阿蒙涅姆赫特二世供品。\n这件器物将盛放供奉之物的空间、祈祷文字与王权象征结合在一起。观看时，可以先辨认中央图案，再沿桌边寻找铭文，理解实物供奉与文字祈愿如何配合。","src":"This granite offering table has two rectangular basins hollowed out on either side of the sema tawy, (symbol of unified Egypt) and hetep (symbol of offering). An offering formula encircles the table, asking the deities Re, Geb, Osiris and Anubis to grant offering to King Amenemhat II.","i":56},{"id":"model-shield-of-nakhti","no":"1453","en":"Model Shield of Nakhti","cn":"纳赫提的盾牌模型","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"木、石膏底料","dim":"高 31.8 cm · 宽 20.2 cm · 厚 4.2 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 阿西尤特","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这件盾牌模型上部渐窄，顶缘呈弧形，表面绘成红棕色，并配有黑色三角图案。它于1903年与其他兵器模型一同出土于艾斯尤特的纳赫提墓。\n纳赫提是第十二王朝的重要官员，担任过国库监督和下埃及国王的掌玺官。墓中放置的兵器模型，是其随葬配置的一部分。\n古埃及实战盾牌通常以木框覆牛皮，背面设置握柄或皮带，用来抵挡矛、箭与近身攻击。这件模型虽然不是实战装备，却保留了当时盾牌的典型轮廓。","src":"Shields were long used in ancient Egypt to protect soldiers from spears and arrows and to deflect blows during hand-to-hand combat. They were commonly rectangular in shape, made by stretching cow-hide or ox-hide over a wooden frame with a handle or a leather strip to grip. This model shield was discovered in 1903 with other votive weapon models inside the tomb of a nobleman named Nakhti, located at Asyut. Nakhti served as 'Overseer of the Treasury' and 'Sealer of the King of Lower Egypt' in Dynasty 12 and his tomb was one of the largest discovered at the site. The model shield is painted reddish brown with a black triangle. Its shape is typical for the time period, tapering towards the top into a curved edge.","i":57},{"id":"model-of-a-man-ploughing-fields","no":"1505","en":"Model of A Man Ploughing Fields","cn":"农夫犁田模型","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"颜料、木","dim":"高 19.5 cm · 宽 18 cm · 长 50 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 明亚","star":false,"n":2,"body":"农夫驱赶两头牛犁地，身后另有两头戴着口套的牛卧在地上。小小的彩绘木模型，将耕作与牲畜休息的场景安排在同一个底座上。\n模型出土于代尔拜尔沙的塞皮二世、塞皮三世墓。尼罗河洪水退去后，会留下肥沃的淤泥，农人再用双牛牵引的犁翻整土壤，为播种作准备。\n中王国富裕墓葬常见这类食品生产模型，可能与人们相信死后仍将在奥西里斯的田野劳作有关。它既寄托来世生活的愿望，也记录了河谷农业中的一道工序。","src":"Models showing various stages in the production of food were included in Middle Kingdom wealthy burials possibly due to the ancient Egyptian belief that work will continue in the fields of Osiris in the afterlife. This painted wooden model was found at Deir el-Bersha in the tomb of Sepi II and Sepi III. It shows a farmer directing two oxen. Behind him are two muzzled oxen resting on the ground. Ploughing took place when the flood waters receded leaving behind a thick layer of fertile silt. A plough drawn by two cattle was used to refresh the soil and prepare it for seeding.","i":58},{"id":"two-figures-holding-cosmetic-vessels","no":"1576","en":"Two Figures Holding Cosmetic Vessels","cn":"捧化妆瓶的双人像","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"蛇纹石","dim":"高 9.7 cm · 宽 4.1 cm · 长 14.1 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"一男一女两名仆役相向跪坐，女子抱着眼妆罐，男子捧着油膏瓶。他们坐在自己的脚跟上，器物被置于身体前方，是整组小像的视觉中心。\n这件作品出土于底比斯阿萨西夫的一座第十二王朝墓葬。古埃及男女都会使用化妆品，它们也用于敬神仪式和下葬准备。\n因此，墓中的化妆器具不仅与日常梳妆有关。这组捧瓶人物把照料身体的用品带入来世，也呈现了当时人们对清洁、修饰与仪式准备的重视。","src":"Cosmetics were used by men and women of all social classes in ancient Egypt since the Predynastic Period. In addition to its practical daily functions, cosmetics were also used in temple rituals to revere the gods. Even in death, cosmetics were an essential part in the preparation for burial and it was common for Egyptians to include items like scented ointments and other cosmetics in their tombs. This charming statuette of two servants holding cosmetic vessels was discovered in a tomb dating to Dynasty 12 in Cemetery 700 at Asasif near the causeway of King Thutmose III in Thebes (Luxor). It shows a pair of servants kneeling, facing one another, on a rectangular base. The two sit back on their heels with their feet perpendicular to the ground. The female clasps a kohl pot while the male grasps an ointment vase.","i":59},{"id":"mourner-figurine-2","no":"1615","en":"Mourner Figurine","cn":"哭丧者陶俑","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 11 王朝","m":"陶","dim":"","prov":null,"star":false,"n":1,"body":"这名女子高举双臂，以强烈的肢体动作表达悲伤。造型虽然简略，哀悼的主题却十分明确。\n古埃及墓葬图像常表现送葬者举臂、哭喊、扯发、捶胸，或把尘土涂在身上。葬仪中，两位女性哀悼者还会分别扮演伊西斯与奈芙蒂斯，呼应神话中两位女神为死者哀悼的情节。\n这件陶俑保留的，正是这种具有仪式意义的悲伤姿态。它帮助我们理解，葬礼上的哀悼既有情感表达，也有约定的角色和动作。","src":"This crude figurine shows a female mourner raising her arms in grief. Mourners often appeared in tomb scenes following the funeral of the deceased with their arms raised, wailing, pulling their hair, beating their chests and smearing dirt on their bodies. Two female mourners would impersonate the goddesses Isis and Nephthys, the first mourners in Egyptian mythology and are usually depicted sitting or standing at either end of the dead body.","i":60},{"id":"seated-statue-of-neferhotep-ii","no":"1716","en":"Seated Statue of Neferhotep II","cn":"奈费尔霍特普二世坐像","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 13 王朝","m":"黑色花岗岩","dim":"高 72 cm · 宽 24 cm · 长 42 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"奈费尔霍特普二世端坐在王座上，身穿传统王室短裙，佩假胡须，双手平放在膝头，头上的王冠已经残损。王座正面两侧的铭文保存了国王的名字与头衔。\n这尊像于1904年出土于卡纳克窖藏。同处还发现了另一尊属于同名国王的王像，但这位统治者的具体身份仍有争议。\n研究者尝试将他与《都灵王表》中的相关名字对应起来。他可能在喜克索斯势力控制三角洲部分地区时，统治中、上埃及。现有线索尚不足以完全确定他的历史位置。","src":"Two royal statues of a king named Neferhotep II/Mersekhemre were discovered in 1904 by G. Legrain in the Karnak Cache (CK104, CK42). The identity of this king is still in doubt as he could be associated with Mersekhemre/Ined of the Turin Canon, who would have reigned from Memphis over Middle and Upper Egypt while the Hyksos’ Dynasty 14 or 15 controlled large parts of the Delta. In this statue, the enthroned Neferhotep II appears with a broken crown. He wears the traditional royal kilt and the false beard. His arms are resting, palms down, on his knees. The statue is void of inscriptions except for the two columns of text, carved on the two jambs of the throne, reading the king’s name and royal titulary.","i":61},{"id":"plumb-line-level","no":"3458","en":"Plumb Line Level","cn":"垂线水平仪","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"木、石","dim":"高 20.2 cm · 长 29.1 cm · 厚 2.5 cm","prov":"上埃及","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这件工具利用重力来判断表面是否水平。木架呈等腰三角形，原本从顶端悬下一根细线，下端系着铅锤；细线现已遗失。铅锤使线保持竖直，再与木架上的基准位置相比较。\n古埃及的建筑工匠和木匠会使用这类垂线水平仪，帮助校准施工或加工的表面。\n它的结构并不复杂，却能把看不见的重力方向转化为可观察的参照。类似原理至今仍用于测量和施工，体现了这种工具设计的实用性。","src":"Plumb lines levels were used by ancient Egyptian builders and carpenters to make perfectly levelled surfaces. This plumb line level had three parts: a wooden vertical isosceles triangle, a string (now missing) and a plumb bob hanging from the apex of the wooden triangle. A plumb bob is a weight that uses gravity to create a perfect vertical line. This simple but well-designed and effective tool is still used today to help builders properly align structures.","i":62},{"id":"pair-of-ivory-clappers","no":"3841","en":"Pair of Ivory Clappers","cn":"象牙响板（一对）","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"象牙","dim":"重 230 g","prov":"上埃及 · 索哈杰","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这对象牙响板采用莲花造型，既是乐器，也带有重生的象征含义。演奏时，两片相互敲击，发出节奏声。\n古埃及响板可以用木、骨、金属或象牙等材料制作，既可双手各持一片，也可将两片连接后单手操作。有些响板还雕成手臂和手掌的形状，可能源自对拍手动作的延伸。\n本件把莲花形象融入乐器。观察它的轮廓，可以看到声音、造型与象征意义如何结合在一件小器物上。","src":"This pair of clappers is made in the form of a lotus flower, a symbol of rebirth. Clappers were a type of percussion instrument, along with included hand-held drums, rattles, castanets and bells. They consisted of two pieces made of wood, bone, metal, ivory or other materials. They were held either in both hands, or fastened together and held in one hand. Some clappers were shaped like arms and hands, suggesting that they began as extensions of natural body sounds like hand clapping.","i":63},{"id":"headrest-of-mesehti","no":"9197","en":"Headrest of Mesehti","cn":"梅塞赫提的头枕","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 11 王朝","m":"木","dim":"高 20.2 cm · 宽 8.2 cm · 长 23.5 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 阿西尤特","star":false,"n":2,"body":"这件木头枕上方是弧形托面，下方由方形承板、短柱和底座支撑。它属于第十一王朝艾斯尤特地方长官梅塞赫提，出土于1893年发现的墓葬。\n头枕在日常生活中用于睡眠时支撑头部，进入墓葬后又具有帮助死者复生的含义。古埃及葬仪文字将托起头部与太阳每天从东方升起相联系。\n因此，这件造型简洁的寝具同时回应了两种需要：生前安睡，以及死后重新抬头、迎接新生的愿望。","src":"Mesehti was a provincial governor of Asyut in Upper Egypt in Dynasty 11. His tomb, discovered in 1893 in Asyut, is famous for its wooden models. This carefully modelled wooden headrest was among the objects discovered. It has a curved top with a square abacus above a short shaft and a base. Ancient Egyptian headrests were used in daily life to support the head while sleeping. They also had a funerary function as explained in the Book of the Dead, to raise and support the deceased head in resurrection just as the sun rises above the eastern horizon each morning.","i":64},{"id":"bronze-vase-of-mesehti","no":"9203","en":"Bronze vase of Mesehti","cn":"梅塞赫提的青铜注水瓶","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 11 王朝","m":"青铜","dim":"高 19.7 cm · 直径 7.8 cm · 重 248 g","prov":"上埃及 · 阿西尤特","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这只青铜瓶口沿较宽，颈部短，瓶身向下逐渐收窄，表面经过细致抛光。它没有可见的焊接痕迹，体现了古埃及金属器制作的水平。\n它出土于第十一王朝艾斯尤特地方长官梅塞赫提墓，是用于倾注液体的奠祭器具。所谓奠祭，就是在仪式中倒出液体，作为供奉。\n梅塞赫提的墓葬配置丰富。这只瓶子既反映了墓主的地位，也让我们看到葬仪并不只依赖文字和神像，还需要可以实际操作的容器。","src":"This bronze libation (ritual pouring of liquid) jar is from the tomb of Mesehti who served as a provincial governor of Asyut in Dynasty 11. As a powerful and important man, Mesehti was given a rich burial. The vase is well-polished with a relatively wide rim, short neck and a tapering body. A masterpiece of ancient Egyptian metalwork, it shows no traces of soldering.","i":65},{"id":"fluted-basin-of-mesehti","no":"9205","en":"Fluted Basin of Mesehti","cn":"梅塞赫提的凹槽铜盆","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 11 王朝","m":"青铜","dim":"高 8 cm · 重 289 g","prov":"上埃及 · 阿西尤特","star":false,"n":1,"body":"宽口沿、平底与细致的凹槽纹，是这只青铜盆的主要特点。器表经过抛光，纹饰与器形共同构成了简洁而讲究的外观。\n它来自第十一王朝艾斯尤特地方长官梅塞赫提的墓葬。与一些中王国官员一样，他选择安葬在家乡的岩凿墓中，而非自己侍奉的国王附近。\n这只盆与同墓的其他随葬用品，展现了地方精英为身后生活所作的准备，也反映了他们在本地拥有的资源与地位。","src":"A bronze fluted basin from the tomb of Mesehti, a provincial governor of Asyut in Dynasty 11. It has a wide rim, flat bottom and finely polished surface. Mesehti was an important man who, like many court officials of the Middle Kingdom, chose to be buried in a magnificent rock-cut tomb located in his hometown rather than near the king whom he served.","i":66},{"id":"silver-necklace-of-mesehti","no":"9208","en":"Silver Necklace of Mesehti","cn":"梅塞赫提的银项链","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 11 王朝","m":"银","dim":"长 14 cm · 重 34 g","prov":"上埃及 · 阿西尤特","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这条项链由十八颗银球组成，出土于第十一王朝艾斯尤特地方长官梅塞赫提墓。今天看到的珠串经过重新穿连，以展示原来的排列形式。\n它没有复杂的坠饰，主要依靠圆珠的重复与银材本身形成装饰效果。作为墓主随葬品的一部分，项链也保留了古埃及地方官员佩饰与收藏的一面。","src":"A silver necklace found in the tomb of Mesehti, a provincial governor of Asyut in Dynasty 11. The necklace is composed of eighteen silver balls that have been restrung in order to see its original form.","i":67},{"id":"sceptre-of-mesehti","no":"9216","en":"Sceptre of Mesehti","cn":"梅塞赫提的瓦斯权杖","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 11 王朝","m":"木","dim":"高 76.4 cm · 宽 4.6 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 阿西尤特","star":false,"n":2,"body":"长杖顶端为兽首，下端通常分叉，这种器物称为“瓦斯权杖”。本件以木材制成，出自第十一王朝艾斯尤特地方长官梅塞赫提的墓葬。\n瓦斯杖具有权能的象征意义，也会被放入墓中，与其他葬具共同为死者的来世生活提供保护。\n辨认它时，可以先记住兽首、细长杖身与分叉末端这几个特点。它们让一根木杖具有了超出日常用具的象征身份。","src":"A wooden was-sceptre from the collection of Mesehti, a provincial governor of Asyut in Dynasty 11. This type of sceptre has an animal head at the top of a long staff usually with a forked end. In a funerary context, it was sometimes included among other tomb equipment intended for the welfare of the deceased in the afterlife.","i":68},{"id":"stick-of-mesehti","no":"9229","en":"Stick of Mesehti","cn":"梅塞赫提的木杖","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 11 王朝","m":"木","dim":"高 87 cm · 宽 9 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 阿西尤特","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这根木杖是梅塞赫提墓中发现的七根大小不一的木杖之一。梅塞赫提是中王国时期艾斯尤特的地方长官，墓内保存了丰富的随葬用品。\n手杖既可以作为实用物品，也能象征权威。非王室成员的墓中有时会放置这类器物，可能是为了将死者与奥西里斯联系起来，或帮助他们完成前往来世的旅程。\n它的外观朴素，却说明随葬品的意义并不完全取决于贵重程度：一根熟悉的木杖，也可以承载对身后生活的期望。","src":"One of seven wooden sticks of various sizes from the tomb of Mesehti, a provincial governor of Asyut in the Middle Kingdom. Sticks were symbols of authority that were sometimes buried with non-royal individuals. This was possibly to link the deceased to the god of the dead Osiris or to aid them on their journey to the afterlife.","i":69},{"id":"ointment-vessel-of-mesehti","no":"9230","en":"Ointment Vessel of Mesehti","cn":"梅塞赫提的雪花石药膏罐","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 11 王朝","m":"雪花石膏","dim":"高 6.5 cm · 重 65 g","prov":"上埃及 · 阿西尤特","star":false,"n":2,"body":"圆润的宽口沿、光滑的罐身和平底，构成了这只油膏罐的典型形制。它用埃及雪花石制成，属于第十一王朝艾斯尤特地方长官梅塞赫提的随葬品。\n古埃及男女都会使用化妆与香膏类用品，这些物品也在宗教和葬仪中发挥作用。因此，油膏罐进入墓葬，既延续了日常身体护理的需要，也与仪式准备有关。","src":"An Egyptian alabaster vessel from the collection of Mesehti, a provincial governor of Asyut in Dynasty 11. It has a wide rounded rim, smooth body and a flat base, the typical form for ointment jars in ancient Egypt. Cosmetic and perfume ointments were used by men and women in ancient Egyptian. These ointments also had important roles in religious and funerary rites.","i":70},{"id":"mirror-of-mesehti","no":"9276","en":"Mirror of Mesehti","cn":"梅塞赫提的铜镜","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 11 王朝","m":"木、青铜","dim":"高 2 cm · 宽 15.5 cm · 长 27 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 阿西尤特","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这面镜子由青铜圆盘和木柄两部分组成。圆盘原本经过抛光，用金属表面反射人像；木柄两侧则各饰一只乌加特眼。\n它出土于第十一王朝地方长官梅塞赫提墓。古埃及男女墓葬中都能见到镜子，常与梳子、眼妆用品和油膏容器放在一起。\n与现代玻璃镜相比，它最值得留意的是镜面的材料：经过精细处理的金属，同样可以满足整理仪容的需要。木柄上的眼睛图案，则为梳妆器具加入了守护意味。","src":"A bronze mirror from the collection of Mesehti, a provincial governor of Asyut in Dynasty 11. It consists of two parts - a bronze disc that would have been polished to create a reflective surface and a wooden handle with a wedjat eye on either side. Mirrors were found in burials of both men and women usually in close association with burial goods like combs, cosmetics like kohl and ointment containers.","i":71},{"id":"model-hes-vase-of-mesehti","no":"9277","en":"Model Hes-Vase of Mesehti","cn":"梅塞赫提的木制赫斯瓶模型","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 11 王朝","m":"木","dim":"高 6.2 cm · 直径 1.6 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 阿西尤特","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这是一只赫斯瓶的木制模型，来自第十一王朝艾斯尤特地方长官梅塞赫提墓。真正的赫斯瓶用于在宗教或葬仪中倾注液体。\n中王国墓葬常放置这类器物模型，希望死者在来世仍具备生活与仪式所需的用品。\n本件的意义正在于“模型”二字：它不必承担真实容器的全部功能，仍可凭借可辨认的形制，在随葬体系中代表相应器物。","src":"A wooden model hes-vase from the burial of Mesehti, a provincial governor of Asyut in Dynasty 11. This type of vase was used to pour liquids for ceremonies and funerary rituals. Placing wooden models in tombs was part of burial practices during the Middle Kingdom that ensured the dead had all the proper supplies for their afterlife.","i":72},{"id":"statuette-of-mesehti","no":"9280","en":"Statuette of Mesehti","cn":"梅塞赫提石雕坐像","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 11 王朝","m":"雪花石膏（埃及雪花石）","dim":"高 22.4 cm · 宽 9.2 cm · 长 16 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 阿西尤特","star":false,"n":1,"body":"梅塞赫提坐在低背椅上，双臂放在膝部。这尊小像用埃及雪花石制成，出自他在艾斯尤特的墓葬。\n梅塞赫提是第十一王朝的地方长官。当时的艾斯尤特是重要商贸中心，地方统治者在那里修建了大型岩凿墓。\n他的墓于1893年被发现，以丰富的随葬品闻名，其中包括木模型和两具大型木棺。与那些表现生活、劳动和仪式的器物相比，这尊坐像直接留下了墓主本人的形象。","src":"A travertine (Egyptian alabaster) statuette from the tomb of Mesehti, a provincial governor of Asyut in Dynasty 11. It shows Mesehti seated on a low-back chair, resting his arms on his knees. Asyut was a prominent commercial centre in the Middle Kingdom where huge rock cut tombs of the town governors were built. Mesehti’s tomb was discovered in 1893 and is most famous for its funerary equipment that included, in addition to this statuette, wooden models and two large wooden coffins.","i":73},{"id":"stela-of-senetites","no":"14101","en":"Stela of Senetites","cn":"塞内提特斯石碑","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"彩绘石灰岩","dim":"高 65.2 cm · 宽 32.5 cm · 厚 11.5 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 索哈杰","star":false,"n":1,"body":"塞内提特斯坐在狮腿椅上，右手持莲花，左手伸向摆满供品的桌子。椅子下方还有一名少女，右手拿镜子，左臂挂着袋子，为供奉场景增添了生活细节。\n这块彩绘石灰岩碑来自阿拜多斯。碑面由圆凸边框围合，上方配有埃及式凹曲檐口，顶部文字为碑主来世的安宁与供给祈愿。\n观看时，可以把上方祷文与下方供桌联系起来：文字提出愿望，图像则将得到供养的情景具体呈现出来。","src":"A painted rectangular limestone stela from Abydos. The stela is framed by a torus moulding surmounted by the Egyptian cavetto cornice. In the top register is an offering prayer for the welfare of Senetites in the afterlife. Below, she is seated on a lion-legged chair, holding a lotus flower in her right hand. Her left hand stretches out to a table laden with a variety of offerings. Under her chair is a young girl holding a mirror in her right hand and a bag hangs from her left arm.","i":74},{"id":"statue-of-a-woman","no":"14506","en":"Statue of a Woman","cn":"女子雕像","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":null,"m":"石灰岩","dim":"高 24 cm · 宽 12.2 cm · 长 16.1 cm","prov":"不明","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这尊女子小像戴着蓬松、末端卷曲的假发。研究者依据这一发式，将它归入中王国时期，并推测人物可能具有王室身份。类似造型与哈托尔女神有关，也见于塞努塞尔特二世王后诺芙蕾特二世的雕像。\n更特别的是肩部残留的羽毛纹。它提示雕像原来的身体可能呈鸟形，而不只是普通的女性人像。\n由于作品保存不完整，身份与原貌都仍需谨慎判断。发式和羽纹，正是现存部分中最有价值的两条线索。","src":"This small statue is probably of a royal woman. It can be dated by its hairstyle to the Middle Kingdom. The woman is wearing a bouffant style hair wig that ends in large curls. This hairstyle was associated with goddess Hathor and is reminiscent of two statues of Queen Nofret II, wife of King Senwosret II of Dynasty 12. Traces of a feather pattern covering the shoulders of the statue suggest its body may have been that of a bird.","i":75},{"id":"mummy-mask-of-mesehti","no":"39209","en":"Mummy Mask of Mesehti","cn":"梅塞赫提的木乃伊面具","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 11 王朝","m":"亚麻布胎彩绘","dim":"高 31.2 cm · 宽 42 cm · 长 84 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 阿西尤特","star":false,"n":3,"body":"大而清晰的双眼、小胡须与浓黑的下巴胡须，构成了梅塞赫提面具鲜明的面容。假发外束着莲花头带，胸前饰有彩色宽项圈。\n面具由卡通纳吉制成，也就是将织物与石膏等材料层层塑形的葬仪材料。它属于第十一王朝后期的艾斯尤特地方长官梅塞赫提，出土于1893年发现的墓葬。\n古埃及葬仪面具用于保护死者头部，并为其保留完整的面貌。本件的五官、发式和颈饰，正服务于这一目的。","src":"Funerary masks were used in ancient Egypt to protect the head of the deceased and to ensure that their features were perfectly portrayed. This cartonnage mummy mask belongs to Mesehti who served as a provincial governor of Asyut during the later stages of Dynasty 11. His tomb was discovered in 1893 at Asyut in Upper Egypt. This coloured cartonnage mask shows him with an oval face, large outlined eyes, a moustache and a thick painted black beard. He wears a hair wig with a lotus fillet (headband) tied around the crown of the head and a multi-coloured broad collar adorns his chest.","i":76},{"id":"mourner-figurine","no":"57338","en":"Mourner Figurine","cn":"哀悼者陶俑（一）","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 11 王朝","m":"陶","dim":"高 18 cm · 长 10 cm","prov":"不明","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这件陶俑用高举的双臂表现女子的哀恸。细节刻画较为简略，但姿态鲜明，能够让人直接辨认出哀悼的主题。\n在古埃及葬仪中，哭喊、扯发、捶胸和举臂都是表达悲伤的动作。两名女性哀悼者还会扮演伊西斯与奈芙蒂斯，通常分处死者身体两端。\n从这一背景看，陶俑表现的既是悲伤中的人物，也是葬仪中一个有明确角色和动作的参与者。","src":"This crude figurine shows a female mourner raising her arms in grief. Mourners often appeared in tomb scenes following the funeral of the deceased with their arms raised, wailing, pulling their hair, beating their chests and smearing dirt on their bodies. Two female mourners would impersonate the goddesses Isis and Nephthys, the first mourners in Egyptian mythology and are usually depicted sitting or standing at either end of the dead body.","i":77},{"id":"mourner-figurine-1","no":"57339","en":"Mourner Figurine","cn":"哀悼者陶俑（二）","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 11 王朝","m":null,"dim":"高 19 cm · 宽 7 cm · 长 10 cm","prov":"不明","star":false,"n":1,"body":"女子将双臂高高举起，以身体动作传达悲伤。古埃及墓葬图像中常见相似姿态，送葬者也会哭喊、扯发、捶胸或将尘土涂在身上。\n其中，两位女性哀悼者会分别扮演伊西斯与奈芙蒂斯，呼应神话中的哀悼情节，并出现在死者身体两端。\n这件造型简略的陶俑，把葬礼上的一个典型动作保留下来。理解这种动作所属的仪式，比单看人物表情，更有助于读懂作品。","src":"This crude figurine shows a female mourner raising her arms in grief. Mourners often appeared in tomb scenes following the funeral of the deceased with their arms raised, wailing, pulling their hair, beating their chests and smearing dirt on their bodies. Two female mourners would impersonate the goddesses Isis and Nephthys, the first mourners in Egyptian mythology and are usually depicted sitting or standing at either end of the dead body.","i":78},{"id":"small-gold-pendant-treasure-of-tod","no":"65738","en":"Small Gold Pendant (Treasure of Tod)","cn":"托德宝藏·小金花坠饰","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"金","dim":"高 2.8 cm · 宽 0.2 cm · 长 1.1 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这枚金花坠饰以细金条悬挂，体量虽小，花形的处理却细致精巧。它于1936年与其他器物一同被发现，属于托德宝藏。\n在这件作品上，装饰效果主要来自花朵轮廓与纤细悬带的配合。它为这批包含金银器、宝石和印章的宝藏，增添了一件小巧的首饰。","src":"A small gold pendant in the form of a flower suspended on a thin strip of gold. It was discovered in 1936 among other artefacts of the Tod Treasure. This precious piece is a delicate and exquisite display of wealth.","i":79},{"id":"cylinder-seal-treasure-of-tod","no":"65747","en":"Cylinder Seal (Treasure of Tod)","cn":"托德宝藏·青金石圆筒印章","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"青金石","dim":"高 0.3 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"把这枚圆筒印章放在湿软的泥面上滚动，就能留下连续的图案，用来标示归属或确认文书。筒身有穿孔，便于系绳携带。\n印章以青金石雕成，1936年出土于托德宝藏。图案分为两层：下层是条纹，上层排列着三只有羚羊般长角的四足动物，带有美索不达米亚风格。\n它将实用的印记功能与精细雕刻结合在一起。材料和图案也说明，这批宝藏中的一些物品与埃及之外的地区存在联系。","src":"A cylindrical seal carved of lapis lazuli with Mesopotamian motifs. It was discovered in 1936 among other artefacts as part of the Tod Treasure. The seal was pierced so that it could be hung on a string and when needed rolled on soft clay to indicate ownership or authenticate a document. It is decorated with two incised registers: a striated lower register and an upper register showing three quadrupeds with antelope-like horns in motion.","i":80},{"id":"small-cylinder-seal-treasure-of-tod","no":"65751","en":"Small Cylinder Seal (Treasure of Tod)","cn":"托德宝藏·小圆筒印章","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"青金石","dim":"高 1.6 cm · 直径 1 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":2,"body":"这枚青金石圆筒印章上，重复排列着具有美索不达米亚风格的四足动物。它于1936年出土于托德蒙图神庙地下，是托德宝藏的一部分。\n青金石不是埃及本地常见的原料，最近的重要产地远在今天的阿富汗一带。宝藏中大量使用这种石材，反映了埃及与古代近东之间的物资往来。\n小小的印章因此包含两种线索：动物纹样指向外来艺术传统，宝石本身则提示了跨越遥远地区的贸易联系。","src":"This cylinder seal was discovered in 1936 under the Temple of Montu at Tod among other artefacts that became known as the ‘Tod Treasure’. The seal is carved out of lapis lazuli and is decorated with repeated quadrupeds of Mesopotamian style. With the nearest source for lapis lazuli being in Afghanistan, the extensive use of this gemstone in many of the artefacts in the Treasure of Tod is a clear evidence of Egypt's trade with the ancient Near East.","i":81},{"id":"amulet-treasure-of-tod","no":"65775","en":"Amulet (Treasure of Tod)","cn":"托德宝藏·卧牛青金石护身符","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"青金石","dim":"高 2.1 cm · 宽 1.1 cm · 长 2.9 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这枚护身符被雕成卧伏的牛形动物，可能是一头有角公牛。石上留有穿孔，可以系绳佩戴。\n它以青金石制成，1936年随托德宝藏一同出土。青金石的原料需要通过远距离贸易进入埃及，最近的重要来源在今天的阿富汗一带。\n一枚体量很小的佩饰，也能反映古代贸易的广度：珍贵石材经过运输和加工，最终成为人们可以随身携带的护身之物。","src":"A lapis lazuli amulet discovered in 1936 among other artefacts in the Tod Treasure. The amulet is in the form of a recumbent bovid (perhaps a bull with horns). The stone was pierced so that it could be strung and worn. The reach of Egypt’s far-flung trade network is evident as the nearest source for lapis lazuli was in Afghanistan.","i":82},{"id":"pendant-treasure-of-tod","no":"65778","en":"Pendant (Tod Treasure)","cn":"托德宝藏·荷鲁斯童子坠饰","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"青金石","dim":"高 4.4 cm · 宽 1.6 cm · 长 1.7 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这枚青金石坠饰表现的是孩童形态的荷鲁斯，石上有可供穿绳的小孔。它于1936年发现于托德宝藏。\n人物属于埃及神祇，材料却需要从国外输入。这件作品究竟是在埃及用进口原料雕成，还是在国外制作后运来，目前仍不清楚。\n它提醒我们，器物的原料来源、制作地点与图像传统，可以分别属于不同地区。判断一件古物的来历，往往需要把这些线索逐一分辨。","src":"This lapis lazuli pendant was discovered in 1936 among other artefacts in the Treasure of Tod. It is carved in the shape of god Horus the Child and is pierced so that it could be strung. It is not clear whether this figurine of an Egyptian god was made abroad or in Egypt using imported raw material (lapis lazuli).","i":83},{"id":"cylindrical-container-with-handle-treasure-of-tod","no":"65788","en":"Cylindrical Container with Handle (Treasure of Tod)","cn":"托德宝藏·带柄银质圆筒器","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"银、琥珀金","dim":"高 23 cm · 长 10 cm · 直径 4.9 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这只圆筒形容器用银和金银合金制成，外壁环绕两道金银合金丝带，提柄则以银钉固定。提柄可能方便穿入肩带，让容器可以随身携带。\n它于1936年与其他托德宝藏器物一同出土。宝藏中许多物品可能来自埃及以外的地区，反映出广泛的国际交流。\n这件器物值得仔细观察的是连接方式：环带如何围住筒身、提柄如何固定，都比笼统地欣赏贵金属材质，更能体现制作上的巧思。","src":"A cylindrical container made of silver and electrum discovered in 1936 among other artefacts of the Tod Treasure. The case is encircled by two bands of electrum wires and the elegant handle is riveted with silver nails. The handle may have allowed the case to be suspended by a strap to the shoulder. Many of the objects in the Treasure of Tod were probably imported from various parts of the ancient world, reflecting ancient Egypt’s wide international trade network.","i":84},{"id":"small-bowl-treasure-of-tod-2-1","no":"65789","en":"Small Bowl (Treasure of Tod)","cn":"托德宝藏·小金碗","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"金","dim":"高 2.5 cm · 直径 10.1 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这只小金碗由很薄的金片制成。碗底以三个圆圈为中心，向外延伸出弯曲的纹带，图案通过从金属背面锤击的“锤揲”工艺形成。\n它于1936年出土于托德宝藏。碗的形状与风格可与伊拉克南部乌尔苏美尔墓葬中的器物比较，显示出埃及以外的艺术联系。\n托德宝藏中不少碗器都带有古代近东或地中海地区的特征。这只小碗既是一件精细金工，也为研究不同地区之间的器物交流提供了材料。","src":"This small gold bowl was discovered in 1936 among other artefacts of the Tod Treasure. It is made of a very thin sheet of gold. The base has three circles and curving bands emanate from this central motif, all made by repoussé (shaping metal by hammering from the reverse side). The shape and style of many bowls in the Tod Treasure are not Egyptian in origin but come from the ancient Near East and Mediterranean. The bowl is similar in shape and style to the grave goods found in the Sumerian Tombs of Ur in southern Iraq.","i":85},{"id":"small-bowl-with-handles-treasure-of-tod","no":"65790","en":"Small Bowl with Handles (Treasure of Tod)","cn":"托德宝藏·带双耳银碗","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"银","dim":"高 6.2 cm · 宽 11.3 cm · 长 12.5 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"两只把手分置碗身两侧，表面以螺旋纹装饰。这些起伏纹样由工匠从银片背面锤击而成，属于锤揲工艺。\n银碗于1936年出土于托德宝藏。它的装饰风格与传统埃及器物有所不同，因此被认为可能来自国外，经贸易网络进入埃及。\n与同批常见的竖棱纹银碗相比，本件最醒目的特点就是旋转展开的螺旋纹。把两者对照，可以看到宝藏内部并不只有一种装饰传统。","src":"A silver bowl with two handles discovered in 1936 among other artefacts in the Tod Treasure. The bowl is decorated with spirals made by repoussé (shaping of metal by hammering from the reverse side). The decoration is of a non-Egyptian style suggesting a foreign origin for the vessel that was probably brought to Egypt via its extensive trade network.","i":86},{"id":"small-bowl-treasure-of-tod-4","no":"65791","en":"Small Bowl (Treasure of Tod)","cn":"托德宝藏·竖棱纹银碗","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"银","dim":"高 4.0 cm · 直径 11.2 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"银碗外壁排列着宽厚的竖向凸棱，纹带略有收窄，由工匠从金属背面锤击成形。规则的起伏，使碗身的轮廓更富变化。\n它于1936年出土于托德蒙图神庙地下。整批宝藏装在四只铜合金箱中，藏于神庙基础的沙层内。\n其中两只箱子刻有阿蒙涅姆赫特二世的名字。这批器物可能由他奉献，以纪念修建神庙的父亲塞努塞尔特一世。银碗的出土位置与箱上铭文，共同提供了理解奉献背景的线索。","src":"A silver bowl decorated with a series of thick vertical gadroons (slightly tapered bands). This decorative motif was made by hammering metal from the reverse side, also known as repoussé technique. It was discovered in 1936 among other artefacts deposited in four copper-alloy chests hidden in the foundation sand under the temple dedicated by King Senwosret I for god Montu at Tod. Two of the chests bore the name of King Amenemhat II who possibly deposited them in memory of his father Senwosret I.","i":87},{"id":"a-string-with-carnelian-beads-treasure-of-tod","no":"65821","en":"A String with Carnelian Beads (Treasure of Tod)","cn":"托德宝藏·红玉髓串珠","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"红玉髓","dim":"长 15.7 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这串珠饰由五十八颗形状不规则的红玉髓珠组成。它们可能大多来自美索不达米亚，但具体来源仍需结合其他证据判断。\n1936年，这些珠子与其他器物一起，在托德蒙图神庙基础中的四只铜合金箱内被发现，成为托德宝藏的一部分。\n与金银容器相比，珠饰呈现了宝藏中另一类珍贵材料。不同形状的珠子被集中保存，也让我们看到这一仪式埋藏所汇集的物品相当多样。","src":"A string of fifty-eight irregularly shaped beads of carnelian (a semi-precious gemstone). These beads may mostly have come from Mesopotamia. They were deposited, along with other artefacts, inside four copper-alloy caskets discovered in 1936 in the foundations underlying the Temple of the god Montu at Tod.","i":88},{"id":"collar-necklace-treasure-of-tod","no":"65823","en":"Collar Necklace (Treasure of Tod)","cn":"托德宝藏·青金石项圈（大）","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"青金石","dim":"高 1 cm · 宽 2 cm · 长 27.5 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这件项圈以大颗楔形青金石珠为主体，再用两排圆珠将它们连接起来。楔形珠上钻有两至三个孔，使多排珠串能够保持整体的排列。\n这些大珠的样式与古埃及常见的“苍蝇形坠饰”相近。青金石深邃的蓝色，则是整件首饰最鲜明的视觉特点。\n项圈出自托德宝藏。制作所需的青金石通过远距离贸易进入埃及，可能来自阿富汗。观看时，可以同时留意珠形与穿孔结构，理解它如何由一颗颗石珠组成宽阔的颈饰。","src":"Valued for its gorgeous colour, lapis lazuli was brought to Egypt (possibly from Afghanistan) through its extensive trade networks. This lapis lazuli necklace from the Tod Treasure is a statement piece. It is composed of wedge-shaped beads in the style of the famous ‘Fly Pendants’ known in ancient Egypt from Predynastic times through the late New Kingdom. The large wedge-shaped beads are pierced by two or three holes and are joined by two rows of round beads to create a collar.","i":89},{"id":"collar-necklace-treasure-of-tod-duplicate","no":"65824","en":"Collar Necklace (Treasure of Tod)","cn":"托德宝藏·青金石项圈（小）","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"青金石","dim":"长 15.7 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"楔形青金石珠与两排圆珠相连，组成这件托德宝藏项圈。每颗楔形珠钻有两至三个孔，既便于穿连，也帮助维持项圈的排列。\n青金石在古埃及不仅因蓝色而受珍视，还具有宗教含义。它的颜色被联想到黎明前的天空、原初之水，以及神祇的头发。\n这件首饰因此可以从两方面欣赏：一是珠形与串接的设计，二是蓝色石材在当时观念中的象征意义。","src":"This lapis lazuli necklace from Tod Treasure is composed of wedge-shaped beads that are pierced by two or three holes and joined by two rows of round beads to create a collar. Lapis lazuli held a special religious significance in ancient Egypt, as it is the colour of the sky before dawn, the colour of the primordial ocean and the hair of the gods.","i":90},{"id":"necklace-treasure-of-tod-1","no":"65827","en":"Necklace (Treasure of Tod)","cn":"托德宝藏·青金石项链（双锥珠）","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":null,"m":"青金石","dim":"长 56 cm","prov":"上埃及","star":false,"n":1,"body":"项链中央是一颗较大的菱形珠，两侧珠子逐渐缩小，双锥形、菱形与桶形珠交替排列。不同珠形与大小变化，让单排珠串具有清楚的节奏。\n这条青金石项链于1936年随托德宝藏一同出土，属于重要的仪式埋藏。\n它的装饰效果主要来自石珠本身。沿着项链从中央向两端看，可以辨认工匠如何利用形状和尺寸的变化，组织整条首饰。","src":"This lapis lazuli necklace is from the important ritual deposit known as the Tod Treasure discovered in 1936. It is composed of bicone-shaped, lozenge-shaped and barrel-shaped beads strung on a single strand. The beads tapper down in size as they move away from the central large lozenge-shaped bead.","i":91},{"id":"necklace-treasure-of-tod","no":"65830","en":"Necklace (Treasure of Tod)","cn":"托德宝藏·青金石项链（桶形珠）","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"青金石","dim":"长 67 cm","prov":"上埃及","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这条项链由桶形珠与近球形珠穿成单排，整体以青金石的蓝色形成统一效果。两种珠形相互搭配，使结构简洁的珠串仍有细微变化。\n它属于1936年发现的托德宝藏。青金石因色彩鲜明而受到古埃及人的喜爱，也是这批宝藏中反复出现的材料。\n与同批楔形珠项圈相比，本件采用较为简洁的单排设计，可以从中看到相同石材在不同首饰结构中的运用。","src":"Valued for its gorgeous blue colour, lapis lazuli was a favoured gemstone in ancient Egypt. This lapis lazuli necklace is from the important ritual deposit known as the Tod Treasure discovered in 1936. It is composed of barrel-shaped and spheroid-shaped beads strung on a single strand.","i":92},{"id":"small-bowl-treasure-of-tod-1-1","no":"65839","en":"Small Bowl (Treasure of Tod)","cn":"托德宝藏·银碗（直棱纹）","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"银","dim":"高 5.7 cm · 直径 12.5 cm","prov":"上埃及","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这只小银碗饰有竖向棱纹，纹饰以锤揲工艺制成，即从金属背面锤击，使正面形成起伏。\n在古埃及观念中，银与白色、光亮相联系，也在宗教仪式中发挥作用。对托德宝藏中部分银器的分析显示，其银材纯度较高，而且很可能由国外输入。\n本件既展示了金属塑形工艺，也将人们的视线引向原料来源。碗身上的规则纹饰与银材的跨地区流动，是理解它的两个角度。","src":"A small silver bowl with vertical band decoration (gadroon) made by hammering the metal from the reverse side (repoussé). Silver was associated with ‘white’ and ‘light’ in ancient Egypt and played an important role in religious rituals. Recent analysis of various silver artefacts found as part of the Tod Treasure reveal that the silver was relatively pure and almost certainly imported to Egypt.","i":93},{"id":"small-bowl-treasure-of-tod","no":"65840","en":"Small Bowl (Treasure of Tod)","cn":"托德宝藏·银碗（折痕尚存）","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"银","dim":"高 4.7 cm · 直径 12.5 cm","prov":"上埃及","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这只银碗虽然已经恢复原形，表面仍能看到折叠留下的痕迹。出土时，包括它在内的多件托德宝藏银器都曾被压平、折叠，可能是为了在小型铜箱中容纳更多物品。\n修复后，碗身竖向凸棱与口沿处圆润的收束重新显现。纹饰由从银片背面锤击的方式制作。\n折痕并非无关紧要的损伤：它们记录了器物被埋藏前的处理方式，也让人能够区分最初制作、入藏折叠与现代修复这几个不同阶段。","src":"A silver bowl with repoussé decoration consisting of vertical gadroons rounded at the rim. It was discovered in 1936 among other artefacts of the Treasure of Tod. Many of the silver vessels of the Tod Treasure, including this small bowl, were found flattened and folded. It is possible that this was done to fit as many pieces as possible into the small copper chests used to hold the ritual deposit. Expert conservators have restored the bowl to its original shape but traces of the folds can still be seen.","i":94},{"id":"small-bowl-treasure-of-tod-1","no":"65841","en":"Small Bowl (Treasure of Tod)","cn":"托德宝藏·银碗（小号）","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"银","dim":"高 4.3 cm · 直径 7.7 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"圆润的口沿下，竖向纹带沿碗身排列，构成这只小银碗的主要装饰。它于1936年随托德宝藏一同出土。\n托德宝藏中的进口材料与珍贵制品，反映了当时埃及活跃的对外交流。像这类银器，也被用于呈现国王将外来财富带入埃及、再奉献给神的角色。\n把它放回整批神庙埋藏中理解，便能看到一件小器皿如何同时涉及贸易、王权与宗教供奉。","src":"A silver bowl discovered in 1936 as part of the Treasure of Tod. It is decorated with vertical bands and a rounded rim. Imported raw materials and precious products like this silver are evidence of an intensely active and expansive trade network during this period. The Tod Treasure also highlights the role of the king in Egypt as the one who brings wealth to Egypt from abroad.","i":95},{"id":"small-bowl-treasure-of-tod-2","no":"65849","en":"Small Bowl (Treasure of Tod)","cn":"托德宝藏·银碗（圈足双环）","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"银","dim":"高 4.5 cm · 直径 11.2 cm · 重 55.18 g","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"银碗以竖向纹带装饰，底部另有双圈图案。它属于托德宝藏，原与其他器物一起装入四只铜箱，埋在塞努塞尔特一世修建的神庙地面下。\n其中两只箱子刻有阿蒙涅姆赫特二世的名字，因此这批供奉可能由他安排，用来敬奉蒙图神，并纪念父亲塞努塞尔特一世。\n本件外观并不复杂，出土环境却十分关键。它说明研究古物时，盛放它的箱子、箱上的铭文与发现地点，同样能够提供重要信息。","src":"A silver bowl decorated with vertical bands and a double circle at the base. The Tod Treasure was found under the floor of the temple built by King Senwosret I inside four copper boxes, two of which were incised with the name of the King Amenemhat II. It is possible that King Amenemhat II made this offering to honour his father King Senwosret I as well as the god Montu.","i":96},{"id":"small-two-handled-bowl-treasure-of-tod","no":"65861","en":"Small Two-Handled Bowl (Treasure of Tod)","cn":"托德宝藏·双耳银碗","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"银","dim":"高 5 cm · 宽 10.5 cm · 长 12 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"两侧把手与斜向棱纹，使这只银碗有别于同批竖纹器物。纹带在口沿处圆润收束，起伏由工匠从金属背面锤击而成。\n这件薄壁器物出土时曾被压平、折叠，后来经过修复，才恢复成今天的形状。它于1936年发现于托德神庙地面下，与其他带有异地特色的器物一同埋藏。\n观看时，可以先辨认斜纹的走向，再观察把手与碗身的关系，体会同类银器在细部设计上的变化。","src":"A silver bowl with two handles, decorated with slanted band decoration (gadroon) rounded at the rim. The decoration was made using repoussé technique (the shaping of metal by hammering the reverse side of the piece). The thin-walled vessel was found folded and flatted but has been restored to its original shape. It was discovered in 1936 among other exotic artefacts under the temple floor at Tod.","i":97},{"id":"small-bowl-treasure-of-tod-3","no":"65868","en":"Small Bowl (Tod Treasure)","cn":"托德宝藏·银碗（高身）","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"银","dim":"高 6.8 cm · 长 12 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"碗身上的竖向凸棱，由背面锤击银片形成。这种锤揲纹饰在托德宝藏的多件银器上都能见到。\n这件作品值得关注的，还有原料与风格之间的关系。对相关银材的科学分析提示其可能来自今天土耳其的安纳托利亚地区，而器形与装饰又可与爱琴海的米诺斯、迈锡尼文化比较。\n原料来自哪里，与器物采用哪种艺术风格，并不一定是同一个问题。将两类线索结合，才能更完整地理解它在古代交流网络中的位置。","src":"Various styles of silver vessels including cups and bowls were found as part of the Tod Treasure. Many of the vessels like this silver bowl were decorated with vertical bands (gadroons) created using repoussé technique. Though scientific analysis of the silver suggests the metal comes from Anatolia in Turkey, the style resembles Minoan and Mycenaean cultures in ancient Greece.","i":98},{"id":"small-two-handled-cup-treasure-of-tod","no":"65898","en":"Small Two-Handled Cup (Treasure of Tod)","cn":"托德宝藏·双耳银杯","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"银","dim":"高 6.8 cm · 长 12 cm · 直径 7.2 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这只银杯表面没有纹饰，两只高把手从杯身两侧伸起。纤薄的杯壁与细长把手，使整体造型显得轻巧。\n它出自托德宝藏。由于器壁很薄，研究者认为它可能并非用于普通的日常饮用。对同批部分银器的分析还显示，银材纯度较高，而且很可能来自埃及之外。\n与装饰繁密的银碗相比，本件主要依靠器形取胜。高把手、薄杯壁与光素表面，构成了它最鲜明的特点。","src":"An undecorated silver bowl with two high handles, found among the artefacts of the Tod Treasure. The cup has thin walls suggesting it was not used for practical purposes. Recent analysis of various silver artefacts found as part of the Tod Treasure reveal that silver was relatively pure and almost certainly imported to Egypt.","i":99},{"id":"small-cup-treasure-of-tod","no":"65899","en":"Small Cup (Tod Treasure)","cn":"托德宝藏·单柄银杯","g":"main","p":"中王国时期","d":"第 12 王朝","m":"银","dim":"高 7.2 cm · 宽 8.7 cm · 长 11 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这只银杯表面光素，细巧的把手用铆钉固定在杯身上：上端两钉，下端一钉。这样的连接细节，是观察本件金工工艺的好线索。\n银杯曾被压平、折叠，以便放入保存托德宝藏的铜箱。它的器形在埃及较为少见，却可与安纳托利亚和迈锡尼地区的同类器物比较。\n从把手结构到外来器形，再到入箱时的折叠处理，这件杯子保留了制作、流通与埋藏的不同信息。","src":"This silver cup was folded and flattened to fit into the copper chests that held the Tod Treasure. The cup is undecorated with a delicate handle riveted to the body (one nail at the bottom and two nails at the top). The shape of the cup is foreign to Egypt but similar in type to those from Anatolia (Turkey) and Mycenae (Greece).","i":100},{"id":"ceremonial-axe-head","no":"1460","en":"Ceremonial Axe Head","cn":"礼仪用战斧斧头","g":"main","p":"第二中间期","d":null,"m":"铜","dim":"宽 9.3 cm · 长 10.3 cm · 重 162 g","prov":"下埃及 · 科姆埃尔希森","star":false,"n":2,"body":"斧头中央的镂空图案是一只格里芬：鹰首、狮身，并生有双翼。这种神话动物在这里象征埃及对外敌的压制。\n古埃及实战斧的刃部多为半圆或新月形，用绳索绑在木柄上，用于近身搏斗。礼仪斧虽然借用了相近外形，却常带有精美镂空，无法承担真正的作战任务。\n这类斧可能由士兵在重要国家仪式的列队活动中携带。本件的重点，因此在于图像和象征意义，而非杀伤能力。","src":"Ancient Egyptian soldiers used battle axes in hand-to-hand combat to inflict deep wounds on their enemies. The blades of battle axes were most commonly semi-circular or crescent-shaped and tied to a wooden handle with cords. Ceremonial axe heads, though similar in form, had beautiful openwork designs that made them unusable in combat. These axes were perhaps carried by soldiers on parade during important state ceremonies. This ceremonial axe head has openwork showing a griffin, a mythical falcon-headed lion with wings that symbolised Egypt’s domination over foreign enemies.","i":101},{"id":"mother-and-child","no":"1644","en":"Mother and Child","cn":"母子陶像","g":"main","p":"第二中间期","d":null,"m":"陶","dim":"高 10.3 cm · 宽 2.6 cm · 长 3.4 cm","prov":"东部沙漠 · 泽特山","star":false,"n":1,"body":"女子背着一个孩子，姿态简洁，主题鲜明。这件陶像原本是一件献给哈托尔女神的祈愿供品。\n母亲背负孩子的日常形象，被制作成陶像并献入宗教场所，使生活中的亲子关系也成为人们向神表达心愿的一种方式。","src":"This figure of a woman carrying a child on her back was dedicated as a votive offering to the goddess Hathor.","i":102},{"id":"colossal-head-of-ramesses-ii","no":"2191","en":"Colossal Head of Ramesses II","cn":"拉美西斯二世巨像头部","g":"main","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 19 王朝","m":"红色花岗岩","dim":"高 116 cm · 宽 53 cm · 长 60 cm","prov":"下埃及 · 东部省","star":false,"n":1,"body":"拉美西斯二世年轻的面容被浓密卷发包围，额前饰有圣蛇，冠饰结合了双角、双羽与日轮等元素。头像在下巴处断裂，却仍保存了丰富的头部细节。\n它于1888年出土于尼罗河三角洲东部布巴斯提斯的芭丝特大神庙。结合当地发现的其他残像，研究者认为它原属于一尊持神标的国王巨像。\n神标上端仍保留一位男神的头部，可能是普塔—索卡尔—奥西里斯。观看时，可以把繁复冠饰与残存神标分别辨认，想象这尊王像原来更完整的构成。","src":"This colossal statue head of King Ramesses II was discovered in 1888 at the great temple of goddess Bastet at Bubastis (Tell-Basta) in the eastern Delta. Based on its similarity to other fragmentary statues discovered at the same spot, this royal head is part of a colossal of the king as a standard bearer. Ramesses II wears a diadem encircled by uraeus snakes topped with a crown composed of two outstretched horns, two tall feathers, a sun disk and two uraeus snakes. His youthful face is framed by a thick curled wig that sits low on his forehead, hiding his ears. The wig is encircled by a fillet fronted by a coiled uraeus snake. The king’s head is broken off at the level of the chin. Only the upper part of a standard that was once held by the king remains, showing the head of a male deity, most likely Ptah-Sokar-Osiris, topped with the atef crown.","i":103},{"id":"stela-of-smentaui-and-huy","no":"2202","en":"Stela of Smentaui and Huy","cn":"斯门塔维与胡伊石碑","g":"main","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"石灰岩","dim":"高 52 cm · 宽 40.5 cm · 厚 6 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"石碑上层是被神化的阿蒙霍特普一世及其母亲阿摩斯—奈芙尔塔里，他们坐在供桌前。下层两名跪拜者分别是斯门塔维和胡伊，可能正是委托制作这块石碑的人。\n这块圆顶石灰岩碑于1887年发现于底比斯西岸的库尔纳。两名男子之间的文字，记录了他们向国王与王后献上的祈祷。\n阿蒙霍特普一世和母亲后来成为底比斯墓地工匠及其家人的守护者。这块碑说明，王室人物在去世之后，仍可能进入普通人的宗教生活。","src":"A round-topped limestone stela discovered in Qurna (West Thebes) in 1887. In the upper register of the stela is a double scene of the deified King Amenhotep I and his mother Queen Ahmose-Nefertari seated at an offering table. In the lower register, Smentaui (left) and Huy (right) who apparently commissioned the stela are kneeling in adoration. Columns of texts in the space between the two men recite their prayers to Amenhotep I and Ahmose-Nefertari who became patrons of the workmen of the Theban necropolis and their families.","i":104},{"id":"head-of-king-amenhotep-iii","no":"2218","en":"Head of King Amenhotep III","cn":"阿蒙霍特普三世头像","g":"main","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"陶","dim":"高 39.5 cm · 宽 27.5 cm · 长 29 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":2,"body":"这件烧制陶土头像表现阿蒙霍特普三世。国王头戴凯普雷什冠，也就是常说的蓝冠，额前竖起一条具有守护意味的圣蛇。\n头像来自卡纳克窖藏，可能制作于国王统治晚期。宽大的杏仁形眼睛尤其醒目，这种面部特征后来也成为阿玛尔纳艺术中常见的风格。\n它为观察不同时期艺术之间的联系提供了一个细节：后来显著发展的造型特点，有时在更早的作品中已经可以看到端倪。","src":"A fired clay head from the Karnak Cache (CK 663) portraying King Amenhotep III. The king wears the khepresh crown (sometimes called the blue crown), while a royal uraeus snake rears protectively on his forehead. The large almond eyes of the king later became a stylistic feature of Amarna art. The head was probably made towards the end of King Amenhotep III’s reign.","i":105},{"id":"double-statue-of-nakhtmin-and-tiy","no":"2250","en":"Double Statue of Nakhtmin and Tiy","cn":"纳赫特敏与提伊双人像","g":"main","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"石灰岩","dim":"高 57.5 cm · 宽 40.7 cm · 长 64 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 索哈杰","star":false,"n":1,"body":"书吏纳赫特敏与妻子提伊并肩坐在供桌前。提伊将右手轻搭在丈夫左肩上，椅子下方还有一只拿着果实玩耍的小猴，为端正的双人像增添了生活气息。\n纳赫特敏戴齐肩假发，穿褶纹长裙和凉鞋。提伊是伊西斯女神的歌者，身穿在右胸下方打结的褶纹长衣，衣摆垂至脚踝。\n这组雕像发现于阿拜多斯北部墓地，艺术风格指向第十八王朝晚期至第十九王朝初。夫妻之间的触碰、小猴与供桌，共同构成了兼具家庭意味和供奉用途的场景。","src":"A remarkable double statue of an ancient Egyptian scribe named Nakhtmin, and his wife Tiy who served as a ‘Chantress of goddess Isis’. The statue was discovered during excavations in Abydos (northern necropolis). It depicts the couple sitting side by side, each on a stool. Nakhtmin is seated on the left, wearing a shoulder-length hair wig that half covers his ears, a long-pleated apron reaching to the middle of the calf with a trapezoidal centre piece and a pair of sandals. His wife wears a long hair wig and a long-pleated garment knotted below her right breast reaching down to her ankles. She places her right hand tenderly on her husband’s left shoulder. Below her chair, is a little monkey playing with a piece of fruit. The back pillar of the statue is somewhat narrower than the two chairs of the seated couple, extending up to their head level. The entire group is fixed on a step in front of an offering table. The art stylistic details of the statue point at a date in late Dynasty 18 or early Dynasty 19.","i":106},{"id":"stela-of-hornakht","no":"2353","en":"Stela of Hornakht","cn":"霍尔纳赫特石碑","g":"main","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 19 王朝","m":"石灰岩","dim":"高 48.2 cm · 宽 7.9 cm · 长 37 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 索哈杰","star":false,"n":1,"body":"霍尔纳赫特站在奥西里斯与伊西斯面前献上供品，是石碑的主要场景。他可能生活在第十九王朝，担任过敏神的大祭司。\n这块圆顶石灰岩葬碑出土于阿拜多斯。碑顶饰有翼日轮和卧姿阿努比斯，阿努比斯前腿间持权杖，背上配有连枷。底部两行象形文字则为霍尔纳赫特祈求供奉。\n画面与文字分工明确：上方的神圣形象提供守护，中间呈现献祭者，下方祷文说明他的愿望。顺着这个次序阅读，便容易理解整块碑的内容。","src":"A round-topped limestone funerary stela discovered in Abydos. The top of the stela is decorated with the winged sun disk with the recumbent figure of Anubis holding a sekhem sceptre between his front legs and a flail over his back. The main scene on the stela shows Hornakht who served as a high priest of god Min, probably in Dynasty 19, presenting offerings to the enthroned god Osiris and the goddess Isis. The two lines of hieroglyphic text at the bottom of the stela are an offering prayer for Hornakht.","i":107},{"id":"kneeling-statue-of-tjainefer","no":"3753","en":"Kneeling Statue of Tjainefer","cn":"恰伊涅费尔跪像","g":"main","p":"新王国时期","d":null,"m":"花岗岩","dim":"高 42 cm · 宽 14.5 cm · 长 24 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":2,"body":"阿蒙大祭司恰伊涅费尔跪坐在脚跟上，双手扶着置于膝前的羊首瓶。公羊是阿蒙—拉的神圣动物，因而这只容器与人物的祭司身份直接相关。\n这尊花岗岩像于1904年出土于卡纳克窖藏，造型风格提示其年代为第十九或第二十王朝。人物戴长假发，耳朵露在外面，身后设有背柱。\n基座与背柱上的铭文写明主人姓名、头衔，并祈求阿蒙—拉赐予来世的福祉。人物虔敬的姿态、羊首瓶与祷文，围绕同一位神祇形成完整的表达。","src":"This kneeling granite statue was discovered in 1904 in the Karnak Cache (CK 396). It represents Tjainefer, a high priest of Amun, wearing a long wig that frames his face and reaches to his upper chest leaving his ears exposed. He kneels on a rectangular base, sitting back on his heels with his feet perpendicular to the ground against a dorsal pillar. A ram-headed vase is steadied between his knees and his outstretched arms, palms resting flat half way up the vase. The ram was a sacred animal for the supreme deity of ancient Egypt Amun-Re. A horizontal line of incised hieroglyphs bordered by two incised lines runs around the base, starting at its front face and ending at the back. The back pillar is also decorated with a single column of text. The inscriptions on the statue provide its owner’s name, title and an offering prayer invoking Amun-Re to grant him a number of favours for his welfare in the afterlife. Stylistic details of the sculpture suggest a date in Dynasty 19 or 20.","i":108},{"id":"statue-of-amun-re-and-thutmose-iii","no":"3781","en":"Statue of Amun-Re and Thutmose III","cn":"阿蒙-拉与图特摩斯三世双人像","g":"main","p":"新王国时期","d":null,"m":"片岩","dim":"高 68 cm · 长 45 cm","prov":"上埃及","star":false,"n":1,"body":"图特摩斯三世坐在高背王座上，左臂环抱一尊较小的阿蒙神像。国王头戴涅墨斯头巾与阿特夫冠，佩假胡须，手中握着象征生命的安赫符号。\n王座两侧刻有上下埃及统一的图案，双脚下则是象征传统敌人的“九张弓”。王权、国家统一与神的守护，在同一件作品中并置。\n这组双人像于1904年出土于卡纳克窖藏。阿蒙的形象损毁明显，发现者勒格兰认为可能与阿肯那顿时期有关。残损部分也因此成为研究雕像后续经历的线索。","src":"This dyad was found by in the Karnak Cache (CK 135) in 1904. Here, King Thutmose III is seated on a high-back throne, decorated on both sides with the sign of unification between Upper and Lower Egypt. He wears a pleated nemes headcloth, fronted by a uraeus snake and topped with an atef crown. A royal false beard is attached to his chin and a royal kilt is wrapped around his waist. In his clenched fist is the ankh sign of life, while his left arm embraces a damaged smaller figure of god Amun. Legrain attributed the mutilation of Amun’s figure to the reign of Akhenaten. The incised inscription on the right jamb of the throne identifies Thutmose III as: ‘the good lord, Menkhepere, endowed with life’. The king’s bare feet trample over nine bows, symbol of the traditional enemies of Egypt in ancient times.","i":109},{"id":"sphinx-of-thutmose-iii","no":"3788","en":"Sphinx of Thutmose III","cn":"图特摩斯三世狮身人面像（方解石）","g":"main","p":"新王国时期","d":null,"m":"雪花石膏（埃及雪花石）","dim":"高 38.1 cm · 长 68 cm","prov":"上埃及","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这尊狮身人面像以埃及雪花石制成，人物头戴褶纹涅墨斯头巾，额前原有一条圣蛇。两只前爪之间的王名圈，明确写出了图特摩斯三世的名字。\n雕像发现于卡纳克窖藏，圣蛇头部、鼻尖与右前腿已有缺损。尽管如此，人面与狮身结合的整体造型仍清楚可辨。\n观看时，可以把注意力放在头巾褶纹和前爪间的铭文：前者体现雕刻的细致，后者则为人物身份提供了直接依据。","src":"This finely executed travertine (Egyptian alabaster) sphinx was discovered in the Karnak Cache (CK 363). It shows a human-headed sphinx, wearing the traditional pleated nemes royal head dress, fronted by a protective uraeus snake. The royal cartouche carved between the paws of the sphinx gives the name of King Thutmose III. The head of the uraeus, the tip of the nose and the right foreleg of the sphinx are broken.","i":110},{"id":"upper-part-of-a-statue-of-thutmose-iv","no":"3799","en":"Upper Part of a Statue of Thutmose IV","cn":"图特摩斯四世雕像上半身","g":"main","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"深色花岗岩","dim":"高 32.5 cm · 宽 14.2 cm · 长 25 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这件雕像只保存了头部与上半身。人物双臂交叉，持弯钩与连枷，胸前佩颈饰，原本可能穿着与塞德节庆典有关的礼服。\n圆形假发从额前向外隆起，盖住耳朵，后部垂至肩后。这种发式是判断身份的关键线索，研究者据此推测，雕像可能表现图特摩斯四世。\n由于身份尚未完全确定，理解这件残像时，最可靠的起点仍是现存细节：持物、颈饰与假发的形状。","src":"Head and torso of a king holding a crook and a flail in his crossed arms. A gorget collar adorns his chest and he was probably wearing the sed (jubilee) cloak. His round hair wig protrudes off his forehead, covering his ears and ending behind his shoulders. The sculpture probably represents King Thutmose IV whose reign is well noted for this hair style.","i":111},{"id":"block-statue-of-sobeknakht","no":"3995","en":"Block Statue of Sobeknakht","cn":"索贝克纳赫特方块坐像","g":"main","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 19 王朝","m":"闪长岩","dim":"高 36.4 cm · 宽 16.8 cm · 长 23.9 cm","prov":"不明","star":false,"n":3,"body":"索贝克纳赫特坐在厚垫上，长披衣包裹身体，双手平放在膝头。面容安静，脚部刻画细致，是一尊轮廓紧凑的方块坐像。\n他可能生活在第十九王朝，担任阿蒙领地的监督。披衣正面的一列文字记录了他的姓名与头衔。\n背柱上的祷文尤其亲切：它请求哈托尔女神赐给索贝克纳赫特一颗快乐的心，让他在阿蒙的领地中度过美好的时光。这样的愿望，使正式的官员形象也带上了个人对幸福的期待。","src":"A block statue of Sobeknakht who served as a ‘Supervisor at the Domain of Amun’ most likely in Dynasty 19. He is seated on a thick cushion, wearing a feathered hair wig and a long cloak. His face reflects a peaceful expression. Both hands are placed flat on his knees and his feet are carefully sculpted. The vertical column of incised hieroglyphs on the front of the cloak states his title and name. An offering formula inscribed on the back pillar implores the goddess Hathor to give Sobeknakht a joyful heart and a perfect time in the Domain of Amun.","i":112},{"id":"votive-stela-of-ramose-and-wepmose","no":"4288","en":"Votive Stela of Ramose and Wepmose","cn":"拉莫斯与维普摩斯还愿碑","g":"main","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 19 王朝","m":"石灰岩","dim":"高 43.5 cm · 宽 7 cm · 长 24.5 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 阿西尤特","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这块还愿碑上出现了胡狼、公牛、鹅和其他动物，它们分别与神祇相联系。碑由拉莫斯和维普摩斯献给阿蒙—拉及艾斯尤特的地方神乌普瓦韦特，风格属于第十九王朝。\n画面分为三层。上层拉莫斯跪拜胡狼形的乌普瓦韦特，旁边的公牛代表阿蒙—拉的一种形态。中层维普摩斯向两只胡狼礼拜；下层他又跪在展翅的鹅与两只卧伏动物之前。\n这件作品出自艾斯尤特杰法伊哈皮三世墓。它展示了一个重要特点：同一位神可以借不同动物形象出现，而一块奉献碑也能汇集多种地方宗教象征。","src":"An extraordinary limestone votive stela from the tomb of Djefaihapy III at Asyut (also known as the Salakhana tomb). It was dedicated by two men named Ramose and Wepmose to Amun-Re and Wepwawet (the local deity of Asyut). The iconography of the stela suggests a date in Dynasty 19. In the upper register, Ramose kneels before the jackal god Wepwawet who stands on a sledge-like standard. The short column of text above the deity’s head says: ‘Wepwawet of Upper Egypt, the Controller of the Two Lands’. Behind Wepwawet, is a bull described in the text as ‘Amun-Re Kamutef’ (the bull of his mother - a term originally denoting the king’s strength and fertility). In the middle register, Wepmose stands, raising both hands in adoration, before two jackals (Wepwawet of Upper Egypt and Wepwawet of Lower Egypt). Beneath the two jackals, is an offering table and smaller eels and fish above a large eel or snake. The eel was originally a sacred animal of the primeval deity Atum. In the lower register, Wepmose kneels in adoration before a goose with flapping wings and two recumbent goats. The goose has an erect phallus and is probably depicted here as an aspect of the god Amun. The two goats are also connected with Amun and Wepwawet.","i":113},{"id":"king-amenhotep-iii","no":"5797","en":"King Amenhotep III","cn":"阿蒙霍特普三世像（雪花石膏）","g":"main","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"雪花石膏（埃及雪花石）","dim":"高 32.5 cm · 宽 27.1 cm · 长 32 cm","prov":"不明","star":false,"n":2,"body":"这件王室雕像保留了上半部，人物戴褶纹涅墨斯头巾，额前饰圣蛇，下巴佩假胡须。头部装束清楚表明了国王身份。\n雕像以埃及雪花石制成。研究者根据造型细节，推测它属于阿蒙霍特普三世。他统治时期的繁荣，也为多种艺术创作提供了条件。\n虽然尚不能完全确定雕像的归属，现存的头巾、圣蛇与面部处理，仍展示了这件王室作品的精细之处。","src":"The upper part of a travertine (Egyptian alabaster) royal statue wearing a pleated nemes headcloth decorated with a uraeus snake and the false beard. Stylistic details suggest it belongs to King Amenhotep III whose reign was a time of prosperity and artistic expression.","i":114},{"id":"statue-of-saroy","no":"5872","en":"Statue of Saroy","cn":"萨罗伊跪像","g":"main","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 19 王朝","m":"黑色花岗岩","dim":"高 59 cm · 宽 30.5 cm · 长 33 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"王室书吏萨罗伊跪着扶住一根神标，神标上部现已折断。他右臂贴着标杆，左手从前方支撑，形成明确的奉献姿态。\n萨罗伊在拉美西斯二世时期任职。双层条纹假发与褶纹长袍符合拉美西斯时代的服饰风格，颈部佩双重荣誉项圈及胸饰。胸前文字写有他的姓名和头衔，右肩则刻着拉美西斯二世的王名圈。\n人物的职衔、王名与颈部饰物，共同说明他与宫廷的关系；扶持神标的动作，则突出作品的宗教性质。","src":"A kneeling statue of Saroy who served as a Royal Scribe under Ramesses II. Saroy is holding a standard along his right arm, supporting it with his left hand. The upper part of the standard is broken. He wears a double striated hair wig and a long pleated robe in fashion during the Ramesside era. Around his neck is a double shebyu-collar of honour and a pectoral. The two creases on his neck are also typical from the reign of Amenhotep III throughout the Amarna Period and into the early Ramesside Period. A single horizontal line of text on his chest mentions his name and title. The royal cartouche of King Ramesses II is carved on his right shoulder.","i":115},{"id":"double-statue-of-kheperkarasoneb-and-meryt","no":"6026","en":"Double Statue of Kheperkarasoneb and Meryt","cn":"凯佩尔卡拉索内布与梅丽特双人像","g":"main","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"石灰岩","dim":"高 36.9 cm · 宽 19.3 cm · 长 22.8 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":2,"body":"凯佩尔卡拉索内布与妻子梅丽特并肩坐在高背椅上。按照当时的艺术惯例，男子位于左侧，戴齐肩假发，穿中长短裙。\n梅丽特身穿贴身长裙，假发前方的两束辫发垂到胸前，后部则是一片较宽的发束。两人的发式与衣着，是辨认这组像细节的重点。\n这件石灰岩双人像来自底比斯西岸的代尔巴哈里。艺术风格与雕像上的供奉祷文，都指向第十八王朝初期。它以并坐的方式，保存了夫妻共同接受供奉的形象。","src":"A limestone statue of Kheperkarasoneb and his wife Meryt from Deir el-Bahri in West Thebes. The couple are seated side by side on a high back chair. Following ancient Egyptian artistic conventions, the man is seated on the left side. He wears a shoulder-length hair wig and a mid-length kilt. Meryt wears a close-fitting dress and a hair wig with two braids falling on her chest and a broader section of hair at the back. The style of art and the offering formula inscribed on the sculpture suggest a date at the beginning of Dynasty 18.","i":116},{"id":"colossal-dyad-of-amun-and-mut","no":"6729","en":"Colossal Dyad of Amun and Mut","cn":"阿蒙与穆特巨像","g":"main","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"石灰岩","dim":"高 414 cm · 宽 186 cm · 长 169 cm · 重 5000 g","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"阿蒙与穆特并坐，穆特用左臂环抱阿蒙，阿蒙则握着象征生命的安赫符号。这组巨像将两位神祇的关系表现得亲近而庄重。\n雕像残件发现于卡纳克阿蒙大神庙第四、第五塔门之间的柱廊，1998至1999年间重新拼合。阿蒙的双羽冠大部缺失，穆特则戴双冠、三分式假发和秃鹫头饰，身穿羽纹长裙。\n王座与基座铭文提到霍伦海布。两位神的面容，也带有霍伦海布及其王后穆特奈杰梅特的特征，让王室形象与神圣形象在这件作品中相互关联。","src":"Discovered in the colonnade of King Thutmose I between the fourth and fifth pylons at the Great Temple of Amun and Karnak, this colossal dyad represents god Amun and his consort goddess Mut. It was found in pieces that were reassembled in 1998/1999. The goddess Mut sits to Amun’s right, embracing him with her left arm. Amun’s left hand grasps an ankh sign (life). He wears a broad collar, an elaborate corselet and a pleated kilt. The double feathered crown atop his head is mostly lost. Mut wears a double crown, a tripartite wig with a uraeus snake, a vulture headdress and a feathered dress with two straps. The texts on the throne and on the statue base name King Horemheb of Dynasty 18. Interestingly, the facial features of the divine couple also reflect that of Horemheb and his wife Queen Mutnedjmet.","i":117},{"id":"sphinx-of-thutmose-iii-1","no":"9360","en":"Sphinx of Thutmose III","cn":"图特摩斯三世狮身人面像（花岗岩）","g":"main","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"花岗岩","dim":"高 34 cm · 宽 25 cm · 长 63 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这尊花岗岩狮身人面像表现图特摩斯三世。人首戴着褶纹涅墨斯头巾，额前饰有保护性的圣蛇，与狮身组合成传统的王室形象。\n它出土于卡纳克窖藏。两只前爪之间的象形文字称国王为“孟凯佩拉，善神，两地之主，阿蒙所爱者”，并为他祈愿永恒的生命。\n这段铭文既说明身份，也表达祝愿。将它与狮身人面像的造型一起看，便能理解作品如何同时呈现国王的力量、神的眷顾与长存的愿望。","src":"A granite sphinx of King Thutmose III discovered in the Karnak Cache (CK 495). It shows a human-headed sphinx wearing the traditional pleated nemes headcloth decorated by the protective uraeus snake. The hieroglyphic text between the paws of the sphinx identifies the king as ‘Menkhepre, the good god, lord of the Two Lands, beloved of Amun, life eternally’.","i":118},{"id":"stela-of-djedmutiuesankh","no":"465","en":"Stela of Djedmutiuesankh","cn":"杰德穆提乌桑赫石碑","g":"main","p":"第三中间期","d":"第 21 王朝","m":"彩绘木","dim":"高 25 cm · 宽 3.5 cm · 长 20.5 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"杰德穆提乌桑赫双臂举起，向鹰首的拉—霍拉赫提神礼拜。她戴长假发，头顶香膏锥与莲花花蕾，身穿宽松薄衣；神面前的供桌上则堆满供品。\n这块圆顶碑于1907年出土于卢克索西岸的麦迪奈特哈布。顶部绘有弧形天空符号与细致的翼日轮，神祇身上的方格纹衣服也颇为醒目。\n碑文是一首祈求太阳神将她接纳为追随者的赞歌。图像中的礼拜姿势与文字中的请求相互呼应，使碑面的内容形成完整的祈愿。","src":"This round-topped stela of Djedmutiuesankh was found in 1907 at Medinet Habu on the west bank at Thebes (Luxor). The curved sign of heaven and a beautifully detailed winged sun disc decorate the top of the stela. Below, Djedmutiuesankh is depicted as a middle-aged woman with almond-shaped eyes and arched brows. She wears a loose transparent robe, a long hair wig surmounted by a perfume cone and a lotus bud. She raises both arms in adoration before the enthroned figure of the hawk-headed deity Re-Horakhty who wears a unique checkered pattern garment. Before him, is a table piled high with offerings. The hieroglyphic text is a hymn asking the sun god to place Djedmutiuesankh with his followers.","i":119},{"id":"shabti-box-of-djedmaatiuesankh","no":"2382","en":"Shabti Box of Djedmaatiuesankh","cn":"杰德马阿提乌桑赫沙布提箱","g":"main","p":"第三中间期","d":null,"m":"彩绘木","dim":"高 35 cm · 宽 25 cm · 长 48 cm","prov":"不明","star":false,"n":2,"body":"这只彩绘木箱属于第二十一王朝阿蒙—拉的女歌者杰德马阿提乌桑赫，用来收纳沙布提俑。古埃及人相信，这些小俑会在来世被召唤出来，代替主人承担劳动。\n木箱由多块木板以木钉连接，表面覆石膏并施彩，拱形箱顶与下埃及神龛的形式有关。一侧绘有卧姿阿努比斯，另一侧是碑主跪坐在纸莎草船上的形象。\n短侧面还绘有太阳神之眼、象征西方的符号，以及代表主人灵魂的“巴”。不同图像共同围绕死者的守护、供养与来世生活展开。","src":"A painted wooden shabti box belonging to Djedmaatiuesankh who served as a ‘Chantress of Amun-Re’ in Dynasty 21. The shabti (funerary figurines) required for her burial would have been deposited in this box, where they were believed to lie sleeping until summoned to work on her behalf in the afterlife. The box has a barrel vaulted roof associated with the Lower Egyptian shrine. It is made of a number of wooden pieces pegged together and plastered over. The recumbent figure of god Anubis is shown holding the crook and flail of kingship on one side of the box, while Djedmaatiuesankh appears kneeling with one raised knee on a papyrus boat on the opposite side. She wears a red fillet and a long dress. The two short sides of the box show the left eye of the sun god with the hieroglyph for the West reaching out to extend life to the deceased and the ba (spirit) of Djedmaatiuesankh standing over food offerings in a gesture of adoration presumably toward the sun god.","i":120},{"id":"sphinx-of-shepenwepet","no":"4379","en":"Sphinx of Shepenwepet II","cn":"舍彭维佩特二世狮身人面像","g":"main","p":"第三中间期","d":null,"m":"灰色花岗岩","dim":"高 42.7 cm · 宽 25.2 cm · 长 48 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":2,"body":"这尊狮身人面像保留了前半部，女性头部下方伸出人的双臂，捧着一只羊首容器。它表现的是舍彭维佩特二世，努比亚国王皮耶之女。\n她担任“阿蒙神妻”，这是以底比斯为中心的重要女祭司职位。她的任期跨越第二十五王朝塔哈尔卡时期，并延续至第二十六王朝普萨美提克一世在位第九年之后。\n雕像于1904年出土于卡纳克窖藏。容器与基座上的姓名、头衔，以及另一尊相似雕像提供的对照，共同支持了对人物身份的判断。羊首容器也呼应了她与阿蒙崇拜的密切关系。","src":"The ‘god’s Wife of Amun’ was the highest-ranking priestess of that deity whose cult was centred in Thebes in Upper Egypt. It first appeared as an office in the Middle Kingdom. Its political potential reached its zenith in the Late Third Intermediate Period. Following the Persian invasion of Egypt in 525 BC, the title fell out of use. This granite sphinx of Shepenwepet II was discovered in 1904 in the Karnak Cache (CK 132). Shepenwepet II was the daughter of the Nubian King Piye. She served as ‘god’s Wife’ from the reign of King Taharqa (Dynasty 25) until after year nine of King Psametek I (Dynasty 26). The statue shows the forepart of a sphinx (rear part missing) with female head and human arms holding a ram-headed vessel decorated with a uraeus snake (partly broken). Shepenwepet II wears a hair wig that falls flat at the back and at the front, it divides into two large locks forming curled braids. Her name and titles are carved on the ram-headed vessel and on the statue base. Although the reading of the second cartouche of Shepenwepet is doubtful, an identical statue found at the sacred lake at Karnak (now in the Berlin Ägyptisches Museum) permits its attribution to Shepenwepet II.","i":121},{"id":"block-statue-of-penuuepeqer","no":"6525","en":"Block Statue of Penuuepeqer","cn":"佩努乌佩克尔方块坐像","g":"main","p":"第三中间期","d":"第 22 王朝","m":"硬砂岩","dim":"高 33.5 cm · 宽 15 cm · 长 24.6 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":4,"body":"佩努乌佩克尔蹲坐在垫上，身体被披衣完全包住，仅双手以浮雕显露，右手握着折叠的布。他戴齐肩条纹假发，假胡须与方块状的身体相连。\n这尊杂砂岩方块坐像于1904年出土于卡纳克窖藏，年代约为第二十二或第二十三王朝。主人在卡纳克阿蒙—拉神域担任过重要祭司职务。\n披衣正面的小画框内刻着底比斯三神：阿蒙—拉、穆特和孔苏。周围铭文则记录主人的姓名、职衔与家世，使人物与他所侍奉的神祇共同出现在雕像正面。","src":"A greywacke cube statue belonging to Penuuepeqer discovered in the Karnak Cache (CK 182) in 1904. Penuuepeqer held important priestly titles at the precinct of Amun-Re at Karnak. Judging by the sculpture’s stylistic details and its inscriptional material, it can be dated to Dynasty 22 or 23. Penuuepeqer is squatting on a cushion. He wears a shoulder-length striated hair wig that leaves his ears exposed and a false beard that is connected to the body block. A cloak fully covers his body with only the hands indicated in relief and the right hand holds a folded cloth. The statue has a shallow back pillar that ends just where it meets the wig. On the front of the cloak is a framed scene depicting the Theban triad: Amun-Re, Mut and Khonsu-Nefer-Hotep. The inscriptions give the name, titles and filiation of the statue owner.","i":122},{"id":"stela-of-neskhons","no":"468","en":"Stela of Neskhonsu","cn":"涅斯孔苏石碑","g":"main","p":"后期埃及","d":null,"m":"彩绘木","dim":"高 29 cm · 宽 3 cm · 长 26 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"天空女神努特弓起身体，手指和双脚触地，构成整块木碑的外框。她的身体之下，涅斯孔苏举手礼拜拉—霍拉赫提与西方女神，玛阿特女神则从身旁环抱着她。\n这块圆顶彩绘木碑出自代尔巴哈里的蒙图祭司墓地区。涅斯孔苏的丈夫是蒙图祭司，碑文也显示她本人来自祭司家庭。\n下方祷文请求太阳神赐予来世所需的供给。天空的环抱、女神的守护与供奉的祈愿，在同一碑面上组合成一套完整的保护图景。","src":"This round-topped painted wooden stela of Neskhons was found at Deir el-Bahri in an area dedicated for the burials of the priests of god Montu. Neskhons' husband was a priest of Montu. The stela is framed by the arched body of the sky goddess Nut who touches the earth with the tips of her fingers and her feet. A winged sun disc spans above hieroglyphs that read Behdety (a form of Horus of Edfu). The central scene on the stela shows Neskhons embraced by goddess Maat as she stands at an altar, her hands are raised in adoration before the falcon-headed god Re-Horakhty and the goddess of the West. On the lower part of the stela, an offering formula asks god Re-Horakhty to grant Neskhons provisions for the afterlife. Neskhons was apparently a descendant of a priestly family, as in the text her father Hormaa is referred to as the 'beloved of the god at Karnak'.","i":123},{"id":"statue-of-nesmin","no":"2267","en":"Statue of Nesmin","cn":"涅斯敏雕像","g":"main","p":"后期埃及","d":"第 30 王朝","m":"花岗岩","dim":"高 107 cm · 宽 24 cm · 长 45 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"涅斯敏左腿前迈，双臂垂在身侧，两手各握一块布。他戴长假发、佩假胡须，身穿短裙，整体姿态简洁端正。\n这尊花岗岩像于1904年出土于卡纳克窖藏。雕像提到第三十王朝国王奈克塔内布二世，造型也与该王时期的其他作品相近，因此年代较为明确。\n结合涅斯敏的另一尊雕像和一件提桶上的铭文，研究者能够整理出他的多项头衔，涉及卡纳克、卡布和托德等宗教地点。一位祭司的活动范围，也由分散保存的器物逐渐清晰起来。","src":"This granite statue was discovered in the Karnak Cache (CK 89) in 1904. It represents Nesmin son of Psametik with the left leg forward. He wears a long hair wig, a false beard and a short kilt. His arms hang down by his side and in each hand, he holds a kerchief. Nesmin is the owner of another statue (now in the Egyptian Museum, Cairo) and a situla (now in the Louvre). All three monuments make it possible to establish a complete list of his titles that link him to many religious localities, such as Karnak, el-Kab and Tod. The mention of King Nectanebo II on this statue and its similar art style to another statue (CK422) from the reign of the same king, both secure a date in Dynasty 30.","i":124},{"id":"donation-stela-of-apries","no":"2347","en":"Donation Stela of Apries","cn":"阿普里斯赠地石碑","g":"main","p":"后期埃及","d":"第 26 王朝","m":"石灰岩","dim":"高 46 cm · 宽 9.5 cm · 长 20 cm · 厚 9 cm","prov":"不明","star":false,"n":1,"body":"画面上，阿普里斯国王正向圣牛阿匹斯献祭；下方八行文字却说明，实际捐赠者是帕恩乌赫姆之子帕迪埃斯特。这种王室形象与私人捐赠并置的安排，是赠地碑的一项特点。\n这块圆顶石灰岩碑出土于上埃及赫尔莫波利斯，铭文纪年为第二十六王朝阿普里斯在位第十三年。\n赠地碑用于记录向神庙捐赠土地的行为。虽然捐赠者常是非王室成员，碑面仍通常以在位国王作为正式奉献者，反映土地奉献与王权之间的关系。","src":"The term ‘Donation Stelae’ refers to stelae that record a donation of land to a temple. These stelae date from the Third Intermediate Period to Dynasty 26. Although the actual donors of the stelae were often non-royal people, yet the reigning king was usually depicted as the official donor. This limestone rounded top stela was discovered at Hermopolis Magna (Ashmunein) in Upper Egypt. It is dated by its inscriptions to year 13 of the reign of King Apries, the fourth king of Dynasty 26. The stela is topped by the winged sun disc. Below, King Apries is making an offering to the sacred bull Apis. The eight lines of hieroglyphic text at the bottom of the stela indicate that the donation was made by Padiest son of Paenouhem.","i":125},{"id":"mask-and-bead-net-of-hekaemsaf","no":"2362","en":"Mask and Bead Net of Hekaemsaf","cn":"赫卡姆萨夫金面罩与珠网","g":"main","p":"后期埃及","d":"第 26 王朝","m":"金、青金石、费昂斯彩陶","dim":"高 6.8 cm · 宽 46 cm · 长 145 cm","prov":"孟菲斯 · 萨卡拉","star":false,"n":2,"body":"金面罩的眼白以长石制成，瞳孔为黑曜石，眼睑与眉毛则用青金石镶嵌。不同材料的颜色与光泽，共同塑造出赫卡姆萨夫的面容。\n他在第二十六王朝阿玛西斯时期担任“王室船队长”，完整墓葬发现于萨卡拉。木乃伊除金面罩外，还覆盖着精美织物及葬仪饰件。\n胸前八排珠饰以金鹰首收尾，下方是张开双翼的努特女神。纵向金带两侧排列荷鲁斯四子，以多重神圣形象守护死者。面罩本身由金片锤揲成形，兼具精细工艺与葬仪意义。","src":"A golden mask and mummy trappings from the wooden coffin and mummy of Hekaemsaf who served as a ‘Chief of Royal Boats’ under King Amasis in Dynasty 26. His intact burial was found at Saqqara and the mummy was covered with a golden mask and richly embroidered cloth wrappings. The mask is made of a repoussé gold plate; the eyes are of feldspar, the pupils of obsidian, the eyelids and eyebrows of lapis lazuli. Hekaemsaf’s hairstyle frames his face and hangs on either side of his beard. A collar of eight rows of beads ending in golden falcons heads covers his chest. Below the collar is a kneeling figure of the sky goddess Nut extending her winged arms. An inscribed golden band runs down from below the kneeling goddess and on each side of the band are the Four Sons of Horus in repoussé gold.","i":126},{"id":"statuette-of-a-falcon","no":"2375","en":"Statuette of a Falcon","cn":"荷鲁斯鹰像（镀金铜）","g":"main","p":"后期埃及","d":"第 26 王朝","m":"青铜","dim":"高 22.4 cm · 宽 6.8 cm · 长 16.9 cm","prov":"下埃及 · 西部省","star":false,"n":2,"body":"这只镀金青铜隼代表与王权有关的荷鲁斯神。头部、羽毛和颈饰以金色突出，宽项圈下还垂着太阳与心形组合的护身符。\n小像于1893年出土于三角洲西部的赛伊斯，年代为第二十六王朝。它采用失蜡法铸造：先以蜡制作模型，再包覆泥料，熔去蜡后向留下的空腔注入金属。\n基座铭文记有奉献者伊姆霍特普及其父亲的名字。将有姓名的神像献入神庙，可以让奉献者在宗教观念中持续参与供奉，即使本人无法进入日常祭仪的场所。","src":"This gilt bronze votive statuette of a hawk was discovered in 1893 at Sais (Sa-al-Hagar) in the western Delta and is dated to Dynasty 26. The statuette was made using the lost-wax technique in which a wax model was enclosed in clay and allowed to dry. The wax was then melted before the molten metal was poured into the resulting clay mould. Gold was used here to highlight the falcon’s head, plumage and jewellery. The statuette shows the avian form of god Horus, who was associated with kingship, wearing a crown (now partly broken) and a broad gilded collar ending in a solar-heart amulet. This amulet was probably used by ancient Egyptian kings as an attribute of god Horus, therefore, indicating the divine status of the king. The solar disk above the heart identified the king’s heart with the sun and may have signalled his ability to maintain maat (justice) in the same way the sun illuminated the universe. Such votive statuettes were donated to the temple to honour its deities. The gilded dedicatory text on the base of the statuette names a certain Imhotep, son of Padineith. By naming the dedicant in the inscription, he could magically participate in the daily temple rituals that common people were not allowed to attend.","i":127},{"id":"stela-of-khonsuirdis","no":"2622","en":"Stela of Khonsuirdis","cn":"孔苏伊尔迪斯石碑","g":"main","p":"后期埃及","d":null,"m":"彩绘石灰岩","dim":"高 51 cm · 宽 34.5 cm · 厚 12.8 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 阿斯旺","star":false,"n":1,"body":"孔苏伊尔迪斯在两组相对的场景中献上供品，分别面向阿图姆与拉—霍拉赫提。碑顶的翼日轮细节丰富，下方七行象形文字记录了他的姓名、职衔和家世。\n这块圆顶彩绘石灰岩碑来自上埃及纳格哈萨亚墓地，年代为第二十六王朝。铭文说明，碑主曾任敏神的大祭司。\n左右呼应的图像与下方个人信息相结合，让这块葬碑同时具备献祭场景、身份记录和身后祈愿的作用。","src":"A painted limestone round-topped stela from Nag el-Hassaya cemetery in Upper Egypt. The stela belongs to Khonsuirdis and is dated to Dynasty 26. In the lunette, is a beautifully detailed winged sun disk. Below, is a double scene showing the stela owner presenting offerings to Atum (left) and Re-Horakhti (right). A seven-line hieroglyphic text at the bottom of the stela gives the deceased’s name, titles and filiation. It appears from the text that Khonsuirdis served as a high priest of Min.","i":128},{"id":"stela-of-nebethutiyt","no":"2625","en":"Stela of Nebethutiyt","cn":"内贝胡提伊特石碑","g":"main","p":"后期埃及","d":"第 26 王朝","m":"彩绘石灰岩","dim":"高 53.5 cm · 宽 5.5 cm · 长 33 cm","prov":"上埃及","star":false,"n":1,"body":"内贝胡提伊特举起双手，在左右两组画面中分别向拉—霍拉赫提和阿图姆礼拜。碑顶绘有弧形天空符号，以及带两条圣蛇的翼日轮。\n她是普萨美提克的女儿，身份是叉铃演奏者。石碑出土于上埃及纳格哈萨亚墓地，属于第二十六王朝。\n画面下方各有一篇七行的颂歌，请求两位神赐予碑主供品。礼拜动作与祷文内容相呼应，也为我们保留了一位参与宗教音乐活动的女性的名字。","src":"A painted limestone stela from Nag el-Hassaya cemetery in Upper Egypt. It belongs to the sistrum player Nebethutiyt, daughter of Psametik and is dated to Dynasty 26. On the rounded-top of the stela is a curved sign for the sky and a winged sun disc with two uraeus snakes. In the double scene below, Nebethutiyt raises both hands in adoration before Re-Horakhti (right) and Atum (left). Under the scene, are two hymns, each is composed of seven horizontal lines of hieroglyphs, invoking the two deities to grant offerings for the stela owner.","i":129},{"id":"stela-of-nehemesbastet","no":"2904","en":"Stela of Nehemesbastet","cn":"内海梅斯芭丝特石碑","g":"main","p":"后期埃及","d":"第 26 王朝","m":"石灰岩","dim":"高 45 cm · 宽 4.5 cm · 长 33.2 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 索哈杰","star":false,"n":1,"body":"内海梅斯芭丝特站在前方，父亲与母亲跟在身后，三人都举起双臂，向拉—霍拉赫提献上摆满供品的桌子。家庭成员共同礼拜，是这块碑的主要场景。\n这件彩绘石灰岩碑来自阿拜多斯，年代为第二十六王朝普萨美提克一世时期。顶部绘天空符号、翼日轮与圣蛇，下面还有象征美好、守护与永恒的图案。\n人物上方的十二列文字为亡者祈求供奉。通过姓名、家庭关系和献祭场景，碑面把个人的来世愿望放在家人与神祇的共同守护之中。","src":"A painted limestone stela from Abydos. It belongs to Nehemesbastet daughter of Padewen and Neshathor and is dated to the reign of Psamtek I who ruled Egypt in Dynasty 26. A curved sign of the sky and a winged sun disc with two uraeus snakes fill the rounded top of the stela. Below, a nefer sign (beauty) is flanked by two wedjat eyes and two shen signs (eternity). The main scene on the stela shows Nehemesbastet followed by her father Padewen and her mother Neshathor. All three are standing, raising both arms in adoration and presenting an offering table laden with an assortment of offerings to god Re-Horakhty who stands on the left, on a pedestal in the form of the maat sign (justice). His head is topped by the sun disc fronted by a uraeus snake and his hands clasp the was sceptre (prosperity). Twelve vertical columns of hieroglyphic text, painted above the heads of the main characters in the scenes, recite an offering formula for the deceased.","i":130},{"id":"naophoros-statuette-of-pa-kher-khonsu","no":"3764","en":"Naophoros Statuette of Pa kher Khonsu","cn":"帕赫尔孔苏捧神龛像","g":"main","p":"后期埃及","d":"第 26 王朝","m":"片岩","dim":"高 47 cm · 宽 26.5 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":2,"body":"帕赫尔孔苏跪坐，双手捧着一座拱顶小神龛。龛中是狮首形态的穆特女神，头顶日轮与圣蛇；龛门上方还饰有翼日轮。\n小像于1905年出土于卡纳克窖藏，可能属于第二十六王朝前半期。铭文记录了主人多项宗教与行政头衔，包括“神父”、科普托斯的神衣祭司和掌印监督。\n神龛两侧、基座与背柱上的文字都与主人身份和祈愿有关。把神像捧在身前的姿态，直观表达了他与神祇之间的侍奉和庇护关系。","src":"This kneeling naophoros statuette of a man named Pa-kher-Khonsu was discovered by G. Legrain in the Karnak Cache in 1905 (CK 549). As indicated by the inscriptions on his statuette, Pa-kher-Khonsu held a number of important titles, such as the ‘God’s Father’, ‘Stolist of Coptos’, and ‘Overseer of the Seal’. One of his priestly titles: ‘The Priest of Gold’ connects him with the cult of goddess Hathor. The statuette shows him wearing a shoulder-length striated hair-wig and a short plain kilt. He kneels, sitting back on his heels with his feet perpendicular to the ground. Between his fingertips he holds a rectangular vaulted-top naos, housing a figure of goddess Mut depicted with the head of a lioness surmounted with a cobra and a sun-disk. The lintel of the naos is decorated with the winged sun-disk, and on either side of its door is a vertical column of hieroglyphs providing the name and titles of Pa-kher-Khonsu. On the statuette base is a horizontal line of inscription, and on the back pillar are two further vertical columns of texts reading an offering prayer in his favour. The statuette is probably to be dated to the first half of Dynasty 26, to the reign of Psamtek I or Apries.","i":131},{"id":"statue-of-wadjet","no":"5104","en":"Statue of Wadjet","cn":"瓦吉特狮形铜像","g":"main","p":"后期埃及","d":null,"m":"青铜","dim":"高 43.8 cm · 宽 36 cm","prov":"下埃及 · 西部省","star":false,"n":1,"body":"瓦吉特通常以眼镜蛇形象出现，是下埃及的守护女神，常与南方的奈赫贝特并列。本件却将她表现为狮形，展现了同一位神祇的另一种面貌。\n这尊还愿青铜像出土于三角洲西部的赛伊斯。王座侧面铭文称她为“瓦吉特，布托之主，天空的女主人”，为辨认身份提供了直接证据。\n她的狮形可能与泰芙努特、塞赫麦特等狮形女神之间的联系有关。这件作品说明，古埃及神的形象并非固定不变，铭文有时比外形更能明确其身份。","src":"This votive bronze statue of goddess Wadjet in her leonine form was discovered in Sais in the western Delta. Wadjet was the patroness of Lower Egypt and was traditionally paired with goddess Nekhbet of the South. She was often depicted as a cobra wearing the red crown of Lower Egypt or as a lioness. She probably acquired her leonine form because of her association with other leonine goddesses, such as Tefnut and Sekhmet. The text on the side of the throne identifies her as ‘Wadjet, Lady of Buto, Mistress of Heaven’.","i":132},{"id":"upper-part-of-a-royal-statue","no":"5787","en":"Upper Part of a Royal Statue","cn":"国王立像残躯","g":"main","p":"后期埃及","d":null,"m":"闪长岩","dim":"高 79.6 cm · 长 28.9 cm","prov":"不明","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这是一尊尚未完成的立像，可能表现一位国王。人物左腿前伸，双臂贴着身体，双手握起，膝盖以下已经残缺。\n额头上方保留一块长方形凸起，可能原计划雕成圣蛇；背柱也只完成了粗略修整。\n这些未加工完的部分，使它具有不同于成品雕像的价值。我们能够看到工匠预留的石料和造型尚未细化的状态，从中了解雕像逐步成形的过程。","src":"An unfinished standing statue, probably of a king, with the left leg advanced, arms against sides and hands closed. There is a rectangular projection above the forehead, probably intended for a uraeus snake. He wears a loincloth and the legs are broken off from the knees down. The back pillar is only roughed out.","i":133},{"id":"stela-of-wennefer","no":"32711","en":"Stela of Wennefer","cn":"温内费尔彩绘木碑","g":"main","p":"后期埃及","d":null,"m":"彩绘木","dim":"高 45.5 cm · 宽 4.3 cm · 长 28 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"温内费尔站在祭坛前，举起双手，分别向拉—霍拉赫提和阿图姆礼拜。两组场景被彩色边框围合，上方绘有天空符号与翼日轮。\n这块彩绘木碑出自底比斯西岸代尔巴哈里的蒙图祭司墓地区。温内费尔来自一个有影响力的祭司家族，人物前方文字写有他的姓名与头衔。\n下半部是两篇各六行的太阳颂歌，分别赞美升起与落下的太阳。左右对称的图像与文字，使一天之中太阳的不同阶段共同进入碑主的祈愿。","src":"This painted wooden stela was found in the area dedicated to the burials of the priests of god Montu at Deir-el-Bahri in West Thebes. Its owner Wennefer was a descendant of a powerful priestly family. The stela shows a winged sun disc under the curved sign of heaven above a double scene bordered by a colourful frame. The scene shows Wennefer standing at an altar, both hands raised in adoration before the hawk-headed god Re-Horakhty (left) and god Atum (right). Wennefer is clad in a long transparent robe. His name and title are given in the text before his head. The remainder of the stela has two columns of six horizontal lines of text containing two sun hymns glorifying the rising and setting sun.","i":134},{"id":"golden-necklace-dendera-treasure-hoards","no":"2554","en":"Golden Necklace (Dendera Treasure Hoards)","cn":"登德拉宝藏·金项圈（十挂饰）","g":"main","p":"希腊罗马时期","d":null,"m":"金","dim":"高 14 cm · 宽 4 cm · 长 12 cm · 直径 12.5 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 基纳","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这件托勒密时期的金项圈，以金丝为主体，两端用钩闭合，下方悬挂十个象征性形象。它属于1914年在登德拉被查获的一批宝藏器物。\n挂饰中可以辨认出河马女神塔沃里特、坐姿伊西斯、戴双冠的隼、人首鸟、乌加特眼和站立的奈菲尔图姆。不同神祇与符号集中在同一件首饰上。\n“登德拉宝藏”并非一次发现的单一收藏，而是在神庙与围墙之间陆续发现的多批珍贵器物。这件项圈展示了其中首饰与神圣图像相结合的一面。","src":"The so-called ‘Dendera Treasure Hoards’ were caches of spectacular objects of great art-historical value that were discovered in the area between the Dendera temple and its enclosure wall. Some objects, like this Ptolemaic golden necklace, were part of a hoard confiscated in 1914 at Dendera. The necklace is made of a gold wire closed with two hooks. Hanging from this wire are ten symbolic figures (from the left): Taweret (hippopotamus goddess of childbirth), goddess Isis seated, two falcons wearing the double crown, two human-headed birds wearing the solar disc between two horns, two more falcons wearing the double crown, a wedjat eye and a standing figure of god Nefertum.","i":135},{"id":"necklace-with-ornaments-and-pendant","no":"2555","en":"Necklace with Ornaments and Pendant","cn":"登德拉宝藏·金项圈（孩童荷鲁斯吊牌）","g":"main","p":"希腊罗马时期","d":null,"m":"金","dim":"高 21 cm · 宽 1.5 cm · 长 15 cm · 直径 14.5 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 基纳","star":false,"n":1,"body":"项圈中央是一块薄金牌，牌上表现孩童荷鲁斯：头戴双冠，左手持象征生命的安赫，右手持与哈托尔有关的叉铃。金牌下缘向后折起，以增加硬度。\n两侧串有乌加特眼、贝斯神小像与饰圆圈纹的球形珠，金丝两端用钩闭合。这件托勒密时期首饰于1914年发现于登德拉。\n观看时，可以先辨认中央孩童神，再看两旁反复出现的守护形象。它把可佩戴的首饰与祈求神圣庇护的图像组合在一起。","src":"A Ptolemaic golden necklace discovered at Dendera in 1914. The necklace is made of a solid gold wire with fourteen ornaments and closes at each end by a hook. The central pendant is a large gold plaque whose upper corners are rounded. The bottom of the plaque is folded back, giving it a little more rigidity. On the plaque, Horus the Child wears a double crown, holds an ankh sign (life) in his left hand and a sistrum (symbol of goddess Hathor) in his right hand. On each side of this plaque is strung a series of objects, six on one side, seven on the other. They include: two wadjet eyes, five figures of the god Bes and five spherical beads decorated with small circles.","i":136},{"id":"silver-statue-of-ihy-dendera-treasure-hoards","no":"2558","en":"Silver Statue of Ihy (Dendera Treasure Hoards)","cn":"登德拉宝藏·伊希银像（高49厘米）","g":"main","p":"希腊罗马时期","d":null,"m":"银","dim":"高 49 cm · 宽 15.5 cm · 长 21 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 基纳","star":false,"n":1,"body":"孩童神伊希身体微微前倾，双臂自然下垂，戴贴头小帽，胸前挂着心形护身符。圆润的腹部象征他带来丰足与繁荣的能力。\n伊希与欢乐和音乐有关。这尊银像表面已明显氧化，1918年出土于登德拉神庙圣湖附近的还愿埋藏。\n同批还发现了另一尊几乎相同的伊希像。这些神像与仪式器具、首饰等共同组成登德拉宝藏，反映了神庙奉献中丰富的器物类型。","src":"The ‘Dendera Treasure Hoards’ were caches discovered at Dendera in the area between the temple proper and its enclosure wall. They included spectacular silver, gold and bronze objects of great art-historical value. Among the discovered object were statues of divinities, ritual instruments, jewellery and mirrors. This silver statue was part of a votive ritual hoard discovered in 1918 near the sacred lake of the temple. The heavily oxidised statue shows the child god Ihy who personified joy and music in ancient Egypt. Ihy is nude, his body slightly tilted forward and his arms hanging down beside his body. He wears a skull cap and a heart-amulet hangs on his chest. His well-fed belly symbolises his ability to bring prosperity and abundance. The statue is almost identical with GEM 2559 (also from the same Dendera Treasure Hoard).","i":137},{"id":"silver-statue-of-ihy-dendera-treasure-hoards-1","no":"2559","en":"Silver Statue of Ihy (Dendera Treasure Hoards)","cn":"登德拉宝藏·伊希银像（高50厘米）","g":"main","p":"希腊罗马时期","d":null,"m":"银","dim":"高 50 cm · 宽 17 cm · 长 25 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 基纳","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这尊伊希银像与同批另一件作品几乎相同：孩童神裸身站立，身体略向前倾，双臂垂在身侧，头戴小帽，胸前佩心形护身符。\n伊希象征欢乐与音乐，饱满的腹部还带有丰足的含义。银像表面明显氧化，仍能辨认出主要造型。\n它于1918年发现于登德拉神庙西南侧圣湖附近。与同类神像一起观看，可以看到神庙还愿器物中重复采用相近神圣形象的现象。","src":"The ‘Dendera Treasure Hoards’ were caches of spectacular gold and silver objects, including statues of deities, ritual instruments, jewellery and mirrors. The caches were discovered at Dendera in the area between the temple proper and its enclosure wall. This heavily oxidised silver statue was among the objects discovered in 1918 near the sacred lake south-west of the temple of Dendera. It shows the god Ihy nude, his body slightly tilted forward and his arms hanging down beside his body. He wears a skull cap and a heart-amulet hangs on his chest. Ihy personified joy and music in ancient Egypt. His well-fed belly symbolises his ability to bring prosperity and abundance. The statue is almost identical with GEM 2558 (also from the same Dendera Treasure Hoard)","i":138},{"id":"silver-statue-of-a-goddess-dendera-treasure-hoards","no":"2560","en":"Silver Statue of a Goddess (Dendera Treasure Hoards)","cn":"登德拉宝藏·女神银像（高41厘米）","g":"main","p":"希腊罗马时期","d":null,"m":"银","dim":"高 41 cm · 宽 9.5 cm · 长 19 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 基纳","star":false,"n":1,"body":"女神端坐，戴三分式假发、额带、圣蛇与双冠，颈佩宽项圈，身穿贴身长裙。她可能是伊西斯，也可能是哈托尔，身份尚不能完全确定。\n右手握在膝上，拳心留有小孔，提示这里原本可能持一根权杖；另一只手则平放。这个小孔为复原雕像原貌提供了线索。\n银像于1918年与其他还愿器物一同出土于登德拉神庙圣湖附近，同批还有一尊几乎相同的女神像。","src":"A statue of a goddess (probably Isis or Hathor) from the so-called ‘Dendera Treasure Hoard’ - a votive ritual hoard of silver, gold and bronze objects discovered in 1918 near the sacred lake, south-west of the Dendera temple. The statue is almost identical with GEM 2561 (also from the same Dendera Treasure Hoard). The seated goddess wears a tripartite hair wig topped with a fillet, a uraeus snake and a double crown. She wears a broad collar and a close-fitting dress. Her right hand is clenched on her lap, suggesting that it once held a sceptre as indicated by the centred hole in her fist, while the other hand rests flat.","i":139},{"id":"silver-statue-of-a-goddess-dendera-treasure-hoards-1","no":"2561","en":"Silver Statue of a Goddess (Dendera Treasure Hoards)","cn":"登德拉宝藏·女神银像（高43厘米）","g":"main","p":"希腊罗马时期","d":null,"m":"银","dim":"高 43 cm · 宽 10 cm · 长 18 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 基纳","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这位坐姿女神双手握起，置于膝侧，戴着双冠、圣蛇、额带与三分式假发，颈部饰有宽项圈。她可能表现伊西斯或哈托尔，但现有线索不足以明确区分。\n银像于1918年出土于登德拉神庙圣湖附近，属于一批还愿埋藏，同批还包括金、银、青铜等多种材料的器物。\n它与另一尊女神银像造型十分接近。对照两件作品，可以留意手势等细节，理解相近的神像如何保留各自的变化。","src":"A statue of a goddess, probably Isis or Hathor, from the so-called ‘Dendera Treasure Hoards’ (caches of gorgeous silver, gold and bronze objects discovered in the area between the Dendera temple and its enclosure wall). The statue was discovered in 1918 near the sacred lake of the temple and is almost identical with GEM 2560 that came from the same votive ritual hoard. The seated goddess wears a tripartite hair wig topped with a fillet, a uraeus snake and a double crown. She wears a broad collar and a close-fitting dress, and her hands are clenched beside her knees.","i":140},{"id":"a-gilt-hawk-figure-dendera-treasure-hoards","no":"2564","en":"A Gilt Hawk Figure (Dendera Treasure Hoards)","cn":"登德拉宝藏·鎏金银鹰像","g":"main","p":"希腊罗马时期","d":null,"m":"银","dim":"高 19 cm · 宽 8.5 cm · 长 15 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 基纳","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这只小鹰表面鎏金，羽毛以刻线细细表现。小巧的体量与清楚的羽纹，是观察它的重点。\n它于1918年发现于登德拉神庙圣湖附近的一批还愿埋藏中。这批器物与当地陆续出土的其他金、银和青铜制品，合称“登德拉宝藏”。\n作为献入神庙的器物，它既体现了金属制作和装饰工艺，也保留了古埃及人以动物形象表达宗教奉献的方式。","src":"This small, gilt hawk with incised plumes was part of a votive ritual hoard discovered in 1918 near the sacred lake of the Dendera temple. The hoard was one of a number of successively discovered caches of spectacular silver, gold and bronze objects, now known as the Dendera Treasure Hoards.","i":141},{"id":"silver-statuette-of-a-sphinx-dendera-treasure-hoards","no":"2567","en":"Silver Statuette of a Sphinx (Dendera Treasure Hoards)","cn":"登德拉宝藏·银斯芬克斯像","g":"main","p":"希腊罗马时期","d":null,"m":"银","dim":"高 16 cm · 宽 8 cm · 长 27 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 基纳","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这尊银制狮身人面小像戴涅墨斯头巾，颈佩宽项圈，双眼原本可能采用镶嵌制作。王室装束与狮身结合，构成容易辨认的传统形象。\n它于1918年出土于登德拉神庙圣湖附近，属于一批用于还愿奉献的金属器物。\n与大型石制狮身人面像相比，这件作品把同类造型缩小并改用银材制作，成为神庙奉献的一部分，也展示了传统形象在不同材料与尺度上的运用。","src":"A silver statuette of a sphinx, discovered in 1918, among other objects in the Dendera Treasure Hoard (a cache of votive silver, gold and bronze objects discovered in 1918 near the sacred lake of the temple of Dendera). The sphinx wears a nemes headcloth, a broad collar and its eyes were probably inlaid.","i":142},{"id":"gold-necklace-dendera-treasure-hoards","no":"2589","en":"Gold Necklace (Dendera Treasure Hoards)","cn":"登德拉宝藏·金项链（神龛吊坠）","g":"main","p":"希腊罗马时期","d":null,"m":"金","dim":"高 13.5 cm · 宽 1 cm · 长 11 cm · 直径 11 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 基纳","star":false,"n":1,"body":"细金丝上穿着八颗金珠，中央悬挂一座小神龛。龛内刻画阿蒙、穆特和孔苏，也就是底比斯三神。\n这件托勒密时期金项链于1914年发现于登德拉。神龛由薄金片制成，连接项链的大环也由同一金片折成。\n制作上的细节与宗教图像同样值得注意：工匠用很少的材料构成悬挂结构，再把完整的三神组合放进小小的龛形吊坠中。","src":"A Ptolemaic gold necklace discovered at Dendera in 1914. It is made of a thin gold wire carrying eight gold beads and a small thin gold naos (shrine). The naos is joined to the wire by a large ring made using the same folded gold leaf. The Theban triad consisting of Amun, Mut and Khonsu are pictured in the naos.","i":143},{"id":"statue-of-man-carrying-a-naos","no":"2669","en":"Statue of Man Carrying a Naos","cn":"捧神龛的男子立像","g":"main","p":"希腊罗马时期","d":null,"m":"石灰岩","dim":"高 118 cm · 宽 22.5 cm · 长 39.2 cm","prov":"孟菲斯","star":false,"n":2,"body":"男子将一座小神龛捧在身前，龛内是孩童荷鲁斯，又称哈尔波克拉特斯。人物的卷发、短衣与向上凝望的镶嵌双眼，带有罗马时期的造型特点。\n这尊石灰岩像发现于孟菲斯的科姆卡拉遗址，没有铭文说明主人的姓名。研究者主要依据这些风格细节判断年代。\n作品把个人奉献者与神像放在同一构图中。虽然我们无法叫出他的名字，捧龛的姿态仍清楚表达了他与神祇之间的联系。","src":"This limestone statue of a man holding a naos (shrine) was discovered at Kom el-Qala in Memphis (Mit Rahina). The naos holds a figure of Harpocrates (Horus the Child). The statue has no inscriptions but the stylistic details of the sculpture, such as the curly hairstyle, the inlaid eyes gazing upward and the short tunic, all suggest a date in the Roman Period.","i":144},{"id":"isis-and-horus","no":"5132","en":"Isis and Horus","cn":"伊西斯哺乳荷鲁斯石碑","g":"main","p":"希腊罗马时期","d":null,"m":"砂岩","dim":"高 137 cm","prov":"上埃及","star":false,"n":1,"body":"伊西斯坐在抬高的低背王座上，为孩童荷鲁斯哺乳，面前设有供桌。这一主题在碑面上以两组场景重复呈现。\n女神戴三分式假发与秃鹫头饰，上方组合了额冠、双角间的日轮和王座符号。多重头饰帮助说明她的神圣身份。\n这块长方形砂岩碑来自上埃及阿尔曼特，顶部配有埃及式凹曲檐口与翼日轮。母亲哺育孩子的熟悉动作，在这里成为表现神祇关系的核心画面。","src":"A rectangular sandstone stela from Armant in Upper Egypt. The top is decorated with an Egyptian cavetto cornice and a winged sun disk. Below, is a double scene of goddess Isis seated at an offering table, nursing her child Horus. The low-backed throne on which the goddess sits is raised on a pedestal. Isis wears a tripartite hair wig, a vulture headdress topped by a diadem and a sun disk in between two horns surmounted by a throne.","i":145},{"id":"faience-amulet-dendera-treasure-hoards","no":"74660","en":"Faience Amulet (Dendera Treasure Hoards)","cn":"登德拉宝藏·釉陶护身符","g":"main","p":"希腊罗马时期","d":null,"m":"费昂斯彩陶、金","dim":"高 5 cm · 宽 1.4 cm · 长 2.7 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 基纳","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这枚贴金釉陶护身符出土时，并非单独放置，而是与一只鹰木乃伊一起藏在鹰形容器内。\n它属于1918年在登德拉神庙圣湖附近发现的一批还愿器物。理解这件展品，发现时的组合尤其重要：护身符、动物木乃伊和外部鹰形容器，共同构成了一组宗教奉献。","src":"A gilt-faience amulet found along with a mummified hawk inside a hawk figure, as part of a votive ritual hoard discovered in 1918 near the sacred lake of the Dendera temple (one of a group of caches, known as the Dendera Treasure Hoards).","i":146},{"id":"naos-shaped-amulet-dendera-treasure-hoards","no":"74674","en":"Naos-Shaped Amulet (Dendera Treasure Hoards)","cn":"登德拉宝藏·神龛形护身符","g":"main","p":"希腊罗马时期","d":null,"m":"银、金","dim":"高 5 cm · 宽 3.7 cm · 长 4 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 基纳","star":false,"n":1,"body":"小神龛中置着一只鹰，这枚护身符以银制成，表面贴金。它于1918年出土于登德拉神庙圣湖附近的还愿埋藏。\n发现时，护身符与一只鹰木乃伊同放在另一件鹰形器内。外层器物分为上下两部分，像盒身与盒盖一样可以合拢。\n从外层鹰形容器，到内部木乃伊，再到龛中小鹰，相关物件反复使用同一动物形象。这种组合比单独观看护身符，更能说明它原本的宗教环境。","src":"The so-called 'Dendera Treasure Hoards' were caches of spectacular silver, gold and bronze objects of great art-historical value, including divine statuettes, ritual instruments, jewellery and mirrors. The caches were discovered in and around the Dendera temple (the area between the temple and its enclosure wall). This gilt-silver amulet in the form of hawk inside a naos (shrine) was part of a votive ritual hoard discovered in 1918 near the sacred lake of the temple. It was found along with a mummified hawk inside a hawk figure consisting of two parts as if a box and its lid.","i":147},{"id":"anubis-on-a-chest","no":"6","en":"Anubis on a Chest","cn":"阿努比斯神箱","g":"tut","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"木、金、银、石英岩、黑曜石、雪花石膏（埃及雪花石）","dim":"高 54.3 cm · 宽 37 cm · 长 95 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":true,"n":1,"body":"一只黑金相间的胡狼伏在箱顶，长尾垂到箱后。它代表木乃伊制作之神、墓地守护者阿努比斯。这件神箱发现于图坦卡蒙墓宝藏室的入口内侧。\n箱体外形模仿埃及神庙的塔门，固定在贴金木橇上，并配有长抬杆。箱内分成四个小格和一个大格，分别存放用亚麻布包裹的祭仪用品与首饰。\n它既是收纳器，也以神庙形制和守护神像赋予所藏物品神圣意义。观看时，箱顶的阿努比斯与箱身的建筑造型，可以联系起来理解。","src":"This large carrying chest was found just inside the Treasury. The box is shaped like the pylon gateway walls that stand in front of Egyptian temples. It is fixed onto a gilded wooden sledge with long carrying poles. An impressive black and gold figure of the god Anubis as a jackal sits on top, with its tail hanging down at the back of the box. Anubis was god of mummification and the guardian of the necropolis. Inside, the box is divided into four small compartments that contained cult objects wrapped in linen and one large compartment holding jewellery.","i":148},{"id":"the-golden-burial-mask-of-tutankhamun","no":"8","en":"The Golden Burial Mask of Tutankhamun","cn":"图坦卡蒙黄金面具","g":"tut","p":"新王国时期","d":null,"m":"金、玻璃、青金石、黑曜石、红玉髓、费昂斯彩陶、石英岩","dim":"宽 39.3 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":true,"n":2,"body":"这件黄金面具原本覆盖在图坦卡蒙木乃伊的头部和肩部。它保留了国王可辨认的面容，同时将他塑造成与奥西里斯及太阳神拉相联系的神圣形象。\n在古埃及观念中，神的身体可以被描述为黄金，头发则如青金石。面具的材料与色彩因此不仅华丽，也参与表达国王死后的神性。\n背面的铭文逐一把额头、双眼和眉毛等部位与不同神祇相对应，为死者祈求保护。它既是一幅理想化的王者肖像，也是一件围绕身体守护而制作的葬仪用品。","src":"This mask of solid gold is one of the most famous objects in the world. It was found placed over the head and shoulders of Tutankhamun’s mummified remains. The king is made to look like the god Osiris, ruler of the underworld, and the sun god Re whose body was made of gold and hair of lapis lazuli. At the same time, this is a perfect version of Tutankhamun’s face, recognisable from his coffins, statues and temple reliefs. An inscription on the back provides further protection by identifying parts of the mask with different gods ‘Your forehead is Anubis, your right eye is the night boat (of Re), your left eye is the day boat, your eyebrows are in the company of nine gods’.","i":149},{"id":"canopic-shrine-on-a-sledge","no":"9","en":"Canopic Shrine on a Sledge","cn":"卡诺匹斯神龛","g":"tut","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"木、金","dim":"高 198 cm · 宽 122 cm · 长 165 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":true,"n":1,"body":"四位女神站在神龛四周，张开双臂，守护图坦卡蒙保存内脏的容器。她们分别是伊西斯、奈芙蒂斯、塞尔凯特和涅伊特。\n神龛以木材制成，外覆多层金箔，安置在木橇上。外部敞开式罩棚与内部龛体上，都排列着具有保护意味的眼镜蛇饰带，并镶有红、蓝、绿玻璃。\n神龛内还套有卡诺匹斯圣柜和小金棺。就像国王遗体被多层棺具包围一样，取出的内脏也被层层安置、分别守护。","src":"Made of wood covered in layers of gold foil, Tutankhamun’s canopic shrine protected his mummified internal organs. Like the large shrines that surrounded the sarcophagus and the coffins, the canopic shrine protected the canopic chest and the miniature coffins inside. An open canopy topped by a frieze of protective cobras inlaid with red, blue and green glass sits on a sledge. Under this is a wooden shrine decorated with scenes of gods on each side and another frieze of colourful cobras. Four gracious figures of the goddesses Isis, Nephthys, Selket and Neith guard the shrine with outstretched protective arms.","i":150},{"id":"canopic-coffinette","no":"11","en":"Canopic Coffinette","cn":"卡诺匹斯小棺","g":"tut","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"金、红玉髓、玻璃","dim":"高 12 cm · 长 39 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":true,"n":3,"body":"这具小金棺属于保存图坦卡蒙内脏的四件套之一，形制与国王的第二层人形棺相近。四具小棺分别收纳经过木乃伊化处理的肝、肺、肠和胃。\n棺体用黄金锤制，羽毛纹中镶入红玉髓与彩色玻璃。人物戴涅墨斯头巾，受秃鹫与圣蛇守护，双手持弯钩和连枷。\n本件内部的图像与铭文表明，它与奈芙蒂斯女神有关。精细到微小嵌片的装饰，说明这些器官容器也按王室葬仪的要求认真制作。","src":"Tutankhamun’s mummified viscera (liver, lungs, intestines and stomach) were held inside four miniature coffins similar in design to his second anthropoid coffin. Made of beaten solid gold, the coffinettes are exquisitely decorated in a feathered pattern inlaid with red carnelian and coloured glass. Each shows a king wearing a royal nemes headcloth protected by a vulture and a uraeus snake and clutching a crook and a flail. Scenes and inscriptions inside this coffinette show that it is associated with the goddess Nephthys.","i":151},{"id":"royal-diadem","no":"17","en":"Royal Diadem","cn":"图坦卡蒙王冠头带","g":"tut","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"金","dim":"高 39 cm · 宽 11 cm · 长 19 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":true,"n":1,"body":"这条金头带原本围在图坦卡蒙头上，藏在黄金面具之下。带面交替装饰红玉髓圆片与蓝玻璃方片，前方可以安装秃鹫和眼镜蛇，象征对上、下埃及的统治。\n两件前饰能够拆卸，通过背面的凹槽与头带上的插片相接。出土时，它们被另放在国王大腿处。\n头带后方系结处垂下两条饰带与两条圣蛇，并以铰接方式适应不同大小的假发。贵重材料之外，这些可拆卸、可活动的结构，也展现了首饰设计的细致。","src":"Concealed under the golden funerary mask, this elaborate diadem encircled the king’s head. The fillet (headband) is of solid gold decorated with red carnelian roundels and blue glass squares. Upon its discovery, the removable vulture and uraeus snake (symbols of sovereignty over Upper and Lower Egypt) were placed on the king’s thighs. They have grooves on their backs that fit onto tongues sticking out from the front of the fillet. Two ribbons and two uraeus snakes hang from a bow at the back of the fillet and are hinged to fit over different sized wigs.","i":152},{"id":"lion-shaped-perfume-jar","no":"39","en":"Lion-Shaped Perfume Jar","cn":"狮形香油瓶","g":"tut","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"雪花石膏","dim":"高 59.7 cm · 宽 16.8 cm · 长 19 cm","prov":null,"star":true,"n":4,"body":"一只戴冠狮子站在高凳上，实际上却是一只香膏容器。它用埃及雪花石雕成，牙齿和舌头为象牙，已经遗失的耳饰与爪部原本可能以黄金制作。\n香油瓶发现于图坦卡蒙墓附室。卡特记录，出土时内部仍留有干燥、发黑的油脂状香膏残留。狮子胸前的铭牌刻着图坦卡蒙与安克赫塞纳蒙的名字。\n冠形瓶盖当时落在旁边地面上，仍带着用于固定的亚麻布条残迹。它把容器、动物造型与王室姓名组合成了一件精巧的宫廷用品。","src":"This fancy perfume jar in the form of a crowned lion standing on a tall stool was found in the Annex. Howard Carter said it still contained perfumed ointment when found, ‘a dried blackened fatty substance’. The vessel is carved out of Egyptian alabaster. The lion’s teeth and tongue are ivory and his now-missing earrings and claws were probably gold. Tutankhamun and Ankhesenamun’s names are carved into a panel on the front of the lion’s chest. The crown lid was found on the floor next to the jar, with remains of linen strips that had tied it to the top of the lion’s head.","i":153},{"id":"golden-throne","no":"4573","en":"Golden Throne","cn":"黄金宝座","g":"tut","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"木","dim":"高 103.5 cm · 宽 59 cm · 长 73 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":true,"n":5,"body":"椅背正面的图像表现图坦卡蒙与王后置身花饰棚下，上方是阿吞日轮伸下的光芒。这一场景是黄金宝座最醒目的部分。\n宝座以木材为胎，外包金片，再用玻璃、釉料制品和半宝石镶嵌。两侧板由展翼圣蛇组成，蛇翼托护着国王的王名圈。\n它出土于墓葬前室，发现时包裹着亚麻布。虽然椅子按成人尺寸制作，其年代仍应属于图坦卡蒙即位初期。椅背图像也保留了与阿吞崇拜有关的时代痕迹。","src":"This beautifully decorated armchair was found wrapped in linen in the Antechamber. It is made of wood covered with sheets of gold that are both chased (pattern pressed into the metal) and inlaid with glass, faience and semi-precious stones. Side panels are formed from winged uraeus snakes holding the king’s cartouche. The scene on the front of backrest shows the king and queen under a floral canopy pierced by the rays of the Aten sun disk. Although adult-sized, this armchair must date from the beginning of Tutankhamun’s reign.","i":154},{"id":"outer-coffin","no":"7590","en":"Outer Coffin","cn":"图坦卡蒙外棺","g":"tut","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"木","dim":"高 105.5 cm · 宽 86.8 cm · 长 223.5 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":true,"n":1,"body":"这具人形木棺是图坦卡蒙石棺内三层棺中最大的一层。国王被塑成木乃伊形象，双手交叉在胸前。\n棺身与棺盖由木材制成，外覆石膏、亚麻布和薄金箔；面部、耳朵、颈部及双手则使用更厚的金片锤制，使这些部位格外突出。\n发掘时，卡特在移开沉重的石棺盖、揭去两层亚麻包裹后，才见到它。理解这具外棺，可以从层层套合的葬具入手：它既包围着内部两具棺，也共同承担着保护国王遗体的作用。","src":"This is the largest of three coffins found inside the sarcophagus of King Tutankhamun. The excavator Howard Carter wrote that after lifting off the heavy stone sarcophagus lid and peeling back two layers of linen wrappings, ‘a gasp of wonderment escaped our lips, so gorgeous was the sight that met our eyes’. The box and lid of the coffin are made from wood covered in plaster, linen and thin gold foil, while the king’s face, ears, neck and hands are covered in much thicker sheet-gold hammered into shape. The coffin is anthropoid (human-shaped) and shows the king as a mummified figure with crossed hands.","i":155},{"id":"guardian-statue-with-khat-headdress","no":"4","en":"Guardian Statue with Khat Headdress","cn":"戴卡哈特头巾的守护像","g":"tut","p":"新王国时期","d":null,"m":"金、木","dim":"高 192.8 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这尊守护像戴卡哈特头巾，穿褶纹王室短裙，手持权标和长杖。它原本与另一尊几乎相同的雕像一起，守在图坦卡蒙墓主墓室的封闭入口两侧。\n两像可能分别表现国王与他的“卡”，也就是与生命力有关的精神性存在。本件短裙前方的铭文，明确提到国王的“王室之卡”及其登基名涅布赫佩鲁拉。\n略鼓的腹部、较细的双腿和穿孔耳朵，反映了阿玛尔纳艺术的影响。头巾与铭文，则是区分这一对守护像的重要细节。","src":"Two almost identical portrait statues of King Tutankhamun flanked the sealed entrance to his Burial Chamber. The two figures possibly represented the king and his ka (soul). This statue is wearing a khat headdress and a pleated royal kilt, and holds a mace and a long staff. An inscription down the front of its kilt says: ‘The good god, the sovereign, the royal ka of Horakhty, Osiris, the king, lord of the lands, Nebkheperure, justified’. The bulging abdomens, relatively slim legs and pierced ears of the statues reflect the Amarna style of art, common during the reign of King Akhenaten.","i":156},{"id":"guardian-statue-with-nemes-headcloth","no":"5","en":"Guardian Statue with Nemes Headcloth","cn":"戴涅墨斯头巾的守护像","g":"tut","p":"新王国时期","d":null,"m":"木、金、青铜、石膏底料","dim":"高 195 cm · 宽 55 cm · 长 99.7 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这尊与真人等大的守护像戴涅墨斯头巾，身穿褶纹短裙，手持长杖与权标。它与另一尊守护像相向而立，原本分列在图坦卡蒙主墓室的封闭门前。\n黑色的身体具有象征意义：它让人联想到尼罗河洪水带来的肥沃黑土，也表达复生的观念。短裙正面的铭文为图坦卡蒙祈愿，愿他像太阳神拉一样，日日获得生命。\n持杖的死者形象早已见于假门和葬仪图像。本件将这种传统化为立体人像，安置在墓室入口，成为葬仪空间中的守护者。","src":"This life-sized statue of King Tutankhamun is one of a pair that stood face to face before the sealed doorway to his Burial Chamber. Scenes of the deceased holding a staff and a sceptre frequently appear on false doors from the Old Kingdom onwards as well as in vignettes from the Book of the Dead. In this statue, the king wears a nemes headcloth and a pleated royal kilt, and holds a long staff and a mace. The black colouring evokes the fertility of the black silt deposited annually by the Nile flood and also symbolizes resurrection. An inscription down the front of the kilt says: ‘Tutankhamun, may he be given life forever, like Re, every day’.","i":157},{"id":"canopic-chest","no":"10","en":"Canopic Chest","cn":"卡诺匹斯圣柜","g":"tut","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"金、颜料、雪花石膏（埃及雪花石）","dim":"高 85.5 cm · 长 54 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":2,"body":"卡诺匹斯圣柜内凿有四个圆筒形凹槽，原本各放一具黄金小棺，保存图坦卡蒙的内脏。每个槽口上方都有王首形塞盖，五官细节用黑色与红色勾出。\n圣柜原来安放在外层卡诺匹斯神龛中，下承覆金箔的木橇，斜顶柜盖以亚麻绳系牢。\n四角浮雕刻着伊西斯、奈芙蒂斯、塞尔凯特与涅伊特，下方饰带则重复象征稳定的杰德柱和具有守护含义的提特结。内外容器与神祇图像，共同组成一套层层保护的安排。","src":"Tutankhamun’s canopic shrine concealed this exquisite canopic chest. It is shaped like a ritual shrine with a sloping lid that was tied on with linen ropes, all sitting on a gold foil-covered wooden sledge. The chest contains four cylindrical hollows that held four solid gold miniature coffins. Each hollow is topped with a stopper finely carved in the form of a royal head with details picked out in black and red paint. Four protective goddesses Isis, Nephthys, Selket and Neith are carved in raised relief in each corner and stand on top of a frieze of djed pillar (stability) and tyet knot (protection) signs.","i":158},{"id":"lotus-cup","no":"36","en":"Lotus Cup","cn":"莲花杯","g":"tut","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"雪花石膏","dim":"高 18.2 cm · 宽 17.3 cm · 长 28.5 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"杯身像一朵盛开的白莲花，两侧把手则由蓝莲花与花蕾组成。花上托着跪姿的永恒之神赫赫，使一只杯子成为对国王长久生命的祝愿。\n赫赫手持生命符号与象征年岁的棕榈枝，下方配有表示巨大数量的蝌蚪和象征无尽的申环。多种符号组合起来，表达岁月绵延的愿望。\n杯口铭文进一步写道，愿国王的“卡”长存，历经无数岁月，面向北风而坐，眼中尽见幸福。器形、图像与文字，因此都围绕同一个温柔的愿望展开。","src":"The central part of this footed cup is in the form of an open white lotus flower on a stem. Two handles in the form of blue lotus flowers and buds, support baskets carrying kneeling figures of Heh, god of eternity, who holds ankh (life) signs and palm branches (years) resting on tadpoles (one hundred thousand) and shen (infinity) signs. These mean the cup wishes everlasting life for the king. An inscription around the rim says ‘May your ka (soul) live, may you pass millions of years, you who love Thebes, sitting with your face towards the north wind, your eyes beholding happiness’.","i":159},{"id":"fancy-perfume-vase","no":"47","en":"Fancy Perfume Vase","cn":"河神纹香水瓶","g":"tut","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"雪花石膏（埃及雪花石）","dim":"高 69.5 cm · 长 38 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":2,"body":"香水瓶细长的瓶颈两侧，站着两位尼罗河神哈皮。他们将莲花与纸莎草系在瓶颈周围，象征尼罗河谷与三角洲、也就是上下埃及的统一。\n植物标志上托着戴不同王冠的圣蛇，瓶口上方还有一只秃鹫。瓶身铭文写有图坦卡蒙与王后的名字和头衔，底座则以两只隼守护国王的王名圈。\n这件器物发现于主墓室。统一的图案、王室姓名与守护形象层层组合，使一只香水瓶也成为表达王权与神圣庇护的作品。","src":"This exquisite perfume vase was found in the burial chamber. The long slender neck of the vase ends in a flat rim surmounted by a vulture. Two figures of the god Hapy who personified the Nile are knotting lotus and papyrus plants around the neck of the vase, symbolizing the unification of the Nile Valley and Delta. The lotus and papyrus emblems carry royal uraeus snakes wearing the crowns of Upper and Lower Egypt. The names and titles of the royal couple are inscribed on the vase. On the pedestal, the cartouche of Tutankhamun is protected by two falcons perching on the nwb sign for gold.","i":160},{"id":"cow-head","no":"106","en":"Cow Head","cn":"哈托尔牛头","g":"tut","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"木","dim":"高 92 cm · 宽 40 cm · 长 45 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这件牛头由整块木料雕成，头部、双耳和上颈贴金，下颈涂黑。木角外包铜片，再覆厚厚的黑色树脂。出土时，颈部还围着一大块亚麻布。\n它可能代表以母牛形象出现的哈托尔女神，作为西方女神迎接死者进入来世。类似牛头也见于阿蒙霍特普二世和图特摩斯四世的墓中。\n木制神像是王室随葬品的一部分。材料、色彩和包裹方式，让这件牛头既保留雕塑的表现力，也属于具体的葬仪安排。","src":"This head, carved from a single block of wood, was found with the throat wrapped in a large piece of linen like a scarf around its neck. The lower part of the cow’s neck is painted black, while the upper neck, head and ears are covered in gold foil. Her copper covered wooden horns were painted with a thick layer of black resin. Wooden statues of gods were part of royal funerary equipment and cow heads were also found in the tombs of Amenhotep II and Thutmose IV. They probably represented Hathor, goddess of the West, welcoming the dead into her world.","i":161},{"id":"ivory-jewellery-box","no":"250","en":"Ivory Jewellery Box","cn":"象牙首饰盒","g":"tut","p":"新王国时期","d":null,"m":"象牙","dim":"高 13.8 cm · 宽 12 cm · 长 15.7 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这只小盒由象牙板与象牙块拼合而成，配有金制钮、合页和小足。背面刻着象征上埃及的莲花柱，正面与顶部横带则写有国王的名字。\n盒盖上另有一行黑墨僧侣体文字，注明“送葬行列所用的金戒指”。这条记录为理解盒子的内容与用途提供了直接线索。\n它发现于图坦卡蒙墓前室。墓中箱盒超过五十件，小型盒子常用于收纳首饰、化妆品或个人用品。本件将精巧的材料工艺与具体的收纳记录保存在了一起。","src":"This small box was found in the Antechamber. It is constructed from blocks and panels of solid ivory. The back is decorated with a lotus capital column symbolising Upper Egypt and there are two gold knobs, gold hinges and gold feet. The king’s names are carved on the front and in a band running across the top. A line of hieratic text in black ink on the lid says: ‘gold rings for the funeral procession’. Boxes were used for storage in ancient Egypt and Tutankhamun’s tomb included more than fifty examples. Small ones like this often held jewellery, cosmetics or other personal items.","i":162},{"id":"floral-hair-box","no":"255","en":"Floral Hair Box","cn":"花卉纹发盒","g":"tut","p":"新王国时期","d":null,"m":"木、雪花石膏（埃及雪花石）","dim":"高 25.5 cm · 长 35 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"盒盖绘着两束植物，包括纸莎草、曼德拉草果、矢车菊和莲花瓣，盒身四周排列蓝莲花瓣纹。两个黑色钮由黑曜石制成，与彩绘形成鲜明对比。\n它发现于墓葬前室的一只黄色木箱内。卡特记录，盒中有两个用布包裹的圆团，里面是头发。其他墓葬也发现过含头发的泥团。\n这些头发可能来自图坦卡蒙与王后安克赫塞纳蒙，并具有仪式意义，但归属尚未确定。华丽花纹之外，真正特别的是它保存的内容：看似日常的盒子，也可能用于安置与身体有关的仪式物品。","src":"Found inside a yellow-painted wooden box in the Antechamber, this elegant box is decorated in different coloured pigments. There are two bouquets of papyrus, mandrake fruits, cornflowers and lotus petals on the lid and rows of blue lotus flower petals around the sides. The two black knobs are made of obsidian (volcanic glass). The contents were unusual. Howard Carter described finding two round balls of hair covered with cloth. Mud balls containing hair have been found in other tombs. It is possible that this hair came from Tutankhamun and his wife Ankhesenamun and had a ritual significance.","i":163},{"id":"lions-headrest","no":"270","en":"Lions Headrest","cn":"狮子头枕","g":"tut","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"象牙、颜料","dim":"高 18.2 cm · 长 29.5 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"象牙头枕的中央，空气之神舒跪着举起双臂，托住弯曲的枕面。两侧各有一头卧狮，代表地平线的两位守护者。\n舒的头发和短裙细节以黑色描绘，背面一列文字写有图坦卡蒙的姓名与头衔。\n当国王把头放在弧形托面上时，这一姿态便被比作舒神将太阳从冥界托起。头枕因此既是支撑头部的寝具，也以具体造型表达了太阳升起与死者复生的联系。","src":"This ivory headrest has a slim wide base with a central pillar shaped as a kneeling figure of god Shu (air) holding with upraised arms a gracefully curved head support. Flanking god Shu are two crouching lions representing the two guardians of the horizon. Details of the god’s hair and kilt are coloured in black. A strip of text providing King Tutankhamun’s names and titles is written down the back of the kneeling figure. The king’s head resting on the curved head support emulated the sun disc being raised out of the Netherworld by the god Shu.","i":164},{"id":"ostrich-hunt-fan","no":"284","en":"Ostrich Hunt Fan","cn":"猎鸵鸟金扇","g":"tut","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"金","dim":"高 106 cm · 宽 4 cm · 长 19 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"金扇两面的图像，讲述了狩猎的前后过程。一面是图坦卡蒙与猎犬乘车追逐鸵鸟，弓箭已备；另一面则是国王放慢速度返回，两名侍从扛着猎获的鸟。\n扇头与扇柄上的文字说明，羽毛来自赫利奥波利斯以东沙漠的鸵鸟狩猎。图像因此不仅是装饰，也在解释扇羽的来历。\n金扇出土于主墓室。原有羽毛已遭虫蛀，无法保存，但残迹仍显示出褐色与白色相间的排列。今天的扇体、铭文和发掘记录，一起帮助我们了解它原来的面貌。","src":"This fan was found in the Burial Chamber. Upon its discovery, a mass of debris of insect-eaten ostrich feathers were found with it. Although they could not be saved, there was enough left to show that there had been alternating brown and white feathers. Texts on the fan palm (head) and stock (handle) describe how the feathers were obtained through hunting ostriches in the eastern desert of Iwnw (Heliopolis). On one side, Tutankhamun, accompanied by his hunting dog, races his chariot towards fleeing ostrich with his bow and arrow ready to fire. On the other side, he is shown returning at a slower pace with two attendants carrying dead ostriches.","i":165},{"id":"canopic-coffinette-1","no":"470","en":"Canopic Coffinette","cn":"卡诺匹斯小金棺·伊西斯守护","g":"tut","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"金、红玉髓、玻璃","dim":"高 12 cm · 长 39 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":3,"body":"这具黄金小棺原本置于卡诺匹斯圣柜内，用于保存图坦卡蒙经过处理的内脏。棺上人物戴涅墨斯头巾，双手持弯钩与连枷，表面嵌有红玉髓和彩色玻璃。\n正面的一列文字，是以伊西斯女神口吻写成的守护咒文。四具成套小棺各有相应的宗教联系，本件以这段铭文表明与伊西斯的关系。\n王名圈还保留了改刻痕迹，提示它最初可能为另一场王室葬礼准备。这一线索能够说明器物曾被调整使用，但不足以单独确定改用的具体原因。","src":"This elaborately detailed miniature gold coffin is one of a set of four coffinettes placed inside the canopic chest to contain the king’s mummified internal organs. It is made of solid gold decorated with red carnelian and tiny inlays of coloured glass. It shows a king in a royal nemes headcloth holding a crook and flail. The column of text down the front of the coffinette is a spell voiced by the goddess Isis. The royal cartouches show traces of alternation suggesting that the coffinette was originally intended for another royal burial.","i":166},{"id":"canopic-coffinette-2","no":"471","en":"Canopic Coffinette","cn":"卡诺匹斯小金棺·塞尔凯特守护","g":"tut","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"金、玻璃、红玉髓","dim":"高 12 cm · 长 39 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这具小金棺的正面刻着蝎子女神塞尔凯特所说的守护咒文，她在这里负责保护国王的肠。黄金表面嵌入红玉髓和彩色玻璃，人物上身被守护女神的羽翼环抱。\n图坦卡蒙的四具内脏小棺各用亚麻布包裹，直立安放在卡诺匹斯圣柜的四个圆槽内，分别保存肺、肝、胃和肠。\n荷鲁斯四子与四位女神共同参与守护。相似的外形之下，各具小棺仍通过铭文与神祇关系，承担明确的分工。","src":"Four miniature coffins elaborately crafted of solid gold with tiny inlays of red carnelian and coloured glass held Tutankhamun’s mummified viscera (lungs, liver, stomach and intestines). Each was wrapped in linen and placed upright inside one of four cylindrical hollows of a canopic chest. Each coffinette showed a king with his upper body embraced by the wings of the two protective goddesses of Upper and Lower Egypt. The coffinettes were associated with four guarding genii (Four Sons of Horus) who in turn were protected by four protective goddesses (Isis, Nephthys, Selket and Neith). A spell voiced by the scorpion goddess Selket, who protected the intestines, is carved down the front of this coffinette.","i":167},{"id":"duck-head-earrings","no":"485","en":"Duck Head Earrings","cn":"鸭首耳坠","g":"tut","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"金","dim":"高 11.9 cm · 宽 2.2 cm · 长 5.3 cm","prov":"上埃及","star":false,"n":2,"body":"这对耳坠的悬挂结构很特别：一根管子穿过耳垂，两端以透明石英圆片封住。正面刻有国王的小像与两条圣蛇。\n下垂的彩色鸟形组合了镶嵌的隼翼与蓝玻璃鸭头，双爪各抓着象征无尽的申环。鸟下方还悬着五条尾部串珠的圣蛇，形成复杂而富有层次的装饰。\n卡特在检查国王遗体时，记录了耳垂上的圆形穿孔。这为理解耳饰如何佩戴提供了线索，但仅凭耳孔，仍不能确定国王佩戴某一副耳坠的具体时间与场合。","src":"These elaborate earrings were attached by tubes that passed through the king’s lobes. Both outer ends are closed by round disks of transparent quartz. The front faces show tiny portraits of the king and are decorated with two uraeus snakes. Multi-coloured composite birds with inlaid falcon wings and blue glass duck heads hang from the central tubes. Each holds shen (eternity) signs in its outstretched feet. Five uraeus snakes with beaded tails hang down under the birds. According to the excavator Howard Carter, the king’s mummified remains showed ‘the lobes of the ears are perforated by a circular hole’.","i":168},{"id":"festival-earrings","no":"486","en":"Festival Earrings","cn":"塞德节耳环","g":"tut","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"金","dim":"高 13 cm · 宽 2.2 cm · 长 5.3 cm","prov":"上埃及","star":false,"n":1,"body":"耳环上的国王小像站在节庆符号上，两侧是圣蛇，整组装饰由一只隼悬吊。小小的首饰汇集了王者、神鸟与节庆的形象。\n每只耳环由三部分组成，佩戴时需要他人协助：先将带棱的空心管依次穿过坠饰一侧、耳洞与另一侧，再从背后插入细管固定。\n新王国时期，耳饰在男女和儿童中都很流行。图坦卡蒙耳垂上有穿孔，但他成年后是否继续佩戴耳环，学界仍有讨论。复杂的固定结构，则为了解王室耳饰的使用方式提供了实物依据。","src":"In these earrings tiny figures of the king stand on a heb festival sign between uraeus snakes, all suspended from a falcon. Each earring is made up of three parts and it would have been impossible for the king to put these on alone. They were fastened by passing a hollow ridged tube through one side of the earring pendant, the piercing, and then the other side of the earring pendant. This was then fixed by inserting a thinner tube from the back. Earrings became popular during the New Kingdom in Egypt and were worn by men, women and children. Some scholars debate whether Tutankhamun wore earrings beyond puberty.","i":169},{"id":"model-of-tutankhamun-on-a-funerary-bed","no":"3150","en":"Model of Tutankhamun on a Funerary Bed","cn":"葬床上的国王模型","g":"tut","p":"新王国时期","d":null,"m":"木","dim":"高 26 cm · 长 48 cm","prov":"上埃及","star":false,"n":1,"body":"木模型中的国王呈木乃伊形态，躺在狮首葬床上。肘旁分别是一只人首鸟与一只隼，它们各伸一翼，护在国王身体上方。\n人首鸟代表国王的“巴”，即灵魂的一种表现；隼则可能表示国王化身为荷鲁斯。葬床铭文说明，这件模型由帝王谷工程总管玛雅献给国王。\n出土时，模型包在亚麻布中，放于棺形木盒内，盒中另有五件沙布提俑工具。它以缩小的场景，将葬床、国王与守护形象组合在一起，也留下了奉献者的姓名。","src":"This wooden model was found wrapped in a linen cloth inside a sarcophagus-shaped box that also contained five shabti tools. Here, the king is shown as a mummy lying on a lion-headed funerary bed. Two small figures of a human-headed bird and a falcon sit at his elbows and each wraps a wing around the king’s body. The human-headed bird represents the king’s ba or spirit, while the falcon is probably the king transformed into the god Horus. According to inscriptions on the funerary bed, this model was gifted to the king by Maya who served as ‘Overseer of Works in the Valley of the Kings’.","i":170},{"id":"ritual-carrying-box","no":"4881","en":"Ritual Carrying Box","cn":"开口仪式抬箱","g":"tut","p":"新王国时期","d":null,"m":"乌木、木、金","dim":"高 66 cm · 长 95 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"箱身两侧的四根滑动抬杆，使这件木箱能够由四人、也可能八人肩扛。红色木板嵌在乌木框架内，构成箱体与箱盖。它出土于图坦卡蒙墓前室。\n箱前图像称国王为“奥西里斯王、两地之主、涅布赫佩鲁拉”，提示相关雕刻可能完成于国王去世之后。其他铭文则表明，箱子及其内容物可能用于“开口仪式”。\n这种葬仪旨在恢复死者呼吸、进食等能力，使其能够在来世继续生活。抬杆、箱体与铭文相互印证，说明它既是搬运和收纳器具，也参与了具体的仪式活动。","src":"This unusual carrying chest with four sliding poles was found in the Antechamber. It was designed to be carried on the shoulders of four or perhaps eight bearers. The box and lid are constructed from red wood panels inside ebony frames. A scene on the front describes Tutankhamun as ‘the Osiris King, Lord of the Two Lands, Nebkheperure’, suggesting that it was carved after his death. Other inscriptions suggest that the chest and its contents were used during the ‘Opening of the Mouth’ ceremony. This was the last and most important part of the funerary ritual when the deceased was made able to breathe and receive food and drink in the afterlife.","i":171},{"id":"canopic-coffinette-3","no":"16345","en":"Canopic Coffinette","cn":"卡诺匹斯小金棺·涅伊特守护","g":"tut","p":"新王国时期","d":"第 18 王朝","m":"金、玻璃、红玉髓","dim":"高 12 cm · 长 39 cm","prov":"上埃及 · 卢克索","star":false,"n":1,"body":"这具黄金小棺正面的铭文，以涅伊特女神的口吻为死者祈求保护。她守护荷鲁斯四子中的杜阿穆特夫，后者则负责保护国王的胃。\n小棺以红玉髓和彩色玻璃镶嵌，原本包裹亚麻布，置于卡诺匹斯圣柜的一个圆筒形凹槽内。四个槽分别安放四具小棺，保存木乃伊制作时取出的内脏。\n这套安排把容器、器官与守护神逐一对应。与其他小棺对照时，正面铭文是辨认本件宗教分工的重要依据。","src":"Tutankhamun’s canopic chest was hollowed into four cylindrical hollows, each concealed a miniature coffin wrapped in linen. The coffinettes held the internal organs that were removed during the mummification process. Elaborately fashioned of gold inlaid with carnelian and coloured glass, these miniature coffins are remarkable examples of goldsmith art. The inscription down the front of this coffinette are words spoken by the goddess Neith. It was her duty to protect Duamutef who in turn protected the mummified stomach of the king.","i":172}]};
